\par\par \uc2 Media\par \b \uc2 Bob Woodward says he is \u8216\'20\'18crushed\u8217\'20\'19 by \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  layoffs\b0\par\par\uc2 Lucy Campbell \par \uc2 568 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 February 2026\par 22:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Watergate reporter says colleagues and readers \u8216\'20\'18deserve more\u8217\'20\'19 after newspaper lays off hundreds of workers\par \par \uc2 The veteran {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  journalist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/bob-woodward"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bob Woodward}}}\uc2  has said he is \u8220\'20\'1Ccrushed\u8221\'20\'1D by the mass layoffs of hundreds of colleagues at the paper and said the impact would be felt by readers \u8211\'20\'13 noting both \u8220\'20\'1Cdeserve more\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am crushed that so many of my beloved colleagues have lost their jobs and our readers have been given less news and sound analysis,\u8221\'20\'1D Woodward said in his first public remarks on the cuts, which were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/realBobWoodward/status/2019856742130282594"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared}}}\uc2  on X. \u8220\'20\'1CThey deserve more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Woodward said the Post had produced \u8220\'20\'1Cmany superb and excellent groundbreaking stories\u8221\'20\'1D under executive editor Matt Murray. \u8220\'20\'1CThere will be more,\u8221\'20\'1D Woodward said. \u8220\'20\'1CI will do everything in my power to help make sure the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  thrives and survives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Woodward exposed the Watergate scandal with fellow reporter Carl Bernstein, ending \uc2 Richard Nixon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency in 1974 and winning the Post the Pulitzer prize. Their book about the scandal, All the President\u8217\'20\'19s Men, became a bestseller and was later turned into an Oscar-winning film of the same name starring Robert Redford and Dustin Hoffman.\par \par \uc2 Woodward worked for the Post for decades, reporting on every presidency since. He now holds an honorific associate editor title.\par \par \uc2 His statement comes after the storied newspaper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/feb/04/washington-post-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laid off about a third of its staff}}}\uc2  on Wednesday, or more than 300 journalists. The move has resulted in the shuttering of the paper\u8217\'20\'19s sports department and the shredding of teams covering local news, style and the world \u8211\'20\'13 not to mention its audio and video departments, which had already been battered by previous cuts. Commercial teams were also cut.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe aspirations of this news organization are diminished,\u8221\'20\'1D former editor Marty Baron {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/feb/05/mass-layoffs-washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI think that\u8217\'20\'19ll translate into fewer subscribers. And I hope it\u8217\'20\'19s not a death spiral, but I worry that it might be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Post lost hundreds of thousands of subscribers in the fall of 2024 after owner Jeff Bezos {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/oct/25/washington-post-will-not-endorse-presidential-candidate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abruptly shelved its planned endorsement of Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  for president days before the election won by Donald Trump. He also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2025/feb/26/jeff-bezos-washington-post-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reoriented the paper\u8217\'20\'19s opinion pages}}}\uc2  to a more narrow focus on supporting \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonal liberties and free markets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 At the time, Woodward and Bernstein decried Bezos\u8217\'20\'19s decision to spike the planned Harris endorsement and end the paper\u8217\'20\'19s history of endorsing presidential candidates as \u8220\'20\'1Csurprising and disappointing, especially this late in the electoral process\u8221\'20\'1D. They said in a joint statement that the move \u8220\'20\'1Cignores the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s own overwhelming reportorial evidence on the threat Donald Trump poses to democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Post, Woodward {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/news/annals-of-communications/how-jeff-bezos-brought-down-the-washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the New Yorker on Wednesday,}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Clives and is doing an extraordinary reporting job on the political crisis that is Donald Trump\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Upon Bezos\u8217\'20\'19s 2013 acquisition of the paper, Woodward asked him why he had bought the Post. \u8220\'20\'1CI finally concluded that I could provide runway \u8211\'20\'13 financial runway \u8211\'20\'13 because I don\u8217\'20\'19t think you can keep shrinking the business,\u8221\'20\'1D Bezos said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/news/annals-of-communications/how-jeff-bezos-brought-down-the-washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the New Yorker}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CYou can be profitable and shrinking. And that\u8217\'20\'19s a survival strategy, but it ultimately leads to irrelevance, at best. And, at worst, it leads to extinction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A day after announcing the decimation of the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , \uc2 Amazon\uc2  announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/feb/05/amazon-ai-robotics-bezos-washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans to spend $200bn}}}\uc2  on artificial intelligence and robotics in the coming year.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260206em26006si\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
