\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump administration issues rule that makes it easier to fire federal workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 591 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 February 2026\par 19:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 New rule would strip job safeguards for 50,000 federal employees and change how whistleblowers are protected\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  is seeking to finalize its overhaul of the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s civil service system through a{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.federalregister.gov/public-inspection/2026-02375/improving-performance-accountability-and-responsiveness-in-the-civil-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  rule issued }}}\uc2 this week by the office of personnel management (OPM) to strip job protections from 50,000 civil service employees.\par \par \uc2 Under the rule, the president would have the authority to fire and hire an estimated 50,000 career federal employees.\par \par \uc2 The OPM said it was reclassifying certain career civil service roles so agencies can \u8220\'20\'1Cquickly remove employees from critical positions who engage in misconduct, perform poorly, or obstruct the democratic process by intentionally subverting Presidential directives\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/politics/2026/02/05/trump-tightens-control-over-50000-federal-workers/88526572007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  rule }}}\uc2 also would change how whistleblower protections, meant to protect whistleblowers from retaliation, are enforced. Instead of the independent office of special counsel handling most whistleblower disclosures from federal workers, federal agencies would be in charge of determining job protections for whistleblowers in their owndepartment.\par \par \uc2 On Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first day in office on 20 January 2025, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/20/trump-executive-order-schedule-f#:~:text=Schedule%20F%20reclassifies%20jobs%20as%20political%20appointments%2C,a%20negative%20effect%20on%20the%20federal%20government."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued}}}\uc2  an executive order to reclassify thousands of federal employees as political appointees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf these government workers refuse to advance the policy interests of the President, or are engaging in corrupt behavior, they should no longer have a job,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/18/trump-federal-workers-schedule-f#:~:text=%E2%80%9CThis%20is%20common%20sense%2C%20and,out%2C%20with%20which%20Trump%20disagrees."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote }}}\uc2 on his Truth Social platform in April 2025 after the OPM proposed the rule to reclassify the federal civil service employees as political appointees. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is common sense, and will allow the federal government to finally be \u8216\'20\'18run like a business.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 During Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  first term, he sought to enact these changes in October 2020 under a rule known as{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/nov/18/trump-federal-worker-civil-service-protections#:~:text=Donald%20Trump%20is%20expected%20to,powers%20to%20reshape%20the%20bureaucracy."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Schedule F,}}}\uc2  but the change was rescinded when Biden took office before it could be implemented.\par \par \uc2 The latest rule will be reviewed by a federal judge, and critics, notably the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees (AFGE)\uc2  union and Democracy Forward non-profit, have already expressed intent to challenge the rule in court.\par \par \uc2 Traditionally, only political appointees \u8211\'20\'13 roughly 4,000 positions \u8211\'20\'13 can be dismissed \u8220\'20\'1Cat will\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Under the new rule, many non-partisan roles would be shifted into a category called \u8220\'20\'1CSchedule Policy/Career\u8221\'20\'1D, in effect treating them as political appointees. That reclassification could allow the administration to remove employees it views as disloyal. The rule \u8211\'20\'13 set to be published in the Federal Register on Friday \u8211\'20\'13 also states that \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonal or political loyalty tests as a condition of employment\u8221\'20\'1D are prohibited.\par \par \uc2 Critics argue the change would open the door to politically motivated purges. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have successfully fought this kind of power grab before, and we will fight this again. We will return to court to stop this unlawful rule and will use every legal tool available to hold this administration accountable to the people,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Skye Perryman\uc2 , CEO of Democracy Forward.\par \par \uc2 The largest union representing federal workers called the rule \u8220\'20\'1Ca direct assault on a professional, nonpartisan, merit-based civil service\u8221\'20\'1D. In a statement, the \uc2 AFGE\uc2  president, \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , said the OPM was \u8220\'20\'1Crebranding career public servants as \u8216\'20\'18policy\u8217\'20\'19 employees, silencing whistleblowers, and replacing competent professionals with political flunkies without any neutral, independent protections against politicization and arbitrary abuse of power\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Stripping civil service protections has also been a central plank of \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Project 2025 blueprint.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Thursday, anticipating the rule\u8217\'20\'19s release, the OPM director, Scott Kupor, said the reclassification would bring \u8220\'20\'1Cmuch-needed accountability to career policy-influencing positions in the Federal government\u8221\'20\'1D.Shrai Popat contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260205em250053g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
