\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US agency investigates \uc2 Nike\uc2  for alleged discrimination against white workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Sara Braun \par \uc2 616 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 February 2026\par 21:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 EEOC\uc2  demands firm turn over \u8216\'20\'18DEI-related objectives\u8217\'20\'19 amid Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown on diversity initiatives\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Equal Employment Opportunity Commission\uc2  (\uc2 EEOC\uc2 ) has launched an investigation into \uc2 Nike\uc2  over allegations that the sports giant discriminated against white employees and job applicants.\par \par \uc2 The federal agency is demanding that \uc2 Nike\uc2  turn over information related to the allegations, including the company\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CDiversity, Equity, and Inclusion-related 2025 Targets and other DEI-related objectives\u8221\'20\'1D, it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eeoc.gov/newsroom/eeoc-files-subpoena-enforcement-action-against-nike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Nike\uc2 , which described the escalation as \u8220\'20\'1Csurprising and unusual\u8221\'20\'1D, insisted that it adheres to \u8220\'20\'1Call applicable laws\u8221\'20\'1D on discrimination.It comes amid a broader crackdown by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration on diversity initiatives, which he has repeatedly decried as \u8220\'20\'1Cradical\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen there are compelling indications, including corporate admissions in extensive public materials, that an employer\u8217\'20\'19s Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion-related programs may violate federal prohibitions against race discrimination or other forms of unlawful discrimination, the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  will take all necessary steps \u8211\'20\'13 including subpoena enforcement actions \u8211\'20\'13 to ensure the opportunity to fully and comprehensively investigate,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 EEOC\uc2  chair, Andrea Lucas.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EEOC\uc2  is responsible for enforcing laws that make it illegal to discriminate against a job applicant or an employee because of the person\u8217\'20\'19s race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability or genetic information. The federal agency has the authority to investigate charges against employers who are covered by the law.\par \par \uc2 Lucas, a Republican, was appointed as acting head of the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  by the US president in 2025. Her predecessor during the Biden administration, Charlotte Burrows, was fired shortly after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to office last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTitle VII\u8217\'20\'19s prohibition of race-based employment discrimination is colorblind and requires the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  to protect employees of all races from unlawful employment practices,\u8221\'20\'1D Lucas said. \u8220\'20\'1CThanks to President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to enforcing our nation\u8217\'20\'19s civil rights laws, the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  has renewed its focus on evenhanded enforcement of Title VII.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On his first day in office, Trump signed an order directing federal agencies to terminate all \u8220\'20\'1Cequity-related\u8221\'20\'1D grants or contracts. He also signed a follow-up order requiring federal contractors to certify that they don\u8217\'20\'19t promote DEI. The administration has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/18/trump-administration-schools-dei-programs-deadline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targeted universities}}}\uc2 , urging them to eliminate diversity initiatives or risk losing federal funding.\par \par \uc2 The information that the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  is seeking dates back to 2018, and includes criteria used to select employees for layoffs, information related to the company\u8217\'20\'19s tracking, use of worker race and ethnicity data, and information about \u8220\'20\'1C16 programs which allegedly provided race-restricted mentoring, leadership, or career development opportunities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lucas has targeted programs related to diversity and gender since being appointed by Trump in 2025, in alignment with the administration\u8217\'20\'19s agenda. In a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/01/27/us/politics/eocc-dei-employment-discrimination.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  with the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , she said that her goal was to undo the consequences of an \u8220\'20\'1Caggressive focus by D.E.I. activists\u8221\'20\'1D under the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, a \uc2 Nike\uc2  spokesperson said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have had extensive, good-faith participation in an \uc2 EEOC\uc2  inquiry into our personnel practices, programs, and decisions and have had ongoing efforts to provide information and engage constructively with the agency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have shared thousands of pages of information and detailed written responses to the \uc2 EEOC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s inquiry and are in the process of providing additional information.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nike\uc2  is a \u8220\'20\'1Cproud American company\u8221\'20\'1D, the spokesperson added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are committed to fair and lawful employment practices and follow all applicable laws, including those that prohibit discrimination. We believe our programs and practices are consistent with those obligations and take these matters seriously. We will continue our attempt to cooperate with the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  and will respond to the petition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260204em2400691\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
