\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Striking Starbucks workers urge customers to delete coffee chain\u8217\'20\'19s app\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 627 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 February 2026\par 11:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Unionized baristas continue to fight for a fair contract and ask public for solidarity as strike stretches into third month\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/02/starbucks-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Striking Starbucks baristas}}}\uc2  are calling on customers of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest coffee chain to delete its popular mobile app in solidarity with their demands for a first union contract.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks Workers United, which has been coordinating a strike for almost three months, is vowing to press ahead.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe baristas are still fighting for a fair contract, and this fight is active and ongoing,\u8221\'20\'1D said KC Ihekwaba, a barista at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in Lafayette, Colorado, on a solidarity union call earlier this week. \u8220\'20\'1COur fire for change is still burning. Our spirits still strong.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re asking for has not changed. We\u8217\'20\'19re demanding livable wages, stable and predictable hours, and an end to union busting. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  still has not delivered on any of that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since 13 November last year, Starbucks Workers United began an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/nov/19/starbucks-workers-strike-us-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfair labor practice strike}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since December 2021, workers won union elections at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unionelections.org/data/starbucks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 600 Starbucks stores}}}\uc2 . With several stores hit by closures, Starbucks Workers United{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/02/starbucks-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  now represents }}}\uc2 about 11,000 baristas at 576 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores in the US. A further 15 storesfiled for a union election last month.\par \par \uc2 At the end of December, the union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seattletimes.com/business/starbucks/majority-of-starbucks-striking-baristas-are-returning-to-work/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scaled}}}\uc2  back the scope of the strike, with most stores giving a return to work notice to \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , with the aim to keep several hundred to 1,000 workers on strike in a rotational basis given the financial burdens of long strikes for low-income employees, and to put energy into increasing the number of unionized \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores.\par \par \uc2 About 1,000 baristas across nearly 50 stores are on strike. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have definitely made it known that we deserve a fair contract and union busting has got to stop now,\u8221\'20\'1D said Christi Gomoljak, a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  barista, during a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://us06web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_v9hE4OtvTHab8iwixPo7rA#/registration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 solidarity call}}}\uc2  announcing the \u8220\'20\'1CDelete the App\u8221\'20\'1D campaign.\par \par \uc2 Gomoljak and her co-workers recently organized a union at the Downtown Disney Starbucks in Anaheim, California, and walked out on strike in November 2025.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are calling on \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  customers everywhere to delete the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  mobile app off your phone,\u8221\'20\'1D Gomoljak added. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen baristas get a fair contract, you can reload the app on your phone and then finally, use any gift cards that you might have gotten from the holidays. But trust me, coffee with a union contract tastes so much better, and it is worth the wait.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Liz Shuler\uc2 , president of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the largest federation of labor unions in the US, said on the call: \u8220\'20\'1CSupporting our baristas as they take on one of the most powerful companies in the world \u8230\'20\'26 is an incredible way to make an impact. This fight is about something way bigger than just coffee. It\u8217\'20\'19s about whether we as working people get to live with dignity in this world that we make possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has downplayed the strike and its impact, claiming that fewer than 1% of the chain\u8217\'20\'19s stores were ever affected, and more than half either continued operating, or reopened, shortly after the strike. They did not comment on the app deletion campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe union has called for an unconditional return to work at nearly all of the coffeehouses on its strike list,\u8221\'20\'1D said a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  spokesperson, Jaci Anderson. \u8220\'20\'1CWe see this as a positive step and hope it signals a willingness to return to the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CWith more than 30 tentative agreements already in place, we\u8217\'20\'19re confident we can move quickly toward a fair contract \u8211\'20\'13 one that reflects that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  offers the best job in retail, with pay and benefits averaging over $30 an hour for hourly partners.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260204em24002pd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
