\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Minnesota workers pressure employers to take action against ICE operations\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,068 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 January 2026\par 13:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Target, Delta and \uc2 Hilton\uc2  targeted with actions leading up to economic blackout of no work, shopping or school\par \par \uc2 Some of the US\u8217\'20\'19s biggest companies are coming under increasing pressure to speak out about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Immigration and Customs Enforcement ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ice-us-immigration-and-customs-enforcement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ICE}}}\uc2 )\u8217\'20\'19s operations in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/minnesota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Workers throughout Minnesota have been pressuring their employers to act following the death of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/08/minnesota-ice-shooting-nicole-macklin-good"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Renee Good}}}\uc2 , an unarmed woman killed by a federal immigration officer in Minneapolis earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 The killing on Saturday of Alex Jeffrey Pretti, a 37-year-old Veterans Affairs Hospital ICU Nurse and member of the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees (AFGE)\uc2 , intensified those {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mnaflcio.org/news/statement-ices-killing-afge-member-alex-jeffrey-pretti"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calls }}}\uc2 from labor unions against ICE.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CICE continues to make everyone less safe, and Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s Labor Movement repeats and amplifies our call for them to leave our state immediately,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bernie Burnham, Minnesota \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  President, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mnaflcio.org/news/statement-ices-killing-afge-member-alex-jeffrey-pretti"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CMinnesota\u8217\'20\'19s Labor Movement will continue to actively support and stand in solidarity with every worker who has been unlawfully detained. We stand shoulder to shoulder with our fellow Minnesotans in the face of a hostile federal government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Friday, labor unions, community leaders, and faith leaders organized a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iceoutnowmn.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Day of Truth & Freedom}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/23/minnesota-economic-blackout-ice-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling for}}}\uc2  an economic blackout of no work, no shopping and no school.\par \par \uc2 Organizers of the Day of Truth & Freedom have been targeting large corporations in demanding they take stands against ICE, including ceasing economic activity with the agency, and banning the agency from entering work sites.\par \par \uc2 Target, \uc2 Home Depot\uc2 , Enterprise, \uc2 Delta Airlines\uc2  and \uc2 Hilton\uc2  were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CfnANsEjROzW1UEVRes4yjsrVRvg64SHNAh9Gvpaki0/edit?tab=t.0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targeted}}}\uc2  with actions leading up to the 23 January economic blackout. Hundreds of Target workers signed onto a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.startribune.com/ice-raids-minnesota/601546426"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  addressed to the company\u8217\'20\'19s CEO and other leaders criticizing the company\u8217\'20\'19s silence on the ICE operations in Minnesota. None of the companies responded to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s so sad to see Target so silent,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sheletta Brundidge, an activist and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kare11.com/article/news/local/ice-in-minnesota/one-week-after-renee-goods-death-community-members-gather-in-prayer/89-63bb3e60-9a30-4593-8e5b-ac15aa576da7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organizer}}}\uc2  in Minneapolis who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.startribune.com/black-women-are-still-being-blacked-out-of-history/601367843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 started}}}\uc2  a Target boycott with activist Nekima Levy Armstrong against the company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/17/rev-al-sharpton-target-ceo-dei-rollback"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rescinding}}}\uc2  their diversity, equity and inclusion (DEI) initiatives. Levy Armstrong was recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/22/two-arrests-minnesota-church-protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 detained}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  for an anti-ICE protest at a Minnesota church. Brundidge\u8217\'20\'19s marketing company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tcbmag.com/corporate-sponsors-line-up-for-podcaster-sheletta-brundidge/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously worked}}}\uc2  with Target.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat Target CEO should be out in the street talking to people. He should be part of the protesting. He should make sure that the neighbors to his company\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters are taken care of. Has he gone out to the site where Renee Good was killed and dropped off water or hand warmers? Have they done anything for her children? Has he stepped out of that ivory tower to look around and see what is going on?\u8221\'20\'1D added Brundidge.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere was a protest that marched right in front of his headquarters on Friday. They didn\u8217\'20\'19t even mention it, they are silent, and silence says something. Silence doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what to say. Silence says I don\u8217\'20\'19t give a damn. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care about the people that shop here. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care about the people who work here. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care about the people in this community. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care. Keep spending your money.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Target\u8217\'20\'19s executives reportedly met with clergy in Minneapolis last week who protested in the company\u8217\'20\'19s lobby. The Wall Street Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/minneapolis-minnesota-ice-ceo-response-7d225f2e?mod=hp_lead_pos9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  the company began distributing internally updated guidelines for how staff should respond to \u8220\'20\'1Cunannounced immigration-related contacts\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hilton\uc2  has faced scrutiny after a Hampton Inn in its network of hotels {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/05/ice-hilton-minneapolis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cancelled}}}\uc2  the reservation of ICE agents and \uc2 Hilton\uc2  removed it from its network earlier this month. But this past week, Hilton {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/minneapolis-minnesota-ice-ceo-response-7d225f2e?mod=hp_lead_pos9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed}}}\uc2  a decision to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox9.com/news/st-paul-hotel-rooms-canceled-ice-agents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 close}}}\uc2  a DoubleTree hotel and an Intercontinental hotel where ICE agents were staying in the Twin Cities region following reported bomb threats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA safety and security issue is a different issue\u8212\'20\'14it\u8217\'20\'19s closed to all,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Hilton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s CEO, \uc2 Chris Nassetta\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://northstarpolicy.org/metro-surge-cost/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  by North Star Policy Action estimates the immigration enforcement operation is costing taxpayers at least $18m per week. Immigrant workers and business owners generate $41bn annually in economic output for Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want ICE out of Minnesota. In construction, they are causing harm and chaos. People can\u8217\'20\'19t work,\u8221\'20\'1D said a construction worker in Minnesota, a member of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ctul.net/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Centro de Trabajadores Unidos en La Lucha}}}\uc2  (CTUL), who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation to their immigration status.\par \par \uc2 The worker and several of his co-workers and allies delivered a petition to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://investor.drhorton.com/news-and-events/press-releases/2026/01-20-2026-113048753"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest}}}\uc2  US house developer by volume, \uc2 DR Horton\uc2 , at their regional office in Lakeville, Minnesota, on 21 January.\par \par \uc2 They are demanding the developer prevent ICE from entering job sites without a valid warrant and to demand an end to the ICE violence and raids. The worker said no one came to speak with the group, but the police were called to ask the group to leave, which they did peacefully.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe police said we need to leave because it is private property, and a few community members pointed out that this is precisely what we are asking of DR Horton \u8211\'20\'13 to not allow ICE on their private job sites without a signed and valid judicial warrant,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jac Kovarik, the communications coordinator for CTUL, in a statement on the action.\par \par \uc2 DR Horton did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMe and my coworkers haven\u8217\'20\'19t been working for a month now,\u8221\'20\'1D added the worker. \u8220\'20\'1CICE agents are going to construction sites, they\u8217\'20\'19re circling around, apprehending people, assaulting people without a warrant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He noted his church has been providing food and helping to cover rent for him and his co-workers as ICE\u8217\'20\'19s operations have halted construction projects for the contractor where he works.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the US Department of Homeland Security called the actions of labor unions and workers \u8220\'20\'1Cbeyond insane. Why would these labor bosses not want these public safety threats out of their communities?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They added, \u8220\'20\'1Cthese are the criminals these labor bosses are trying to protect,\u8221\'20\'1D citing 23 unnamed photos of claimed undocumented immigrants arrested in Minnesota with criminal records.\par \par \uc2 Under the Trump administration, thousands of people {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2025/aug/29/trump-immigration-ice-cbp-data"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targeted}}}\uc2  by ICE have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/24/trump-immigrants-ice-arrests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/sep/26/immigrants-criminal-record-ice-detention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/22/ice-detentions-record-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record}}}\uc2 , and numerous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/23/us-citizens-ice-passports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US citizens}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/13/ice-immigration-target-minnesota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/nov/23/ice-oregon-student-citizen-detained-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/09/maryland-woman-us-citizen-released-ice-custody"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/01/us-citizen-detained-twice-immigration-agents-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 detained}}}\uc2 . In 2025, Donald Trump also issued more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/04/trump-pardons-arrests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1,600}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/pardon/clemency-grants-president-donald-j-trump-2025-present"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pardons}}}\uc2  of individuals convicted of crimes, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/20/trump-executive-orders-jan-6-pardons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Capitol insurrectionists}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/23/trumps-politics-gilded-age"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wealthy campaign donors}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260125em1p001rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
