\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Minnesotans strike in protest against ICE surge: \u8216\'20\'18No work, no school, no shopping\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato and Rachel Leingang in Minneapolis \par \uc2 1,045 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2026\par 02:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Organizers demand ICE leave state and agency be investigated for constitutional violations\par \par \uc2 Tens of thousands of Minnesotans marched in Minneapolis and otherwise participated in an economic blackout on Friday to protest against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ice-us-immigration-and-customs-enforcement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE)}}}\uc2  surge in the state.\par \par \uc2 About 100 clergy members were arrested by police during the action, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/watch/live/?ref=watch_permalink&v=907816511669873"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video footage}}}\uc2  showed.\par \par \uc2 Beside faith leaders, the \u8220\'20\'1Cno work, no school, no shopping\u8221\'20\'1D day of protest was kicked off by community leaders and labor unions \u8211\'20\'13 and included actions around the state, plus business closures in solidarity.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1CDay of Truth & Freedom\u8221\'20\'1D protest came in the wake of the killing of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/08/minnesota-ice-shooting-nicole-macklin-good"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Renee Good}}}\uc2 , the unarmed woman shot by a federal immigration officer in Minneapolis earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 The protesters\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iceoutnowmn.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demands}}}\uc2  include that ICE leave {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/minnesota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota}}}\uc2 , that the ICE officer who killed Good be legally held accountable, an end to additional federal funding for ICE, and for the agency to be investigated for human rights and constitutional violations.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jan/22/minnesota-economic-blackout-ice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We have to stand together\u8217\'20\'19: Minnesota economic blackout organizers push to take demonstrations nationwide}}}\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of local businesses in Minnesota {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bringmethenews.com/minnesota-lifestyle/growing-number-of-minnesota-businesses-announce-plans-to-close-for-jan-23-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced }}}\uc2 closures in solidarity. Thousands of people took the day off from their jobs to join the action, while others participated by not shopping on Friday. The Minneapolis city council {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DT1LCqCDgnr/?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed}}}\uc2  the day of action and the general strike.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s cultural institutions \u8211\'20\'13 including the \uc2 Walker Art Center\uc2 , the Minneapolis Institute of Art, the Science Museum of Minnesota and the Minnesota Children\u8217\'20\'19s Museum \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/01/22/minneapolis-museums-galleries-general-strike-ice-trump-immigration-raids"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 closed}}}\uc2  on Friday as well.\par \par \uc2 During a protest at the Minneapolis-St Paul airport on Friday morning, hundreds of clergy members called for an end to the ICE surge and urged airline companies to join them in opposing ICE in the state. Video of the action showed hundreds of people walking outside the airport in sub-zero temperatures, singing songs and praying together. Deportation flights go in and out of the airport daily.\par \par \uc2 On Friday afternoon, thousands clad in winter gear and carrying signs filled the streets of downtown Minneapolis to march in subzero temperatures, ending in a rally inside the Target Center, an arena downtown.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to be having dangerously cold weather on Friday \u8211\'20\'13 -10F with wind chills. Like the high is going to be -10F with wind chills of up to -20F,\u8221\'20\'1D Chelsie Glaubitz Gabiou, president of the Minnesota Regional Labor Federation, \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , had told the Guardian earlier.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are a northern state, and we are built for the cold, and we are going to show up, but folks are going to need to pay attention to not just the march, but what people are doing, the individual stories of solidarity that people are going to be doing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s federation of more than 1,000 affiliated local unions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mnaflcio.org/news/minnesotas-labor-movement-endorses-123-day-truth-freedom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed}}}\uc2  the day of action, along with dozens of local labor unions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think what generated the idea for this action came out of the need to figure out what we can meaningfully do to stop it,\u8221\'20\'1D Kieran Knutson, the president of \uc2 Communications Workers of America (CWA)\uc2  Local 7250 in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/minneapolis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minneapolis}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/20/ice-immigrarion-minnesota-economic-protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian last week}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe government in the state of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/minnesota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota}}}\uc2  has not offered any path towards stopping these attacks, this violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A childcare worker in Minneapolis, who requested anonymity for fear of retaliation toward the immigrant families they serve, said they were shutting down for the day after consulting and receiving immense support from the families of the children they care for.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe had time to ask the families that we serve if they would be on board with shutting down and we got a hugely positive response,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe serve families that are on childcare assistance, families that pay out of pocket. So they were all in agreement, even ones that have been trying to go to work, even during this time where they were fearful of being out of their houses. So it was really the families. They all stood up for it, too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/22/ice-detentions-record-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Number of people in ICE detention hits record high, data shows}}}\par \par \uc2 At the \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2  campuses in Minneapolis, St Paul, and Duluth, labor unions representing student workers and staff have called for the university system to shut down on Friday to allow students and workers to participate in the day of action.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2  graduate labor union said ICE\u8217\'20\'19s operations have had an impact on student workers since the beginning of the Trump administration. In early 2025, at least three international students at the \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2  were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sahanjournal.com/immigration/university-minnesota-international-student-dogukan-gunaydin-automatic-stay/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested and detained }}}\uc2 by ICE, despite an immigration judge ordering their release.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really concerning to us that the university is remaining neutral in a time when immigrant communities and international students are literally under attack,\u8221\'20\'1D said Abaki Beck, president of the \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2  graduate labor union. \u8220\'20\'1COne of the other things we\u8217\'20\'19re pushing for on campus specifically is increased support for immigrant workers and international students.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the University of Minnesota cited a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://provost.umn.edu/about-evpp/communications/guidance-university-community-regarding-jan-23-civic-action"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guidance memo}}}\uc2  from university leadership in response to the day of action. They said in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1CThe University of Minnesota fully supports the rights of faculty, staff, and students to engage in lawful civic expression. We also must ensure continuity of operations and meet our responsibilities to students and the university community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Department of Homeland Security (DHS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/01/19/ice-continues-remove-worst-worst-minneapolis-streets-dhs-law-enforcement-marks-3000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  to have made 3,000 arrests in Minnesota over the past six weeks.\par \par \uc2 The US army {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/army-deployment-minnesota-immigration-insurrection-act-31a28c23045bfdb31b27f68507a68ca8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put 1,500 soldiers }}}\uc2 on standby for possible deployment to Minnesota, as 3,000 immigration officers have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/01/12/us/politics/border-patrol-minnesota-surge.html#:~:text=The%20Customs%20and%20Border%20Protection,%E2%80%9Clargest%20operation%20to%20date.%E2%80%9D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dispatched }}}\uc2 to the state by the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is beyond insane. Why would these labor bosses not want these public safety threats out of their communities?\u8221\'20\'1D a DHS spokesperson said in an email in response to the economic blackout.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are the criminals these labor bosses are trying to protect,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson added, citing 23 uncaptioned photos of claimed undocumented immigrants with criminal records who have been arrested by ICE.\par \par \uc2 Nationwide, immigrants with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/nov/21/deportations-us-government-shutdown-ice-data"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no criminal record}}}\uc2  continue to make up the largest group in US immigration detention, which is at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/22/ice-detentions-record-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record levels}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260123em1n002p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
