\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 New York bakery staff push for union, claiming they were forced to bake for Israeli fundraisers\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 678 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 January 2026\par 12:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Breads Bakery workers demand better pay and conditions and criticize chain for supporting \u8216\'20\'18the genocide in Palestine\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Workers at popular {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  City bakery chain Breads Bakery announced a move to unionize, claiming it has \u8220\'20\'1Cunderpaid, undervalued, disrespected, discriminated against, intimidated and hurt\u8221\'20\'1D staff, as well as supported \u8220\'20\'1Cthe genocide happening in Palestine\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The company, which has ties to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2 , expressed concern that \u8220\'20\'1Cdivisive political issues\u8221\'20\'1D had been introduced into its stores. \u8220\'20\'1CWe make babka; we don\u8217\'20\'19t engage in politics,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 But staff involved in the unionization drive claimed that employees were forced by the chain to create products for fundraisers for Israeli organizations, and unable to decline.\par \par \uc2 The union, Breaking Breads, claims that more than 30% of the chain\u8217\'20\'19s 275 workers across New York City had signed union authorization cards, seeking to unionize with \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  Local 2179 and pushing for better pay, improvements to working conditions such as the replacement of broken equipment, and respect on the job.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe owners are the ones who are making it political,\u8221\'20\'1D one worker, who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation, said. \u8220\'20\'1CAll of us in the union, we have lots of many different political beliefs, things we stand for. We\u8217\'20\'19re not telling anyone how they should behave, what they should believe in, where they should donate their money, absolutely not.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut imagine you\u8217\'20\'19re a baker who works at this company, and you\u8217\'20\'19re witnessing videos that are coming out of Gaza that are really difficult to bear, and then your boss tells you that you\u8217\'20\'19re going to be making a new specialty bread item that\u8217\'20\'19s sold special and discounted as a fundraiser for a country that\u8217\'20\'19s doing a genocide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re just asking that workers have the decision about whether or not they can make those.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Breads Bakery uses profits to \u8220\'20\'1Cmaterially support the Israeli occupation\u8221\'20\'1D of Gaza, the union claimed. The bakery chain has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.breadsbakery.com/store-locator/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six locations }}}\uc2 in Manhattan, and was co-founded by Danish\u8211\'20\'13Israeli baker Uri Scheft.\par \par \uc2 The bakery has hired union avoidance consultants, according to the worker, who claimed they had been meeting one-on-one with staff in office meetings, in a effort to deter support for the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy location makes around $15,000 to $20,000 a day on average. We\u8217\'20\'19re a bread bakery. We sell a lot of bread. We have several shelves of bread,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd for almost around a year now, we have not been able to use equipment that we really need to function.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur three demands are for equitable pay, respect, and safety for workers. I joined this unionization effort, because after long enough at Breads, I started noticing these sort of patterns. We have a very high turnover rate. Most people are only there, on average, maybe around three or four months, and I really think a lot of that can be attributed to the disrespect that is shown to workers by management.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union is calling for pay increases across the board; holiday and busy season pay, including Jewish holidays; overtime pay; automatic raises over a set period of time; premium pay for late-shift and overnight work; replacement of broken equipment; proper uniforms for workers doing outdoor work; guaranteed hours every week; a free meal each shift; and at least three days\u8217\'20\'19 notice of each shift schedule.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Breads Bakery did not comment on the hiring of union avoidance consultants, or the criticism of the bakery supporting Israeli fundraisers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBreads Bakery is built on love and genuine care for our team,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe celebrate peace and embrace people of all cultures and beliefs. We\u8217\'20\'19ve always been a workplace where people of all backgrounds and viewpoints can come together around a common purpose, sharing in the joy and love of a bakery, and we find it troubling that divisive political issues are being introduced into our workplace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260115em1f0030g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
