\par\par \uc2 Environment\par \b \uc2 Ex-\uc2 FDA\uc2  workers warn Trump cuts will increase risk of food safety lapses in US\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,123 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 January 2026\par 16:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Current and former workers caution administration\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18politicization of science\u8217\'20\'19 will negatively affect Americans\par \par \uc2 Sweeping cuts and the \u8220\'20\'1Cpoliticization of science\u8221\'20\'1D inside the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  have increased the risk of safety lapses across the US, former agency workers warned.\par \par \uc2 Less than a year after Donald Trump returned to power, and his administration oversaw the firing and resignation of thousands of \uc2 FDA\uc2  employees, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/11/12/health/listeria-food-safety-wellness"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 listeria outbreak}}}\uc2  that killed six people and sickened 27 across 18 states due to contamination of prepared pasta meals underlined the danger posed by safety failings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose kinds of things are going to keep coming,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Harbourt, a former veterinary safety manager at the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , who was fired last year. The agency\u8217\'20\'19s work \u8220\'20\'1Chas been compromised for at a minimum, the short term, hopefully not the long term\u8221\'20\'1D, he claimed. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it\u8217\'20\'19s those aspects of American people\u8217\'20\'19s lives that we almost take for granted that are going to be affected in a very negative way in the coming years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.agencyiq.com/blog/as-government-reform-efforts-converge-significant-fda-staff-cuts-are-likely/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 About 19,700 employees}}}\uc2  worked at the agency before Trump officials introduced waves of firings, voluntary retirement and resignation programs. Thousands subsequently left, although some workers were later rehired.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am concerned that by letting go so many people, by offering early retirement, it\u8217\'20\'19s like that kids\u8217\'20\'19 game Jenga where you pile up all these wooden pieces,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sandra Eskin, CEO of Stop Foodborne Illness, a non-profit, and former deputy under secretary for food safety at the \uc2 US Department of Agriculture\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAnd if you pull one out from the bottom or even the middle, the whole thing falls apart.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not have a robust inspection program for the foods that it regulates\u8221\'20\'1D, she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so if that\u8217\'20\'19s your baseline, and then you\u8217\'20\'19re cutting back inspectors, then that is very concerning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Foreign food inspections by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cspi.org/cspi-news/foreign-food-safety-inspections-hit-historic-low-after-trump-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped}}}\uc2  to the lowest on record since the agency began inspecting foreign food facilities in 2011, aside from during the Covid-19 pandemic. Domestic inspections also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://datadashboard.fda.gov/oii/cd/inspections.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 steeply declined}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Due to cuts, the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 , which works with the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and other agencies to conduct surveillance for food pathogens, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/cdc-quietly-scaled-back-surveillance-program-foodborne-illnesses-rcna227089?link_source=ta_bluesky_link&taid=68add0b9b2316600014ce6de&utm_campaign=trueanthem&utm_medium=social&utm_source=bluesky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reduced}}}\uc2  the number of pathogens they surveil through its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/foodnet/index.htmL/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Foodnet}}}\uc2  surveillance program from eight to two.\par \par \uc2 Frank Yiannas\uc2 , former \uc2 FDA\uc2  deputy commissioner for food policy and response under the first Trump administration, and into the Biden administration, expressed concern about the reduction in surveillance, with food recalls already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wastedive.com/news/food-recall-organic-waste-usda-fda-misfits-markets/761320/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on the rise}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CFoodnet and the pathogens that they track is critical, because it\u8217\'20\'19s the ultimate scorecard of whether we\u8217\'20\'19re getting better or worse on performance in food safety,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CConsumers in general, when they hear there are cuts to food-borne disease surveillance programs at the CDC, they should pay attention,\u8221\'20\'1D added Yiannas. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a good idea if any food-borne illness remains invisible. We need to know about these things so that we can gather why they happen in the first place, and inform future prevention.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the \uc2 FDA\uc2  grapples with these cuts, former workers criticized the treatment of employees, the wastefulness of firings and rehirings, and dismissed claims by the Trump administration that the cuts have no impact on the agency\u8217\'20\'19s ability to effectively execute its mission.\par \par \uc2 Harbourt, the fired safety manager, said his position\u8217\'20\'19s responsibilities were replaced with two full-time employees, who were pulled away from their initial employment positions. \u8220\'20\'1CTurning the federal government into a temp employee agency is going to have negative effects for all Americans across a number of different aspects of their lives \u8211\'20\'13 some of which we\u8217\'20\'19re already seeing,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Rightwing media pundits have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/worthless-parasites-right-wing-medias-denigration-federal-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  federal employees \u8220\'20\'1Centitled bureaucrats\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cworthless parasites\u8221\'20\'1D, and \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely worthless\u8221\'20\'1D amid cuts to the federal workforce. \uc2 Russell Vought\uc2 , whom Trump tapped to lead the office of management and budget, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oBH9TmeJN_M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stated}}}\uc2  shortly before the 2024 election that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe want the bureaucrats to be traumatically affected\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vast majority of federal employees really do try to do the best work for the American public,\u8221\'20\'1D added Harbourt. \u8220\'20\'1CSeeing that framed as something where we\u8217\'20\'19re all worthless, and we\u8217\'20\'19re just leeches on the American taxpayer is objectively false, and it\u8217\'20\'19s been a really discouraging aspect of this whole process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A former \uc2 FDA\uc2  employee, who requested to remain anonymous to speak without fear of retaliation, criticized the manner in which the administration is transforming the agency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are seeing more policy announcements through journal articles and podcasts rather than through carefully constructed guidance documents that allow for the public to provide comment,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 FDA\uc2  has always steered clear from politics as much as it was able, but we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen such a politicization of science with this administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A third former employee at the FDA, who also requested to remain anonymous, said: \u8220\'20\'1CFor impact public health-wise, this is devastating. Agencies like FDA rely on scientific studies, but do you know what can\u8217\'20\'19t happen without funding? Research. And federal agencies have a responsibility to report to the American people, so without communications professionals, research findings and reporting does not get shared and agency web pages sit stagnant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The current leader of the FDA, Martin Makary, and Robert FKennedy Jr, head of the Department of Health and Human Services, which oversees the agency, have both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/2025/jun/12/chemtrails-rfk-jr-truth-behind-conspiracy-theory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed}}}\uc2  and touted health related conspiracy theories. Makary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.importantcontext.news/p/fda-commissioner-hiv-may-very-well"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently promoted}}}\uc2  lab leak conspiracy theories about HIV and Lyme disease on a podcast.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CScientific integrity has been destroyed by Secretary Kennedy and Secretary Makary. Many longtime FDA leaders have been pushed out, or left, because there is no more credibility in US public health,\u8221\'20\'1D the former employee said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that this decimation of the federal workforce will set us back as a country for decades,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are no longer a world leader in public health, and that\u8217\'20\'19s a scary thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Department of Health and Human Servicesdid not comment on Makary\u8217\'20\'19s recent claims. \u8220\'20\'1CFDA inspectors were not impacted, and this critical work will continue uninterrupted,\u8221\'20\'1D Emily Hilliard, a spokesperson, said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe FDA remains fully committed to protecting the public and ensuring the safety and efficacy of the products it regulates. Enforcement decisions are grounded in the latest gold-standard science. This will not change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another former FDA employee, who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation, said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cabsurd\u8221\'20\'1D to claim that thousands of job cuts would have no impact. \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t even pass the laugh test,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat organization isn\u8217\'20\'19t going to be impacted by the departure, not just of a lot of people, but entire offices?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260113em1d002mi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
