\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We are not for sale\u8217\'20\'19: chair of Greenland\u8217\'20\'19s top labor union rebukes Trump\u8217\'20\'19s call for annexation\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 782 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 January 2026\par 17:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 15\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Exclusive: SIK leader Jess Berthelsen rejects Trump claim that the US needs Greenland for \u8216\'20\'18national security\u8217\'20\'19\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/greenland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Greenland}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not be annexed\u8221\'20\'1D, the longtime leader of its largest labor union has declared, refuting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claims that the Arctic territory\u8217\'20\'19s current status poses a national security threat to the US.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with the Guardian, Jess Berthelsen, chair of SIK, Greenland\u8217\'20\'19s national trade union confederation, said people in the territory do not recognize the US president\u8217\'20\'19s allegations that Russian and Chinese ships are scattered throughout its waters. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t see it, we can\u8217\'20\'19t recognize it and we can\u8217\'20\'19t understand it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jan/07/what-are-trumps-real-options-for-gaining-control-of-greenland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 renewed}}}\uc2  its threats to seize Greenland in recent days, and claimed that officials were even considering using military force as an option, following a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jan/03/is-there-any-legal-justification-for-the-us-attack-on-venezuela-trump-maduro"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raid}}}\uc2  in Venezuela that culminated in the arrest and ouster of the country\u8217\'20\'19s president Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro, and his wife Cilia Flores.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jan/06/why-is-donald-trump-renewing-calls-for-takeover-of-greenland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why is Donald Trump renewing calls for takeover of Greenland?}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need Greenland from the standpoint of national security,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2026/01/06/trump-says-his-greenland-fixation-is-about-national-security-europeans-are-skeptical-00712149"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  during an exchange with reporters aboard Air Force One. \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, Greenland is covered with Russian and Chinese ships all over the place.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Berthelsen, who has led {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sik.gl/da/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SIK}}}\uc2  for over 30 years, disputed this allegation. The union represents thousands of workers, from government employees to electricians, mechanics and fishers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Greenland, it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to recognize the demands Trump is setting,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CHis claims about our waters being full of Russian and Chinese ships, we cannot see that at all. We can\u8217\'20\'19t recognize this postulation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Danish navy is traveling in Greenland waters, and our big trawlers are also everywhere. If that had been the case, they could have told us already, but there\u8217\'20\'19s no such thing. So what is it that he\u8217\'20\'19s talking about?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 European leaders have sought to rally behind Greenland and Denmark in recent days. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is for Denmark and Greenland, and them only, to decide on matters concerning Denmark and Greenland,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 , the UK prime minister, \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , the French president, and \uc2 Friedrich Merz\uc2 , the German chancellor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jan/06/stephen-miller-donald-trump-threats-take-over-greenland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  in a rare European rebuke to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Their statement came after \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s deputy chief of staff for policy, claimed during a CNN interview that \u8220\'20\'1Cnobody\u8221\'20\'1D was \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to fight the United States militarily over the future of Greenland\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Berthelsen emphasized that Greenland was a semi-autonomous part of the Kingdom of Denmark, with self-government. SIK is focused on reaching agreements with Greenland\u8217\'20\'19s government and private employers to better their everyday lives, he said \u8211\'20\'13 and eventually work toward independence as a country.\par \par \uc2 An estimated 84% of Greenlanders support independence, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.euractiv.com/news/virtually-no-greenlander-wants-to-join-the-us-poll-finds/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2025 poll}}}\uc2 , which found that just 6% back a US takeover. The territory has a population of about 57,000 people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGreenland is an autonomous part of the Kingdom of Denmark, and we have self-government, and we have agreements with the Danish government,\u8221\'20\'1D said Berthelsen. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s how things operate. If this is to change, we will take the initiative to change. It\u8217\'20\'19s just hard to fathom the fact that that this is the climate among us at the moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 US corporations, like any other company from the world, can already apply to do business in Greenland, he added. SIK has agreements with the Danish state and companies, setting terms for wages and working conditions.\par \par \uc2 Cooperation between Greenland and the US was undermined by the \uc2 US government\uc2  making constant threats to Greenland\u8217\'20\'19s autonomy, including the threat of military intervention, Berthelsen argued.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not for sale and that we will not be annexed,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will determine our own future, and we will continue to work with Denmark and the United States. We have always considered the United States as our ally. That has always been so for many years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not very comfortable to receive threats from a lifelong friend, a lifelong ally. Cooperation cannot take place if we are receiving threats like these constantly. How can we cooperate when we are receiving constant threats with military intervention? Nobody does that to their friends, or people they cooperate with.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Contacted for comment, the White House deferred to a statement made by the press secretary, Karoline Leavitt, on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CAll options are always on the table for President Trump as he examines what\u8217\'20\'19s in the best interest of the United States, but I will just say that the president\u8217\'20\'19s first option always has been diplomacy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260109em19002ef\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
