\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Fema staff outraged by draft plans for deep cuts under Trump\b0\par\par\uc2 Dharna Noor \par \uc2 781 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 January 2026\par 15:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2026.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Staff warn that the homeland security secretary\u8217\'20\'19s proposed cuts could weaken Fema\u8217\'20\'19s disaster response\par \par \uc2 Current and former staff at the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema) expressed outraged over reports that the agency has drafted plans to eliminate thousands of staff in 2026 \u8211\'20\'13 part of a broader restructuring effort being overseen by the homeland security secretary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kristi-noem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kristi Noem}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  seems determined to continue weakening the agency\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to help people before, during and after disasters,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jeremy Edwards, former spokesperson for Fema and the White House during \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 Fema has already seen a mass exodus of staff since Trump re-entered the White House in January. Further cuts would be \u8220\'20\'1Can affront to not only the law, but also to common sense when we are in a situation where states and local communities have been vocal about the fact they do not have the ability or the capacity to replicate what Fema does for them\u8221\'20\'1D, one longtime Fema official, who requested anonymity, said.\par \par \uc2 The response came after dozens of senior agency employees on 23 December reportedly received notice about the launch of a workforce planning exercise, asking them to identify which Fema positions are critically necessary for the agency\u8217\'20\'19s operations and which could be slashed. It also included a spreadsheet outlining a goal to cut Fema staff by more than 50% by the next fiscal year\u8217\'20\'19s start in October, though it reportedly no said decisions about workforce reductions have not been finalized.\par \par \uc2 Reached for comment, a Fema spokesperson said the agency \u8220\'20\'1Chas not issued and is not implementing a percentage-based workforce reduction\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no directive to reduce the agency\u8217\'20\'19s workforce by 50%, and no such target has been approved by [the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 ] or the White House. The materials referenced from the leaked documentation stem from a routine, pre-decisional workforce planning exercise,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said. \u8220\'20\'1CAn accompanying spreadsheet was an internal working tool used to collect planning inputs. Any numerical assumptions reflected in that draft were not approved, were not adopted, and do not represent Fema policy or leadership direction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the 50% target echoes recommendations from the the taskforce that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  set up last year to help overhaul the agency. A draft of that group\u8217\'20\'19s final report, which was leaked to CNN last month, also called for cutting the agency\u8217\'20\'19s workforce in half and shifting many full-time staff out of Washington DC to nationwide regional offices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPolitical leadership at Fema can pretend that this is just a training exercise, but anyone with eyes knows that \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  has been hellbent on such workforce reductions and they have already successfully fired or laid off literally thousands of full time staff,\u8221\'20\'1D said Edwards, the former spokesperson for Fema.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt seems like an oddly specific exercise to do if it\u8217\'20\'19s not something you are actively preparing for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Edwards said he participated in training exercises while at Fema, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut never something like this\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are usually situation-based and related to specific emergency events, in my experience,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo it\u8217\'20\'19s very strange to just randomly say: \u8216\'20\'18What if we cut the staff by 50%?\u8217\'20\'19 It\u8217\'20\'19s less strange when you remember that this type of staff reduction is something this administration has had its eye on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nearly 2,450 employees of Fema are estimated to have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-25-108598"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exited the agency}}}\uc2  since the second Trump administration began. On 31 December 2025, some employees also reportedly received emails saying their positions would not be renewed once their contracts expire in the first days of January.\par \par \uc2 Those recent cuts specifically target the agency\u8217\'20\'19s cadre of on-call response and recovery teams, its term-limited workforce that provides crucial support in disaster response and recovery efforts. These recent changes could be a major blow to disaster recovery, the longtime Fema official said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CImagine if we had to tackle a Helene or Milton or Maria or Irma without the backbone of our forward-deploying force,\u8221\'20\'1D the person said. \u8220\'20\'1CThese decisions are made by people at the top of Fema and at [the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 ] who have no idea how anything works, don\u8217\'20\'19t care about the agency or its people, or the American people. Their only goal is to prove who can show the most fealty to the administration no matter how damaging or cruel those actions end up being.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Edwards said changes under Noem are pushing the agency in the wrong direction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe agency should be focused on preparing communities for inevitable disasters, not its own demise,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020260108em180048t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
