\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 ICE plans $100m yearlong \u8216\'20\'18wartime recruitment\u8217\'20\'19 media blitz to attract new agents\b0\par\par\uc2 Alexandra Villarreal \par \uc2 676 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 December 2025\par 21:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Campaign will target rightwing ideologues to fill ranks to meet Trump deportation goals in 2026\par \par \uc2 US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ice-us-immigration-and-customs-enforcement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE)}}}\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2025/12/31/ice-wartime-recruitment-push/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  planned a $100m, one-year media blitz for what it\u8217\'20\'19s calling \u8220\'20\'1Cwartime recruitment\u8221\'20\'1D, targeting conservative radio show listeners, gun rights aficionados, military affairs followers and men\u8217\'20\'19s interests enthusiasts \u8211\'20\'13 among others in the Maga-verse \u8211\'20\'13 for jobs in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s next phase of its mass deportation campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWant to deport illegals with your absolute boys?\u8221\'20\'1D one of the agency\u8217\'20\'19s ads {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/DHSgov/status/1952853433113035181"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2 , directing interested readers to apply.\par \par \uc2 As ICE looks to hire for thousands of new positions, flush with cash after an unprecedented {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nilc.org/resources/the-anti-immigrant-policies-in-trumps-final-big-beautiful-bill-explained/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 influx}}}\uc2  from Congress last summer, it\u8217\'20\'19s relying on geofencing to ensure people near military bases, Nascar races, gun and trade shows, and college campuses receive its recruitment ads, according to an internal document {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2025/12/31/ice-wartime-recruitment-push/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Officials also intend to spend $8m or more on deals with fitness, military and tactical/lifestyle online influencers, who would use their sway to push the administration\u8217\'20\'19s immigration agenda through livestreams, events, and other content meant for their gen Z and millennial audiences.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica has been invaded by criminals and predators. We need YOU to get them out,\u8221\'20\'1D ICE\u8217\'20\'19s recruiting website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ice.gov/join"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The administration\u8217\'20\'19s hiring push comes after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  signed HR 1 into law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/1/all-actions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in July}}}\uc2 , which allotted $45bn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nilc.org/resources/the-anti-immigrant-policies-in-trumps-final-big-beautiful-bill-explained/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for immigration detention}}}\uc2  and $32bn for immigration enforcement-related activities and personnel.\par \par \uc2 Yet even as ICE now has the funds to hire about 14,000 new employees, its efforts to quickly do so have raised red flags among everyday citizens disgusted by the recruitment ads themselves and experts concerned that the speed and tone with which the federal government is pursuing new agents could attract more aggressive, combat-hungry applicants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re aiming for that sweet spot of people who\u8217\'20\'19ve got something to prove, who want to have that power, under the guise of patriotism,\u8221\'20\'1D Americus Reed, a marketing professor at the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Wharton School\uc2 , told the Post.\par \par \uc2 ICE\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/ice-ads-all-over-streaming-services-spotify-hbo-pandora-1235447970/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial}}}\uc2  ads have leaned heavily on American symbolism \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ice.gov/join"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uncle Sam}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2025/12/31/ice-wartime-recruitment-push/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Washington}}}\uc2 , Lady Liberty \u8211\'20\'13 while casting immigrants as bad actors to convince potential deportation officers to apply.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, ICE is offering an up to $50,000 signing bonus, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/MEPAINUSA672N"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 higher}}}\uc2  than the real median personal income for a year\u8217\'20\'19s work in the US, as well as up to $60,000 in student loan repayment for those who join.\par \par \uc2 The agency has already received more than 220,000 applications and made more than 18,000 tentative job offers, sometimes on the spot. At an ICE recruitment fair in Arlington, Texas, more than a hundred people were waiting outside before the event started. Attenders told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000010354368/what-we-saw-at-a-job-fair-for-ice.html?campaign_id=9&emc=edit_nn_20251231&instance_id=168658&nl=the-morning&regi_id=110371034&segment_id=212947&user_id=224c737bae1a689c717f5bb8261c60df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2  they were there because they were \u8220\'20\'1Cvery patriotic\u8221\'20\'1D and committed to \u8220\'20\'1Cguarding the homeland\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I saw Uncle Sam pointing that finger, I just had it in my heart,\u8221\'20\'1D Mahin Ahmed, an ICE applicant, told the Times. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re thinking, \u8216\'20\'18Look at this guy. He\u8217\'20\'19s an immigrant. He wants to become a deportation officer.\u8217\'20\'19 It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make any sense to you, makes 100 percent sense to me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With more ICE officers available, the White House border czar, Tom Homan, said that the number of immigrant arrests will \u8220\'20\'1Cexplode\u8221\'20\'1D in 2026, including through an increase in enforcement at workplaces, Reuters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-set-expand-immigration-crackdown-2026-despite-brewing-backlash-2025-12-21/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Homan\u8217\'20\'19s comments came after the administration had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/national-security/5647146-immigration-enforcement-tactics-change/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signaled}}}\uc2  it would instead be toning down its public-facing immigration actions to focus on apprehending people with serious criminal convictions, in the face of widespread backlash to its violent and highly visible tactics in major cities around the country.\par \par \uc2 Already, ICE held a record number of people \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/22/ice-detentions-record-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 68,440}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 in detention in recent weeks, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tracreports.org/immigration/quickfacts/detention.html#detention_newbookings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vast majority}}}\uc2  with no criminal conviction. But the administration remained far below its goal of a million deportations in its first year, with about 300,000 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tracreports.org/whatsnew/email.251124.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 removals}}}\uc2  since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second inauguration.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251231elcv005bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
