\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s not a coincidence\u8217\'20\'19: journalists of color on being laid off amid Trump\u8217\'20\'19s anti-DEI push\b0\par\par\uc2 Melissa Hellmann \par \uc2 2,228 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 December 2025\par 20:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Black and brown former employees from \uc2 CBS\uc2 , NBC and Teen Vogue talk about the effects of being let go\par \par \uc2 Trey Sherman was traveling to work on the New York subway when he received an email from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2025/11/07/bari-weiss-cbs-news-remake/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Reiter}}}\uc2 , a CBS News executive, about an imminent meeting on 29 October. Sherman, an associate producer of CBS Evening News Plus at the time, suspected that he would be laid off. CBS News\u8217\'20\'19s parent company, Paramount, had closed a merger with the Hollywood studio Skydance in August, and planned to slash {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/29/business/media/paramount-layoffs-skydance.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 2,000 jobs}}}\uc2  as part of corporate restructuring.\par \par \uc2 Sherman, who is Black, and Reiter, who is white, had an amicable conversation, according to Sherman. Reiter told Sherman that he was being laid off because his show was being eliminated, Sherman said, and that Reiter was unable to assign the team to other positions. Sherman accepted the news and the two men wished each other good luck.\par \par \uc2 But when Sherman left the conference room and entered the newsroom, he said he learned that his white colleagues had been told a very different story. A white co-worker told Sherman that she found it \u8220\'20\'1Cmessed up\u8221\'20\'1D that the people of color on the team had been laid off. Of the nine producers who staffed CBS Evening News Plus, five white people were reassigned to other positions, while the four people of color on the team were let go, according to Sherman and another former staffer who spoke on the condition of anonymity out of fear of retaliation. Later that day, Sherman documented his experience in a viral {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@treymous/video/7566730826885516575"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TikTok video}}}\uc2 . \uc2 CBS\uc2  did not respond to the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Sherman\u8217\'20\'19s role may be the latest casualty in a nationwide {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/nov/08/joy-reid-msnbc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crackdown on diversity}}}\uc2 . Several high-ranking Black officials have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/08/us/politics/black-leaders-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2  from the Trump administration, and thousands of jobs related to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2025/05/27/nx-s1-5307319/dei-jobs-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 diversity, equity and inclusion (DEI)}}}\uc2  have been cut in the private and public sectors. The Guardian talked to seven recently laid off journalists at \uc2 CBS\uc2 , NBC and Teen Vogue who spoke of people of color on their teams being let go while their white colleagues were spared, or the chipping away at coverage focused on marginalized communities.\par \par \uc2 Newsrooms have long been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2018/11/02/newsroom-employees-are-less-diverse-than-u-s-workers-overall/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less diverse}}}\uc2  than the US population, which makes these layoffs in particular especially pronounced. In 1978, the \uc2 American Society of Newspaper Editors\uc2 , an organization for media leaders, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://voices.aaja.org/stories/philadelphia-2017/missed-deadline-the-delayed-promise-of-newsroom-diversity/#:~:text=In%201978%2C%20the%20American%20Society%20of%20Newspaper,the%20nation's%20diversity%20by%20the%20year%202000."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed}}}\uc2  that the racial makeup of newsrooms would reflect the US population by 2000. As the deadline neared in 1998, the society {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/1998/10/26/business/editors-delay-goal-on-diversity-and-add-a-concern-for-women.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moved}}}\uc2  the date to 2025, but newsrooms still haven\u8217\'20\'19t met that goal. According to a 2022 \uc2 Pew Research Center{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2023/04/04/us-journalists-beats-vary-widely-by-gender-and-other-factors/#:~:text=Overall%2C%2076%25%20of%20all%20reporting,workers%20overall%20who%20are%20White."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  of nearly 12,000 journalists, 76% of respondents were white, 8% were Latino/Hispanic, 6% were Black and 3% were Asian. The survey showed an overrepresentation of white journalists, since nearly 58% of the population was white, about 19% were Hispanic, 12% were Black and 6% were Asian in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/race-and-ethnicity/2025/11/03/counting-race-how-the-census-measures-identity-and-what-americans-think-about-it/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 US census}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some journalists see the layoffs as capitulation to the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s war on DEI. After Trump\u8217\'20\'19s January executive orders calling for an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/01/ending-radical-and-wasteful-government-dei-programs-and-preferencing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 end to DEI programs}}}\uc2  and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/01/ending-illegal-discrimination-and-restoring-merit-based-opportunity/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 termination of affirmative action}}}\uc2  in the federal government, Sherman said that \u8220\'20\'1Cone by one, we saw companies get rid of their DEI initiatives\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 CBS\uc2  and NBC are subjected to regulatory scrutiny by the \uc2 Federal Communications Commission (FCC)\uc2 , which oversees radio, television, cable, satellite and wire communications. During his first week in office, \uc2 Brendan Carr\uc2 , the \uc2 FCC\uc2  chair, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.fcc.gov/public/attachments/DOC-409054A1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that the \uc2 FCC\uc2  would end its DEI efforts by, among other things, removing it as a priority from the agency\u8217\'20\'19s budget, and quashing its advisory group and taskforce.\par \par \uc2 Several weeks later, Carr launched an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fcc.gov/sites/default/files/Chairman-Carr-Letter%20to-Comcast-02112025.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation}}}\uc2  into \uc2 Comcast\uc2  and NBC Universal\u8217\'20\'19s diversity initiatives, followed by a similar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fcc.gov/sites/default/files/Carr-Letter-to-Disney-DEI-03252027.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inquiry}}}\uc2  into \uc2 Disney\uc2  and ABC. \uc2 Disney\uc2  told employees in a February {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/disney-is-latest-company-to-shake-up-dei-initiatives-memo-2025-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo}}}\uc2  that it would stop Reimagine Tomorrow, a platform that amplified underrepresented voices, and the corporation\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/disney-diversity-dei-inclusion-annual-report-earnings-2025-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2025 annual report}}}\uc2  eschewed the word \u8220\'20\'1Cdiversity\u8221\'20\'1D for the first time in six years.\par \par \uc2 In July filings to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fcc.gov/ecfs/document/1072299913934/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FCC}}}\uc2  before the merger, \uc2 Skydance\uc2  promised that it would eliminate Paramount\u8217\'20\'19s DEI initiatives and workforce diversity targets. And in October, Bari Weiss, an opinion journalist who advocated to \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tabletmag.com/sections/news/articles/end-dei-bari-weiss-jews"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 end DEI for good}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, was appointed the editor in chief of CBS News. Some CBS News employees have been on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2025/11/07/bari-weiss-cbs-news-remake/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 edge}}}\uc2  since Weiss\u8217\'20\'19s appointment.\par \par \uc2 Then in early November, sources allege that most Teen Vogue employees \u8211\'20\'13 many of whom were women of color \u8211\'20\'13 were let go as publisher Cond\u233\'00\'E9 Nast {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vogue.com/article/teen-vogue-is-joining-voguecom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that the outlet focused on politics, fashion and news would join Vogue\u8217\'20\'19s website. A Cond\u233\'00\'E9 Nast spokesperson said it was inaccurate that most of the staff had been let go. Those reductions came several weeks after NBC News laid off {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/nbc-news-cuts-roughly-150-163358784.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 150 employees}}}\uc2 , and gutted teams on verticals that exclusively covered Black, Asian American, Latino, and LGBTQ+ communities. The equity-focused sections will continue to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thewrap.com/nbc-news-layoffs-number-versant-split/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exist}}}\uc2 , though without a dedicated staff, drawing from content around the newsroom.\par \par \uc2 Some institutions within the journalism industry have also steered away from DEI in their company language since Trump entered office. In April, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.niemanlab.org/2025/04/gannett-will-stop-publishing-diversity-information-citing-trumps-executive-order/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gannett}}}\uc2  removed demographic data and mentions about diversity from its website, citing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order calling for an end to DEI.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration \u8220\'20\'1Chas used its power to exert more control over the media than maybe we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever seen\u8221\'20\'1D, Sherman said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt so happens that part of their agenda is to, let\u8217\'20\'19s be real, not just get rid of DEI initiatives, but to get rid of diversity in and of itself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a political climate that\u8217\'20\'19s hostile to diversity, people of color must start their own media outlets and podcasts, said political commentator and \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  board member \uc2 Roland Martin\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CThese companies are going to learn a hard lesson: if you continue to remove Black, Latino, Muslim and Asian American voices, those consumers are going to go elsewhere.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s not a coincidence\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 After speaking to his white colleagues, Sherman went to Reiter\u8217\'20\'19s office to confront him about the layoff discrepancies. Sherman said that Reiter told him that he chose to keep people he had previously worked with. After Sherman posted his video recapping the conversation with Reiter on \uc2 TikTok\uc2 , he said he received messages from former employees at other media outlets who had similar stories. Mary, a woman of color who is using a pseudonym out of fear of jeopardizing future job prospects, said that she was shocked when she watched Sherman\u8217\'20\'19s video.\par \par \uc2 She was laid off from another \uc2 CBS\uc2  team on the same day as Sherman, and soon realized that out of the dozens of people on her diverse team, the only four who were laid off were people of color. \u8220\'20\'1CWe certainly have white producers, we have white reporters who could have been laid off as well,\u8221\'20\'1D Mary said. They had to have \u8220\'20\'1Cknown that would not look good\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/paramount-layoff-memo-1000-employees-ceo-david-ellison-2025-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo}}}\uc2  to employees, the new \uc2 Paramount Skydance\uc2  CEO \uc2 David Ellison\uc2  wrote that the cuts were necessary for the company\u8217\'20\'19s longevity. \u8220\'20\'1CIn some areas, we are addressing redundancies that have emerged across the organization,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CIn others, we are phasing out roles that are no longer aligned with our evolving priorities and the new structure designed to strengthen our focus on growth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mary and Sherman, though, say it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s methodology for who they chose to lay off reflects the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s assault on diversity. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not accusing any one person of looking at my department and deciding to lay off all the people of color,\u8221\'20\'1D Sherman said, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut I am saying that it\u8217\'20\'19s not a coincidence that the layoffs that they chose to do fell along racial lines.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While Sherman would not comment on whether he was pursuing legal action, Mary said that she and several former \uc2 CBS\uc2  employees have expressed interest in filing a lawsuit: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is very suspicious.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In mid-October, the entire teams behind NBC BLK, NBC Asian America, NBC Latino, and NBC Out were laid off, but content from around the newsroom will continue to populate the verticals. Curtis Bunn, the only reporter at NBC BLK, a vertical that focuses on Black communities, was one of the people who was let go. Over the past two years, he said, he watched the team dwindle from four people to two until the final purge. The layoffs also come as most of \uc2 Comcast\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 NBCUniversal\uc2  cable networks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/andymeek/2025/10/15/layoffs-at-nbc-news-and-the-painful-math-behind-the-versant-spinoff/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spin off}}}\uc2  into a new company called \uc2 Versant Media Group\uc2 , causing NBC News to streamline its operations. (Forty {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/comcast-nbc-news-layoffs-40-job-cuts-shift-to-digital-2025-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 people}}}\uc2  were also let go from NBC in January. An NBC union representative said it does not have a demographic breakdown of the layoffs.)\par \par \uc2 Bunn said that he trusts the company\u8217\'20\'19s reasoning, but he is curious about why the teams that covered marginalized communities were eliminated. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you see what\u8217\'20\'19s happening around you, and you see the nature of even the media companies capitulating to the administration,\u8221\'20\'1D Bunn said, \u8220\'20\'1Cyou can\u8217\'20\'19t help but feel like that has some part or some role in what took place.\u8221\'20\'1D He said that he was told that he could apply for other roles at the company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe journalists behind NBC BLK, NBC Latino, NBC Asian America and NBC OUT have chronicled our communities with depth, nuance and humanity,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 NABJ\uc2  president and co-founder of the 19th, Errin Haines, said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nabjonline.org/blog/nbcnewsmeeting/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIf anything, their work has strengthened our democracy and expanded our nation\u8217\'20\'19s understanding of itself.\u8221\'20\'1D NBC did not initially respond to repeated requests for comment. After this story was published, NBC News spokesperson Dominique Donahue offered a statement: \u8220\'20\'1CMore than half of the employees (of the verticals mentioned) were rehired to new roles producing content for the broader newsroom, which includes content for the verticals.\u8221\'20\'1D The Guardian has not been able to independently verify this information.\par \par \uc2 Traci Lee, a journalist who was NBC Asian America\u8217\'20\'19s digital editorial manager from 2015 to 2019, said that the vertical helped elevate Asian American and Pacific Islanders\u8217\'20\'19 experiences to a national sphere. \u8220\'20\'1CSo often we have other people telling our stories for us, whether it is being glossed over in history books, or perhaps just being excluded from the narrative,\u8221\'20\'1D Lee said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a space where we could, on a national level, tell our own stories.\u8221\'20\'1D When NBC Asian America wrote stories about the concentration camps that held Japanese Americans during the second world war, readers reached out to say that they had never been taught about the topic in school.\par \par \uc2 Leaders from affinity groups including the \uc2 Asian American Journalists Association\uc2 , \uc2 NABJ\uc2  and \uc2 NLGJA\uc2 : the Association of LGBTQ+ Journalists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aaja.org/2025/10/23/aaja-nabj-jaws-and-nlgja-issue-statements-on-nbc-news-decision-to-lay-off-staffers-from-their-sites-dedicated-to-marginalized-communities/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 met}}}\uc2  with NBC\u8217\'20\'19s executives about the layoffs in late October, during which NBC promised to continue covering their communities.\par \par \uc2 It was soon after this that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://peoplesworld.org/article/conde-nast-bends-under-trump-decimates-teen-vogue-staff/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five}}}\uc2  women of color from Teen Vogue were let go. Cond\u233\'00\'E9 Nast, Teen Vogue\u8217\'20\'19s parent company, would not confirm the number of laid-off staff or their demographics.\par \par \uc2 Skyli Alvarez, an Asian queer woman on Teen Vogue\u8217\'20\'19s editorial team who was laid off, said that she was in a state of shock when she realized that most of the laid-off employees were people of color. \u8220\'20\'1CIn the media landscape today, a lot of people of color, a lot of people of marginalized identities, tend to be in these entry-level, associate-level positions,\u8221\'20\'1D Alvarez said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so to me, I was like: \u8216\'20\'18This speaks to a bigger issue beyond all of us.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Cond\u233\'00\'E9 Nast spokesperson said that the restructure is designed to help the company grow, since Teen Vogue has long faced difficulties in reaching audiences. \u8220\'20\'1CRather than continuing to operate independently, bringing Teen Vogue under the Vogue umbrella allows it to tap into a larger audience, stronger distribution and more resources,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said. \u8220\'20\'1CAny organizational changes the company makes are purely driven by business strategy to grow consumer engagement with our titles.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTeen Vogue was one of the last really outspoken publications on problems that affect young people, that young people care about,\u8221\'20\'1D Alvarez said. She hopes that communities of color and LGBTQ+ people will continue ensuring that their perspectives are heard nationwide despite the publication\u8217\'20\'19s absorption.\par \par \uc2 In light of the mass layoffs, some Black creatives have begun gathering online to form a collective in their vision. In early November, Aniyah Freeman, a digital marketer based in New York, put a callout on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/aniyah-freeman-20156914a_now-would-be-a-great-time-for-the-black-journalists-activity-7391508737447968770--Zvk?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAAf_LF4BmafYREpkEpHlMhLWZ7S-tPrEBEk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LinkedIn}}}\uc2  to start a media company with recently laid-off Black journalists. So far, she said, about 200 people have joined a group chat; a core group of 15 recently laid-off Black media professionals from various companies including ABC, \uc2 Rolling Stone\uc2  and Cond\u233\'00\'E9 Nast have met on \uc2 Zoom\uc2  several times.\par \par \uc2 For now, their media company is called Black Media Caucus, and they are working on business plans for a magazine focused on politics, fashion and culture. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to be giving us perspectives that they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to take away from us,\u8221\'20\'1D Freeman said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need Black-owned-and-run establishments that are going to stay that way. This current political climate is an inspiration for all of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251231elcv00565\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
