\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US labor unions gear up to fight against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18Billionaire First\u8217\'20\'19 agenda\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 855 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 December 2025\par 16:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  president \uc2 Liz Shuler\uc2  says union ready to stand up for struggling Americans: \u8216\'20\'18Which side are you on?\u8217\'20\'19\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  has staged a year of \u8220\'20\'1Cunrelenting attacks on working people,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the head of the largest federation of the labor unions in the US. Now they\u8217\'20\'19re preparing to fight back.\par \par \uc2 Liz Shuler\uc2 , president of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , said it was gearing up to challenge the US president\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CBillionaire First\u8221\'20\'1D agenda in 2026 \u8211\'20\'13 and drive candidates in key elections to stand up for \u8220\'20\'1Cstruggling\u8221\'20\'1D Americans.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with the Guardian, she described how the federation has pushed to restore collective bargaining rights for federal workers, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/article/summary-of-afge-lawsuits-against-trump--how-litigation-works-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  lawsuits against the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to weaken unions and worker protections. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople were pissed,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shuler.\par \par \uc2 The House of Representatives{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/press/releases/labor-movement-delivers-bipartisan-victory-house-passes-bill-restore-federal-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  passed }}}\uc2 a bill on 11 December that would restore collective bargaining rights for federal workers in response to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive orders that stripped the rights from more than 1 million federal government employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was through a lot of good old-fashioned organizing,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shuler, who accused the president of overseeing \u8220\'20\'1Cthe biggest attack on unions in our history\u8221\'20\'1D by moving to eliminate collective bargaining for federal workers.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  is now steeling itself for a fight to pass the bill in the Senate in January, kicking off what it likely to be another hectic year. The threat of another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/nov/12/house-bill-government-shutdown-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 government shutdown}}}\uc2  looms at the end of January. The fight over extending {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/14/aca-obamacare-expires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Affordable Care Act subsidies}}}\uc2  is far from over.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re organizing as we speak,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shuler. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can move actual people, in workplaces, in every city, in every state, across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Affordability has come into sharp focus, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/dec/18/november-us-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inflation still stubbornly above typical levels}}}\uc2 , and many Americans grappling with rising bills and prices. The federation intends to build momentum into the 2026 midterm elections on such kitchen table issues, according to Shuler, who said labor organizations were already reaching out to working people, canvassing and knocking on doors, in an effort to break through the noise.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are fed up,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re saturated. I think they\u8217\'20\'19re distrustful of institutions and the media. All of the folks that we have come to rely on over the years seem to be waning in trust, and there\u8217\'20\'19s only one organization left that people do trust, and that\u8217\'20\'19s the labor movement, unions. Our credibility and trust is actually going up. And so we think that we have to capitalize on what our sweet spot is, which is using our sphere of influence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 About 68% of Americans support labor unions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/694472/labor-union-approval-relatively-steady.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Gallup}}}\uc2 , despite a downward trend of union density in the US over the past several decades, which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unions-help-reduce-disparities-and-strengthen-our-democracy/#:~:text=Unions%20lower%20inequality,point%20since%20the%20Great%20Depression."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 correlated with the growth of income inequality}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump promised to lower costs on day one and create good jobs, especially in manufacturing, noted Shuler. Those promises have not yet been fulfilled. Trump described apprehension over affordability as a \u8220\'20\'1Choax\u8221\'20\'1D, and sought to downplay economic concerns such as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/dec/16/jobs-report-october-november"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sputtering job market}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not what people are experiencing,\u8221\'20\'1D Shuler said of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s narrative. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re having to run up their credit-card debt. It\u8217\'20\'19s at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/household-debt-hit-new-high-what-to-do-about-yours-now/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an all-time high}}}\uc2 , just to afford groceries. They\u8217\'20\'19re looking at how they\u8217\'20\'19re going to make their car payment, how they\u8217\'20\'19re going to afford rent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I\u8217\'20\'19m out on the road talking to people, housing and healthcare are two issues everybody is feeling. And that is not on the \u8216\'20\'18Billionaire First\u8217\'20\'19 agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump is \u8220\'20\'1Crewarding the big corporations and the rich\u8221\'20\'1D while many Americans are \u8220\'20\'1Cactually struggling\u8221\'20\'1D, she added. \u8220\'20\'1CI think that\u8217\'20\'19s going to come into sharper focus as we go on into 2026. And that is what the labor movement is going to be very clear on. What are workers\u8217\'20\'19 demands? Who is standing with us when it comes to candidates, and elected officials? And which side are you on?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thousands of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  baristas are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/02/starbucks-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently on strike}}}\uc2 , as they campaign for the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest coffee chain to grant them their first union contract.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/02/starbucks-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re not going anywhere\u8217\'20\'19: how unionization \u8216\'20\'18whirlwind\u8217\'20\'19 set stage for historic Starbucks strike}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis strike has really brought it in sharp focus, this divide that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing of an economy that\u8217\'20\'19s working for the very rich, for the billionaires, the corporations and working people are piecing it together,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shuler. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re often working two or three jobs just to get by.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe future of this economy is absolutely in peril, if you think about how inequality is rampant, but also AI and advanced technology is going to continue to create this divide between the ultra rich and everyday people just trying to make a living.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s only going to get worse if we don\u8217\'20\'19t get the guardrails in place, have more power for working people to negotiate what they need and bring some balance back into our economy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House was contacted for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251225elcp001e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
