\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US lost 105,000 jobs in October and added 64,000 in November, according to delayed data\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 799 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 December 2025\par 14:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Data shows the headline unemployment rate continued to climb and hit 4.6%, a four-year high, last month\par \par \uc2 The US labor market grew by more than expected last month, recovering some of the damage inflicted by the federal government shutdown, according to official data.\par \par \uc2 An estimated 105,000 jobs were lost in October, and 64,000 were added in November, a highly-anticipated report showed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Jobs growth was higher in November than anticipated by many economists, with a consensus forecast of some 40,000 jobs added.\par \par \uc2 But the headline unemployment rate continued to climb \u8211\'20\'13 and hit 4.6%, a four-year high, last month \u8211\'20\'13 amid apprehension around the strength of the US economy.\par \par \uc2 Previous estimates for overall jobs growth in August and September were also downgraded, from a drop of 4,000 to 26,000, and from growth of 119,000 to 108,000, respectively.\par \par \uc2 The latest jobs numbers, typically released monthly, were delayed due to the government shutdown. Federal government jobs declined by 162,000 in October, and 6,000 in November.\par \par \uc2 The latest jobs numbers arrive against a tumultuous background for the US\u8217\'20\'19s economic data, once regarded as the gold standard in government data.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  (\uc2 BLS\uc2 ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/bls/2025-lapse-revised-release-dates.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that full October jobs data would not be released and November\u8217\'20\'19s jobs data was delayed due to the 43-day federal government shutdown. Questions have also been raised about its accuracy.\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve chair {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/jerome-powell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jerome Powell}}}\uc2  warned last week that the data from the \uc2 BLS\uc2  should be treated with a \u8220\'20\'1Cskeptical eye\u8221\'20\'1D while the hangover left from the shutdown works through the system.\par \par \uc2 There are signs that the US\u8217\'20\'19s job market is weakening. ADP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/dec/03/us-private-payroll-jobs-decline-november"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  US private sector employers shed about 32,000 jobs in November after adding 47,000 jobs in October.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/nov/20/us-jobs-report-september-shutdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September jobs report}}}\uc2 , released late in November due to the federal government shutdown, stated the US added 119,000 jobs, higher than economist predictions. Unemployment rate ticked up from 4.3% to 4.4% in September, its highest level since 2021.\par \par \uc2 Powell cautioned last week that jobs figures are likely worse than the numbers that have been reported and that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s immigration policies have hurt labor supply, which has kept the unemployment rate relatively flat.\par \par \uc2 His comments came after the Fed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/sep/17/federal-reserve-interest-rate-decision-jerome-powell-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced }}}\uc2 it was cutting interest rates by a quarter point, a move toward \u8220\'20\'1Crisk management\u8221\'20\'1D over concerns of a weakening labor market.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLabor supply has also come down quite sharply. So, you know, if you had a world where there is just no growth in workers and you really don\u8217\'20\'19t need a lot of jobs to have full employment, some people argue that is what we are looking at,\u8221\'20\'1D said Powell. \u8220\'20\'1CSo, there is an overcount in the payroll job numbers, we think, continuing, and it will be corrected. I don\u8217\'20\'19t have an exact month in my head right now. Again, I think forecasters generally understand that. We think it is about 60,000 a month, so 40,000 jobs could be negative 20, but that could be wrong by 10 or 20 in either direction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Powell also cautioned about the veracity of the jobs report data due to the lack of data collection in October and early November due to the government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to get data, but we are going to have to look at it carefully and a somewhat skeptical eye by the January meeting,\u8221\'20\'1D added Powell.\par \par \uc2 Economists suggested on Tuesday that the latest jobs report was unlikely to persuade policymakers on the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s open market committee to ease monetary policy, and cut rates, at its next meeting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe labor market remains weak, but the pace of deterioration probably is too slow to spur the FOMC to ease again in January,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Samuel Tombs\uc2 , chief US economist at Pantheon Macroeconomics.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BLS\uc2  has been under attack from the Trump administration. In August, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/01/trump-fires-erika-mcentarfer-labor-statistics#:~:text=4%20months%20old-,Trump%20fires%20labor%20statistics%20chief%20hours%20after%20data%20showed%20jobs,this%20Biden%20Political%20Appointee%2C%20IMMEDIATELY."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2 BLS\uc2  commissioner Erika McEntarfer, hours after the July jobs report was published. Trump claimed, without evidence, the report was \u8220\'20\'1Crigged\u8221\'20\'1D to make him look bad.\par \par \uc2 His nominee to replace McEntarfer, EJ Antoni, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2025/09/30/white-house-withdraws-ej-antoni-nomination-lead-bls-00589289"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrawn}}}\uc2  in late September after bipartisan criticism over his lack of qualifications. The \uc2 BLS\uc2  was shut down, furloughing staff, during the 43-day shutdown of the federal government and a new nominee to lead the agency has yet to be made.\par \par \uc2 The lack of leadership at the agency comes as the number of staff at the agency has shrunk under the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 . The agency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amstat.org/docs/default-source/amstat-documents/the-nations-data-at-risk-2025/The-Nations-Data-at-Risk-2025-Report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost 20% }}}\uc2 of staff from fiscal year 2024, 2,058 total employees, to proposed staff levels for fiscal year 2026, 1,851 total employees.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251216elcg003xp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
