\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Just disgraceful\u8217\'20\'19: outcry as Heritage thinktank appoints far-right figure to key post\b0\par\par\uc2 Jason Wilson \par \uc2 2,697 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 December 2025\par 23:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Scott Yenor, who has offered views on women, marriage and LGBTQ+ rights, helped to found secretive fraternal order\par \par \uc2 The Heritage Foundation\uc2 , an influential rightwing thinktank {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2025/nov/20/nick-fuentes-tucker-carlson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently mired in controversy}}}\uc2  over its president\u8217\'20\'19s apparent apology for extremism, has appointed as a director the founder of a secretive all-male network of Christian nationalist fraternal lodges.\par \par \uc2 Scott Yenor, appointed as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/staff/scott-yenor-phd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Heritage\u8217\'20\'19s new director of the B Kenneth Simon Center for American Studies}}}\uc2 , has also recently offered ultra-conservative opinions on women, marriage and LGBTQ+ rights in recent podcast appearances and speaking engagements.\par \par \uc2 They have included that there is{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BV3tH9vyDh8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  an association between homosexuality and pedophilia}}}\uc2 ; that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BV3tH9vyDh8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adultery, homosexuality, no-fault divorce, and abortion should be outlawed}}}\uc2  under a regime of \u8220\'20\'1Csoft patriarchy\u8221\'20\'1D; and that elements of the US Civil Rights Act, including its prohibitions against workplace sex discrimination, should be wound back.\par \par \uc2 Heritage appointed Yenor despite a string of controversies over his reactionary politics, including his resignation in April from the \uc2 University of Florida\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s board of regents after protests and concern from state legislators over his views about women.\par \par \uc2 Heidi Beirich, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://globalextremism.org/heidi-beirich-ph-d/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chief strategy officer and co-founder}}}\uc2  of the Global Project Against Hate and Extremism, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just disgraceful that Heritage, especially given all of its recent scandals over providing cover for antisemitism, would hire Yenor, who has long bashed women and has been investigated by his former employer for civil rights violations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is just another example of Heritage\u8217\'20\'19s dismissive views of women and the organization\u8217\'20\'19s radicalization over the past few years, which includes pushing Project 2025, an authoritarian plan that Trump is now implementing that is devastating the rights of multiple communities, including women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The appointment also came in the face of Heritage\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to stave off criticisms about its president\u8217\'20\'19s apparent defense of a Tucker Carlson interview with the antisemitic Holocaust denier and white nationalist Nicholas Fuentes. In November, Heritage president Kevin Roberts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/nov/06/heritage-foundation-tucker-carlson-nick-fuentes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apologized}}}\uc2  after initially backing Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s interview with Fuentes.\par \par \uc2 In an email to the Guardian, Yenor wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CDegenerates such as yourself who celebrated the assassination Charlie Kirk deserve nothing but scorn, let alone explanations of complex ideas.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was not immediately clear which celebration Yenor was referring to.\par \par \uc2 Heritage director of media and public relations Cody Sargent forwarded a statement from Heritage vice-president of domestic policy \uc2 Roger Severino\uc2 , which read: \u8220\'20\'1CHeritage does not, and does not believe employers should, discriminate on the basis of sex in matters of employment and remuneration. We advocate for the American family in law, policy, and culture.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also pointed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/genevievewood/status/1996310285007638532"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an X post}}}\uc2  from Heritage vice-president of development Genevieve Wood responding to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/2025/12/heritage-foundation-women-voting/685112/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 commentary on Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s appointment in the Atlantic}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Wood\u8217\'20\'19s post \u8211\'20\'13 published two days prior to the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s detailed request to Heritage, and which did not address this reporting \u8211\'20\'13 read: \u8220\'20\'1CAs an employee of @Heritage for almost 20 years, the entire premise of this piece is invalid and disingenuous \u8230\'20\'26 which is apparently why it\u8217\'20\'19s in The Atlantic.\par \par \uc2 Wood added: \u8220\'20\'1CHeritage is fortunate to have amazingly talented teammates, where scholars and staff at all levels (and both sexes) are free to discuss and debate ideas on a wide range of topics without it being cast as a \u8216\'20\'18Heritage policy.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Finally, Sargent wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CTo your questions, you\u8217\'20\'19re welcome to reuse this statement, attributable on background to a Heritage spokesperson: \u8216\'20\'18The Guardian is a leftist gossip rag. Its dishonesty is matched only by its uselessness. We don\u8217\'20\'19t waste time answering its half-baked questions.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The statement matched one provided in response to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/nov/28/project-2025-heritage-foundation-hack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 separate recent reporting}}}\uc2  on \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 . \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  made no undertaking to accept Sargent\u8217\'20\'19s comments on background.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Sodomy would be illegal \u8230\'20\'26 you could make adultery illegal; you can make fornication illegal\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 In recent months, Yenor has made public speeches and podcast appearances spelling out a radical vision for instituting authoritarian patriarchal control in the US.\par \par \uc2 Yenor was a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.solochristo.org/traddad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 featured speaker}}}\uc2  at the \u8220\'20\'1CTrad Dad\u8221\'20\'1D conference held by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.solochristo.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Westminster Presbyterian church}}}\uc2  in Battle Ground, Washington. The conference was held in October 2024, according to the church\u8217\'20\'19s website, but a video of Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s talk, which was entitled Population Decline at the Micro Level, was posted to \uc2 YouTube\uc2  in June.\par \par \uc2 In the talk, Yenor rhetorically asked, \u8220\'20\'1CWhat would be the optimal conditions for family formation and people having kids?\u8221\'20\'1D and answered: \u8220\'20\'1CFirst of all, a healthy sexual constitution that reinforces monogamous, procreative marriage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In turn, he said, this would require \u8220\'20\'1Ca set of laws and manners that reinforce having kids and penalize people for not having kids\u8221\'20\'1D, such that \u8220\'20\'1Cdivorce would be difficult to get or proscribed. Sodomy would be illegal, right?\u8221\'20\'1D He added: \u8220\'20\'1CYou could make adultery illegal; you can make fornication illegal. These all reinforce marriage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yenor went on to say that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe gays \u8230\'20\'26 the feminist ideology \u8230\'20\'26 the transgender ideologies, all of these ideologies\u8221\'20\'1D all \u8220\'20\'1Ccompromise family formation\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthese ideologies can grow only if reality is a little sick. So, I consider feminism to be kind of an ideology of decadence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Towards the end of his address, Yenor offered what he called \u8220\'20\'1Cdifficult\u8221\'20\'1D advice, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthe crucial thing you need to be attached to\u8221\'20\'1D is \u8220\'20\'1Ca fertility cult\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that the only thing that \u8220\'20\'1Creally acts as a prophylactic against the regime, is a fertility cult\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As examples of fertility cults, Yenor cited \u8220\'20\'1CHaredi Jews and the Amish\u8221\'20\'1D who \u8220\'20\'1Creject hook, line, and sinker, the modern world\u8221\'20\'1D, and asked his listeners: \u8220\'20\'1CHow can you simulate those cults locally, where your families are, where it\u8217\'20\'19s not weird to have four kids?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Citing things that work against the \u8220\'20\'1Csocial reinforcement\u8221\'20\'1D of fertility that \u8220\'20\'1Cfertility cults\u8221\'20\'1D provide, Yenor said the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost pernicious of these things\u8221\'20\'1D are \u8220\'20\'1Cyoung women who want to be known for their minds\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m glad that you have a good mind, but if that\u8217\'20\'19s what you want to be known for, like, you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have kids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yenor also suggested \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical measures\u8221\'20\'1D to further the goal of fertility, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI would like to end the sex discrimination regime. Sex discrimination would no longer be a civil matter. Businesses wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have to worry about it, schools wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have to worry about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yenor asked: \u8220\'20\'1CIs it illegal to say that men and women should have different destinies, or at least somewhat different destinies? That will get you in trouble in the workplace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yenor said: \u8220\'20\'1CBasically, the Civil Rights Act, I think, institutionalizes the \u8216\'20\'18battle of the sexes\u8217\'20\'19 and puts the law on the side of feminist indoctrination.\u8221\'20\'1D And: \u8220\'20\'1CSo the only way to kind of end that corrosive ideological commitment of our regime is to scale back how the Civil Rights Act applies to businesses, schools, and every other institution in the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In June, Yenor appeared on the podcast of the so far pseudonymous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theblaze.com/u/auronmacintyre"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blaze Media presenter and columnist}}}\uc2  Auron MacIntyre in an episode entitled Have We Hit Peak Pride?, where the pair celebrated perceived defeats of the LGBTQ+ rights movement.\par \par \uc2 In the podcast, Yenor expressed homophobic beliefs and sought to draw a direct link between homosexuality and pedophilia. MacIntyre and Yenor traded perspectives on gay rights and the purported links between homosexuality and pedophilia.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  contacted Macintyre via the email address publicly listed for him on the Blaze\u8217\'20\'19s website, but the email bounced back undelivered. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  then sent a request for comment for MacIntyre via the Blaze\u8217\'20\'19s press contact form.\par \par \uc2 In the podcast, Macintyre said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you let many of these activists talk long enough, even if they\u8217\'20\'19re very high in message discipline, they\u8217\'20\'19re eventually going to admit that pederasty is a pretty big part of male homosexuality and always has been, and that that\u8217\'20\'19s actually what generates the relationship.\u8221\'20\'1D He added: \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the attempts for message discipline, there\u8217\'20\'19s always this push to kind of lower the age of consent or remove laws between men and boys.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yenor replied: \u8220\'20\'1CThe first wave of gay rights was open and honest about what gay rights would mean. And even to the point where they established a group called NAMBLA, the North American Man/Boy Love Association.\u8221\'20\'1D He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThey were out in the open about what they were going to try to accomplish.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yenor talked extensively about strategies for rolling back gay rights and turning public opinion against LGBTQ+ people.\par \par \uc2 At one point, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere are always problems with the gay lifestyle. They always have psychological problems and physical problems.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also strategized about rolling back same-sex marriage rights, expressing a hope that \u8220\'20\'1Cnecessity will be the mother of invention here\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Yenor pointed to the Dobbs decision\u8217\'20\'19s reversal of abortion rights as an example of overturning \u8220\'20\'1Cthings that seem to be untouchable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On that score, Yenor said: \u8220\'20\'1CI think same-sex marriage is a lesser issue than no-fault divorce.\u8221\'20\'1D And: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very difficult to imagine growing any kind of sustainable marriage culture when you have no-fault divorce, at-will divorce as the basic law of the land.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s impossible to see a victory for a pro-family culture that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t, on some level, revisit that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s history\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  previously reported on Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/19/far-right-fraternal-order-sacr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 central role}}}\uc2  in founding the Society for American Civic Renewal (SACR), a role that was revealed in emails obtained by public record request from his employer, \uc2 Boise State University\uc2  (\uc2 BSU\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 In an email, \uc2 BSU\uc2  confirmed that Yenor is still a tenured professor of political science at the college.\par \par \uc2 The documents included Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s drafts of internal SACR materials in early 2021 that outlined vetting questions for prospective members, instructing members to \u8220\'20\'1Cgauge alignment and fit\u8221\'20\'1D of prospects with questions such as: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat are your thoughts on Christian nationalism?\u8221\'20\'1D; \u8220\'20\'1CComment on the Trump presidency and what it entails for the future\u8221\'20\'1D; and: \u8220\'20\'1CDescribe the dynamic of your household in terms of your role and that of your wife.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The organization\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cinternal\u8221\'20\'1D mission statement prioritized recruiting men who \u8220\'20\'1Cunderstand the nature of authority and its legitimate forceful exercise\u8221\'20\'1D and aimed to \u8220\'20\'1Ccollect, curate, and document a list of potential appointees and hires for a renewed American regime\u8221\'20\'1D. The document made no mention of the US constitution or electoral participation.\par \par \uc2 SACR prayer documents drafted by Yenor drew parallels to biblical conquest narratives, such as Joshua\u8217\'20\'19s forces vanquishing Jericho.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/22/charles-haywood-claremont-institute-sacr-far-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also reported}}}\uc2  on would-be \u8220\'20\'1Cwarlord\u8221\'20\'1D Charles Haywood in establishing the SACR. That reporting revealed that Haywood is a former soap manufacturer who has repeatedly expressed a desire to serve as a \u8220\'20\'1Cwarlord\u8221\'20\'1D at the head of an \u8220\'20\'1Carmed patronage network\u8221\'20\'1D, which he has mused might find itself in conflict with the federal government. Haywood has also expressed a desire to recruit \u8220\'20\'1Cshooters\u8221\'20\'1D to help defend the \u8220\'20\'1Cextended, quite sizeable, compound\u8221\'20\'1D he occupies in Carmel, Indiana, and has funded the SACR through his Howdy Doody Good Times foundation to the tune of at least $50,000.\par \par \uc2 Email records also revealed Yenor in October 2020 coordinating with SACR administrator Skyler Kressin to buy Super-Afrikaners, a 1978 book about the Afrikaner Broederbond. The AB was a secretive, men-only, and self-described Christian nationalist network that promoted white Afrikaner interests and helped bring South Africa\u8217\'20\'19s apartheid architects to power. When Kressin sent Yenor an Amazon listing for the book, Yenor replied within half an hour: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Beirich, the extremism expert, wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact that he is a key player in the Society for Christian Renewal, a secretive men\u8217\'20\'19s only Christian nationalist organization, should have also given Heritage pause.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/29/boise-state-university-professor-scott-yenor-action-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Separately}}}\uc2 , the Guardian previously revealed Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s hitherto hidden role in Action Idaho, a media platform he funded with the help of wealthy donors such as Claremont Institute board chair Thomas Klingenstein, and which was, as the Guardian then reported, involved in an \u8220\'20\'1Cattempt to mainstream extremism in Idaho politics\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Western States Center director of programs Lindsay Schubiner.\par \par \uc2 Emails showed Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to hire the conservative writer Pedro Gonzalez \u8211\'20\'13 who was himself {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://web.archive.org/web/20250831032910/https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/desantis-influencers-defend-unmasked-antisemite-pedro-gonzalez-1234780062/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subsequently embroiled}}}\uc2  in controversy over antisemitic remarks in a private group chat \u8211\'20\'13 as executive director with instructions to \u8220\'20\'1Cestablish the reputation of Action Idaho as a Christian nationalist, populist authority\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In 2023 on X, Gonzalez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commentary.org/abe-greenwald/the-dumb-season-of-our-lives/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  posted that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://web.archive.org/web/20250831032910/https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/desantis-influencers-defend-unmasked-antisemite-pedro-gonzalez-1234780062/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 messages}}}\uc2 , written in 2019 and 2020, were from a \u8220\'20\'1Cdifferent, dumb season in my life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The platform published inflammatory content attacking LGBTQ+ communities and Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s own employer, \uc2 Boise State University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In 2023, Yenor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://idahocapitalsun.com/2023/02/09/boise-state-professor-scott-yenor-takes-a-florida-based-job-with-a-conservative-think-tank/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took up a job}}}\uc2  with the Claremont Institute. He has repeatedly encountered controversy due to his strident anti-feminism.\par \par \uc2 In 2021, when he was employed full-time at Boise State, Yenor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.idahopress.com/news/local/boise-state-professors-anti-feminism-comments-draw-scrutiny/article_85906c25-eba4-5889-a10e-8bb0adf329e6.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced backlash}}}\uc2  over a speech he gave to the National Conservatism Conference (\u8220\'20\'1Cone of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theconversation.com/how-not-to-counter-the-radical-right-228640"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 main meeting grounds}}}\uc2  for the global radical right\u8221\'20\'1D) in which he described \u8220\'20\'1Cindependent women\u8221\'20\'1D working \u8220\'20\'1Cin mid-level bureaucratic jobs like human resource management, environmental protection, and marketing\u8221\'20\'1D as \u8220\'20\'1Cmore medicated, meddlesome, and quarrelsome than women need to be\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In 2023, students at Boise\u8217\'20\'19s Eagle high school \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/local/education/article271744342.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jeered and walked out on}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D a Yenor speech after he was invited to campus by a conservative student club.\par \par \uc2 Those remarks, along with other public commentary in which he highlighted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/scottyenor/status/1879520958027071716"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the high proportion}}}\uc2  of women, Black people and Jewish people in the Democratic senate delegation, came back to haunt Yenor and Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/university-west-florida-board-appointment-desantis-yenor-5cc75bb96871f30f441731c5a725ec6e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier this year}}}\uc2 , after the governor appointed the professor to the board of the \uc2 University of West Florida\uc2  in Pensacola.\par \par \uc2 Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s comments about the makeup of the Senate earned a rebuke from fellow rightwing bomb-thrower, then Florida state senator and now congressman \uc2 Randy Fine\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wusf.org/politics-issues/2025-02-22/desantis-100-percent-behind-uwf-trustee-criticized-randy-fine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called him}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cbigot\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cmisogynist\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/conservatism-higher-ed-ft-scott-yenor/id1677193347?i=1000715709414"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 4 July appearance}}}\uc2  on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://americanreformer.org/2023/10/christian-nationalism-a-primer-for-the-layman/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Christian nationalist}}}\uc2  American Reformer podcast, Yenor addressed criticisms made of him during that time: \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t ever publicly respond to any of the charges that were made against me. This was a little bit, you know, difficult for me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1COne of them, one of the charges that came out was that Yenor may perhaps be an antisemite, because I had said that it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t look to me like the Democrats would elect a Jew as a leader of their national party given their support for \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yenor continued: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd then one of the Republican senators picked that up, the headline up and said, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, we can\u8217\'20\'19t appoint an antisemite to the board of trustees\u8217\'20\'19. And I guess I agree. But, you know, I didn\u8217\'20\'19t like the application in my particular case.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 By April, Yenor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://web.archive.org/web/20250411083240/https://www.insidehighered.com/news/quick-takes/2025/04/11/embattled-university-west-florida-trustee-resigns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had resigned}}}\uc2  from the board after Fine and other state senators in Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated house appeared poised to break with the governor and tank Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation.\par \par \uc2 Rightwing ructions\par \par \uc2 Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s appointment has caused ructions on the right, with many conservatives objecting specifically to his views on women.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/2025/12/heritage-foundation-women-voting/685112/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In the Atlantic}}}\uc2 , conservative writer and podcaster Henry Olsen detailed Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s apparent belief that the success of feminists over more than a century in gaining independent legal recognition for women have had an unacceptable \u8220\'20\'1Cwearing-down effect on the traditional family\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Olsen wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CFor the foundation to allow Yenor to make these arguments now that he\u8217\'20\'19s on its payroll is still a choice, a declaration that it considers them to be reasonable. That\u8217\'20\'19s political poison.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CHeritage and Yenor face a choice. Do they stand within the conservative consensus, seeking to extend its principles into the public consciousness and enact them into law? Or do they stand outside the Trumpian coalition because that coalition\u8217\'20\'19s premises are inadequate to meet our challenges?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On X, a range of far-right activists came to Yenor\u8217\'20\'19s defense, including Christoper Rufo, who posted: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is nothing \u8216\'20\'18conservative\u8217\'20\'19 about using a left-wing magazine to smear Scott Yenor for not upholding the principles of human-resources feminism.\u8221\'20\'1D He also said: \u8220\'20\'1CScott\u8217\'20\'19s idea that private companies should be able to prioritize hiring married men with families is completely within the bounds of reasonable debate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251215elcf003v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
