\par\par \uc2 Games\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Our industry has been strip-mined\u8217\'20\'19: video game workers protest at The Game Awards\b0\par\par\uc2 Alyssa Mercante \par \uc2 668 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 December 2025\par 10:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Outside the lavish event, workers called out the \u8216\'20\'18greed\u8217\'20\'19 in the industry that has left games \u8216\'20\'18being sold for parts to make a few people a lot of money\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the night of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/games/2025/dec/12/star-wars-tomb-raider-clair-obscur-expedition-33-game-awards"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 2025 Game Awards}}}\uc2 , a major industry event where the best games of the year are crowned and major publishers reveal forthcoming projects. In the shadow of the Peacock theater in Los Angeles and next to a giant, demonic statue promoting new game Divinity, which would be announced on stage later that evening, stands a collection of people in bright red shirts. Many are holding signs: a tombstone honouring the \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath\u8221\'20\'1D of The Game Awards\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/games/2025/nov/11/future-class-gamings-oscars-game-awards"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Future Class talent development programme}}}\uc2 ; a bold, black-and-red graphic that reads \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re Done Playing\u8221\'20\'1D; and \u8220\'20\'1Cwanted\u8221\'20\'1D posters for \uc2 Take-Two Interactive\uc2  CEO \uc2 Strauss Zelnick\uc2  and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  CEO \uc2 Phil Spencer\uc2 . This is a protest.\par \par \uc2 The protesters, who were almost denied entry to the public space outside the Peacock theater (\u8220\'20\'1Cthey knew we were coming,\u8221\'20\'1D one jokes), are from United Videogame Workers (UVW), an industry-wide, direct-join union for North America that is part of the \uc2 Communications Workers of America\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe are out here today to raise awareness of the plight of the game worker,\u8221\'20\'1D says Anna C Webster, chair of the freelancing committee, in the hot Los Angeles sun. \u8220\'20\'1COur industry has been strip-mined for resources by these corporate overlords, and we figured the best place to raise awareness of what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in the games industry is at the culmination, the final boss, as it were: The Game Awards.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Webster is referencing several things here. More than 40,000 layoffs have decimated the industry over the past few years; just last month, Grand Theft Auto developer RockstarGames was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/games/2025/nov/07/uk-union-accuses-gta-maker-rockstar-games-of-firing-employees-attempting-to-organise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused of union-busting}}}\uc2  after firing more than 30 staff (the studio {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ign.com/articles/gta-6-developer-rockstar-claims-fired-employees-were-dismissed-for-leaking-specific-game-features-from-upcoming-and-unannounced-titles-not-because-they-were-trying-to-unionize"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denies this}}}\uc2 , saying the employees were leaking confidential information), and AI is being rapidly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/games/2025/dec/10/i-bought-the-games-studio-behind-zombies-run-because-humanity-is-essential-to-storytelling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 injected into game development processes}}}\uc2 . The industry seems unwilling to reckon with these issues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI recently read that a three-minute trailer at The Game Awards {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kotaku.com/game-awards-geoff-keighley-tickets-trailers-clair-obscur-2000652243"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 costs more than $1m,}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D says the union\u8217\'20\'19s local secretary, Kaitlin \u8220\'20\'1CKB\u8221\'20\'1D Bonfiglio. \u8220\'20\'1C[Despite] the pomp and circumstance of all of this, they never seem to acknowledge the historic amount of layoffs that have happened in the industry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For the UVW, there is a core issue here. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s all about greed,\u8221\'20\'1D Webster insists. \u8220\'20\'1CAnyone who works in the games industry can identify that our art form is being sold for parts to make a few people a lot of money. And they don\u8217\'20\'19t care about the games. They don\u8217\'20\'19t care about the art. They just want their money.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For those working in games, the problems plaguing the industry are obvious. But how can UVW make it clear that the issues industry workers face affect players, too? \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re someone who loves video games, if you are frustrated by games that launch buggy and are delayed messes, if you\u8217\'20\'19re frustrated by games you\u8217\'20\'19re excited about getting cancelled without warning, all of that ties back to what we\u8217\'20\'19re doing here,\u8221\'20\'1D treasurer Sherveen Uduwana says. \u8220\'20\'1CGiving us layoff protections, making sure bosses can\u8217\'20\'19t take away our healthcare, making sure they can\u8217\'20\'19t replace us with AI \u8211\'20\'13 that is going to lead to better games for players and more ambitious, interesting, creative projects. It\u8217\'20\'19s really a win-win for players and a win-win for workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a clear love for the industry permeating through this group, a desire to make the medium and the work they cherish even better. The Game Awards is a major night, one that can help prop up smaller independent studios and highlight incredible voice actors. The UVW team recognises that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHave a good time today, and tomorrow, let\u8217\'20\'19s wake up and start organising for better workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights and a better games industry,\u8221\'20\'1D Uduwana says.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251215elcf002e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
