\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The UK needs some media free of US control\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 Comcast\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s move for \uc2 ITV\uc2  starts to focus minds\b0\par\par\uc2 Mark Sweney \par \uc2 1,384 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 December 2025\par 19:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 31\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 With public service broadcasters starting to look like \u8216\'20\'18endangered species\u8217\'20\'19, many want Channel 4 and BBC to work more closely\par \par \uc2 The prospect of \uc2 Comcast\uc2  taking over \uc2 ITV\uc2  has prompted concerns about the impact on British public service broadcasting, a fact that Channel 4\u8217\'20\'19s new chief executive, moving from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2025/dec/10/channel-4-poaches-new-chief-executive-priya-dogra-from-sky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a senior post at Sky}}}\uc2 , will be all too well aware.\par \par \uc2 Sky\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s advertising chief, Priya Dogra, will now be expected to lead the charge to block her former employer\u8217\'20\'19s takeover plan to protect Channel 4.\par \par \uc2 The proposed combination of \uc2 Sky\uc2  and \uc2 ITV\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s broadcasting operation would leave Channel 4 a relative commercial minnow when it comes to TV and digital ad sales, reigniting talk of the need to revisit{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/article/2024/aug/30/more-cuts-and-a-merger-with-channel-4-the-bbc-contemplates-its-radical-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  some form of tie-up with the BBC }}}\uc2 for long-term survival.\par \par \uc2 However, it is the potential ramifications on the future of news provision that are causing the most immediate alarm for many in the TV industry.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/nov/06/sky-owner-comcast-in-talks-to-buy-itvs-broadcasting-arm-for-2bn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surprise news last month}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Comcast\uc2 , which owns assets including Universal Studios and bought {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2006/nov/17/bskyb.itv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\u8217\'20\'19s Sky for \u163\'00\'A330bn in 2018}}}\uc2 , is in talks to buy \uc2 ITV\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s broadcasting business makes commercial sense.\par \par \uc2 Traditional broadcasters are facing a long-term existential threat as audiences and revenues continue to rapidly migrate to global digital players such as \uc2 Meta\uc2 , \uc2 Google\uc2 , \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and \uc2 Netflix\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, the potential \u163\'00\'A31.6bn takeover of \uc2 ITV\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s broadcasting arm and streaming service, which would end 70 years of independence, is laden with regulatory, political and competition concerns.\par \par \uc2 At a stroke \uc2 Comcast\uc2  would control Sky News and ITV News (including its sprawling regional news operation) and become the largest shareholder in ITN, which produces news for \uc2 ITV\uc2 , Channel 4 and Channel 5.\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Comcast\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 40% of ITN would not be a controlling stake \u8211\'20\'13 the owner of the Daily Mail, Thomson Reuters and Informa each hold 20% \u8211\'20\'13 it would still be heavily involved in the news output of most of the main broadcasters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf a deal materialises the fate of ITN is an interesting one that will focus minds politically,\u8221\'20\'1D says one senior TV executive. \u8220\'20\'1CEffectively they will be involved in the news output of all the biggest non-BBC channels other than \uc2 GB News\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Comcast\uc2  guaranteed to keep funding Sky News for a decade, increasing its funding annually in line with inflation, as part of its takeover of \uc2 Sky\uc2  in 2018. As that commitment draws closer to expiring, concerns have been raised about whether the US company will continue to fully fund Sky News, which has an annual budget of \u163\'00\'A3100m but is thought to make losses of as much as \u163\'00\'A380m.\par \par \uc2 Dana Strong\uc2 , the chief executive of \uc2 Sky\uc2 , recently told staff that the broadcaster would continue to back the news operation regardless of any ongoing support by \uc2 Comcast\uc2 , which has cut jobs at NBC News in the US.\par \par \uc2 It is understood that if any deal to buy \uc2 ITV\uc2  is tabled it would include guarantees not to seek permission from the media regulator \uc2 Ofcom\uc2  to vary any of the conditions of its public service broadcast licence, which includes commitments to national and regional news.\par \par \uc2 Last year, \uc2 ITV\uc2  accepted the terms of a new licence which will remain in place until 2034. In May, it also agreed a new five-year news output deal with ITN, which observers point out effectively operates as a guarantee that the status quo will be maintained in the event of a takeover.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are definitely questions about plurality,\u8221\'20\'1D says Stewart Puvis, a former ITN chief executive. \u8220\'20\'1CTheoretically \uc2 Comcast\uc2  could, say, merge \uc2 Sky\uc2  and ITV News and use its position as a 40% shareholder in ITN to assert control and offer Channel 4 and Channel 5 continued news supply but on more expensive terms. I would hope \uc2 Comcast\uc2  realise ways of solving these problems [if the \uc2 ITV\uc2  deal happens].\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey did a deal protecting Sky News to get control of Sky, so they have been round this course before, they understand the sensitivities. The main priority is to keep an eye on their intentions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 British TV executives have previously warned of the risk posed to the UK\u8217\'20\'19s system of public service broadcasers (PSBs) by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2014/aug/21/british-tv-industry-risk-us-tech-media-channel-4-david-abraham"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 large parts of the British television industry being snapped up}}}\uc2  by US corporations.\par \par \uc2 In July, \uc2 Ofcom\uc2  published a report warning that public service television, such as news provision and prestige UK-focused content such as \uc2 ITV\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Mr Bates vs the Post Office, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2025/jul/21/uk-public-service-tv-youtube-ofcom-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 risks becoming an \u8220\'20\'1Cendangered species\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  as viewers migrate to US online platforms and streamers.\par \par \uc2 The watchdog also published data showing that \uc2 YouTube\uc2  had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c4gzvee78eqo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overtaken ITV to become the UK\u8217\'20\'19s second most-watched media service}}}\uc2 , behind only the BBC, with it and \uc2 Netflix\uc2  now the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jul/30/youtube-tv-destination-children-ofcom-survey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two most popular first TV destinations among four- to 15-year-olds.}}}\par \par \uc2 There are those that believe that a Sky takeover of \uc2 ITV\uc2 , against a backdrop of the rise of the viewer shift to mostly US digital companies, heralds the need for closer collaboration between the UK\u8217\'20\'19s biggest broadcasters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe UK wants and needs its own part of mass media which isn\u8217\'20\'19t US controlled,\u8221\'20\'1D says a second broadcasting executive. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a national strategic imperative.I think the government need to work out how the boards of the PSBs have a new part to their remits that obligates them to collaborate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn terms of an \uc2 ITV\uc2  takeover it is less of an issue given \uc2 Sky\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s history in the UK, on balance I think it would help the PSBs as it strengthens \uc2 ITV\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s more to do with how the rest of the PSB system would need to readjust.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Given that advertisers follow eyeballs, a combination of \uc2 Sky\uc2  and \uc2 ITV\uc2  could create a British TV and streaming powerhouse, with the two companies\u8217\'20\'19 sales houses controlling 73% of the total ad spend on traditional TV and broadcasters\u8217\'20\'19 streaming services combined.\par \par \uc2 Any deal will trigger an investigation by the UK competition watchdog, which historically would not have allowed the combination, as \uc2 James Murdoch\uc2  found out after making an audacious move to become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2006/nov/17/bskyb.itv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the biggest shareholder in ITV in 2006.}}}\par \par \uc2 However, \uc2 Sky\uc2  is hoping that the regulator will widen the scope of its definition of the ad market to include the impact of giants such as \uc2 YouTube\uc2 , \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The government has also been pushing regulators to be more \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-business\u8221\'20\'1D, with former Amazon UK chief Doug Gurr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jan/22/doug-gurr-amazon-uk-ex-boss-appointment-competition-and-markets-authority-cma"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 installed at the Competition and Markets Authority (CMA).}}}\par \par \uc2 For clearance to be given \uc2 Sky\uc2  is likely to, at the least, look to shed its third-party ad sales deals. It handles the contracts for media owners including Channel 5 and \uc2 Warner Bros Discovery\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 now facing its own takeover battle between rival {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/dec/05/netflix-frontrunner-warner-bros-discovery-streaming-and-studio-sale"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bids from Netflix}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/dec/08/paramount-skydance-warner-bros-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Paramount Skydance}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to reduce its dominance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it will get cleared,\u8221\'20\'1D says \uc2 Alex DeGroote\uc2 , a media analyst. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Comcast\uc2  will do everything it can to say it will maintain the PSB status quo and obligations, to give the impression it will be a good owner. But you don\u8217\'20\'19t buy to ultimately keep everything the same.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CITV plus \uc2 Sky\uc2  will give them 70% of the [traditional] TV ad market, close to a monopoly. The thrust of the debate will be the CMA being encouraged not to put insurmountable obstacles in place.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Channel 4 has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2017/mar/28/channel-4-will-not-be-sold-off-but-could-be-moved-out-of-london"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seen off multiple attempts at privatisation}}}\uc2  by Conservative governments that argued it would not be able to compete against digital companies such as \uc2 Netflix\uc2  and \uc2 YouTube\uc2  without outside investment.\par \par \uc2 Now, given the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2025/nov/13/bbc-apologises-to-donald-trump-over-edit-of-speech-for-panorama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weakened state of the BBC}}}\uc2  and the commercial threat to Channel 4, which relies on advertising for the vast majority of its income, there are those that believe sporadic talk over the past 15 years on the need for closer collaboration between the two is likely to become a necessity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe may at some point end up in that situation because of the deep cumulative cuts since 2010 in the BBC\u8217\'20\'19s real-terms funding and because Channel 4, too, has a structural funding problem, which is not its fault,\u8221\'20\'1D says Patrick Barwise, emeritus professor of management and marketing at \uc2 London Business School\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChannel 4 has repeatedly beaten the predictions, but that is just postponing the problem. It\u8217\'20\'19s now beginning to run out of road.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251214elce000rt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
