\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A very hostile climate for workers\u8217\'20\'19: US labor movement struggles under Trump\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 2,090 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 December 2025\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 , the federal watchdog for workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights, has been rendered toothless as employees grapple with corporations\par \par \uc2 On a cold January day in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, workers at a \uc2 Whole Foods Market\uc2  store in the heart of the city made history. Organizers won a vote to form a union for the very first time in one of the grocery chain\u8217\'20\'19s 530 US stores.\par \par \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  is owned by \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , which has spent years quashing unionization efforts within its sprawling empire. This result amounted to another blow in the tech giant\u8217\'20\'19s armor.\par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  had shown in the preceding years how \u8211\'20\'13 in the face of heavy resistance from a determined multinational employer \u8211\'20\'13 one such victory could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/02/starbucks-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set the stage for hundreds more}}}\uc2 . A new wave of momentum had taken hold in the US labor movement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are excited to begin the next chapter of this journey,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ufcw.org/press-releases/whole-foods-union-victory/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  the Workers of Whole Foods Center City Philadelphia. Once they had turned the page, however, the chapter proved slow and arduous.\par \par \uc2 Just one week before the \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  union ballot result came through, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returned to the White House. On his watch a crucial federal agency overseeing the US labor force has been \u8220\'20\'1Ccrippled\u8221\'20\'1D, according to insiders \u8211\'20\'13 and the new wave of momentum waned.\par \par \uc2 Excitement gave way to frustration in Philadelphia. \u8220\'20\'1CDue to the fact that the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t functioning \u8230\'20\'26 we\u8217\'20\'19re just waiting around,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ed Dupree, who works at the Whole Foods Center City store.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ), the top US labor watchdog, is tasked with protecting workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights, overseeing the labor movement and ruling on disputes between employers and unions.\par \par \uc2 Its five-seat board, which hears disputes and oversees union elections, requires at least three members to issue a ruling. But days after regaining power, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/28/gwynne-wilcox-trump-labor-board"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired Gwynne Wilcox}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 an unprecedented decision \u8211\'20\'13 from the board, leaving it without this crucial quorum to make decisions.\par \par \uc2 Across the labor movement, many workers, in Philadelphia and far beyond, have been enshrouded in uncertainty ever since.\par \par \uc2 Rather than recognize the result of the vote, \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  objected, triggering a long process of delays and legal challenges. While a regional \uc2 NLRB\uc2  director {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/04-RC-355267"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sided with}}}\uc2  the union, ruling against \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 objections, a spokesperson for the chain told the Guardian it \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly\u8221\'20\'1D disagrees with the regional director\u8217\'20\'19s decision, and claimed \uc2 UFCW\uc2  1776, the union behind the unionization drive, \u8220\'20\'1Cillegally interfered\u8221\'20\'1D with the vote.\par \par \uc2 It continued to appeal, taking the case all the way to the top of the paralyzed \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , where it\u8217\'20\'19s sat ever since \u8211\'20\'13 in limbo. In 2024, the board issued around 150 decisions on labor disputes. Over the past 11 months under Trump, it has issued six.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Trump administration thus far seems to have been treating the agency with this kind of combination of hostility and aggressive neglect,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Lauren McFerran\uc2 , who served as chair of the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an administration that professes to be very pro-worker in its orientation, but we haven\u8217\'20\'19t had a functional agency to resolve labor disputes and to protect workers rights \u8230\'20\'26 in a year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In an interview, the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s acting general counsel denied the agency has been neglected \u8211\'20\'13 and compared its decision to scrap certain policies amid budget constraints with a family, spending carefully. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t always go to Disney World,\u8221\'20\'1D said William Cowen.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Four current rank-and-file workers spoke to the Guardian. Each requested anonymity, fearing retaliation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 NLRB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s employees just want to do our jobs and be treated with respect,\u8221\'20\'1D said one official. \u8220\'20\'1CBut from day one, this administration has crippled the agency, and treated us as enemies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Staff can see \u8220\'20\'1Cfirsthand the damage that is being done\u8221\'20\'1D, the staffer continued, claiming they and their colleagues had been left \u8220\'20\'1Cdemoralized and disgusted\u8221\'20\'1D by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\par \par \uc2 The National Labor Relations Act, enacted in 1935 to federally protect workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights to organize and engage in collective bargaining, now exists \u8220\'20\'1Con paper only\u8221\'20\'1D, the official claimed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo far I think we are relieved the agency has not been shut down,\u8221\'20\'1D added a longtime legal staff employee. \u8220\'20\'1CMany employees have left, either through the \u8216\'20\'18{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/28/trump-federal-workers-buyouts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fork in the road}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19; retirement; or going to the private sector.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ogletree.com/insights-resources/blog-posts/president-trump-nominates-two-for-nlrb-potentially-restoring-quorum/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  nominated}}}\uc2  two board members in July: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/policywatch/nominating-scott-mayer-as-a-member-of-the-nlrb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Scott Mayer,}}}\uc2  counsel for \uc2 Boeing\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/policywatch/nominating-james-murphy-as-a-member-of-the-nlrb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 James Murphy,}}}\uc2  a career \uc2 NLRB\uc2  attorney. These appointments, if approved by the Senate, would restore quorum to the agency\u8217\'20\'19s board.\par \par \uc2 But a high-stakes ruling in August by an appeals court in the fifth circuit, which covers Louisiana, Mississippi, and Texas, has increased concern. Weighing into a case that stems from a lawsuit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.laboremploymentlawblog.com/2025/08/articles/labor-and-employment/fifth-circuit-rules-nlrb-structure-likely-unconstitutional/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , the appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.littler.com/news-analysis/asap/fifth-circuit-upholds-injunction-because-nlrb-structure-likely-unconstitutional"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested}}}\uc2  the plaintiffs will likely prevail on their arguments that the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  is unconstitutional \u8211\'20\'13 and maintained court orders blocking the agency from proceeding with enforcement against the affected companies litigate their constitutional challenges against the agency.\par \par \uc2 The decision \u8220\'20\'1Cbasically halted labor law enforcement\u8221\'20\'1D, claimed an \uc2 NLRB\uc2  field attorney. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are an employer and you don\u8217\'20\'19t want to go to an unfair labor practice trial, if you don\u8217\'20\'19t want a union to be certified at your workplace, you basically have the ability to keep that from happening just by pulling certain procedural levers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe put so much work and effort into investigating these cases, and really finding the meritorious ones, and pursuing them vigorously, only to have this outlier rightwing decision, from a court that increasingly is willing to be the rightwing activists in the judiciary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Until, or unless, the decision is reversed, \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s nothing we can do\u8221\'20\'1D, the attorney said. \u8220\'20\'1CI personally have strong, meritorious cases that are just sitting, because they can\u8217\'20\'19t go anywhere.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another attorney at the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  said it has been \u8220\'20\'1Cdifficult to not see anything happen\u8221\'20\'1D with cases that have circulated. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we have been teeing up cases for when there is an eventual quorum, we cannot actively draft anything other than simple orders in cases we think are straightforward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While major cases gather dust, the number hitting in-trays across the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  reached its highest level in over a decade just before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to office.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/about-nlrb/what-we-do/decide-cases#:~:text=When%20complaints%20of%20Unfair%20Labor,of%20recent%20invitations%20is%20here."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 majority}}}\uc2  of such unfair labor practice (ULP) cases are settled by agreement, rather than litigation. Only the most contentious cases, including when a decision by a regional \uc2 NLRB\uc2  director is challenged, are filed to an administrative judge. If this ruling is appealed, it goes to the board.\par \par \uc2 The agency\u8217\'20\'19s workforce, which had already shrunk considerably, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fedscope.opm.gov/ibmcognos/bi/v1/disp?b_action=powerPlayService&m_encoding=UTF-8&BZ=1AAABnsT72MN42oVOsW6DQAz9mTNph0Y_wyVhYIDjUBiANLBXlFzSqsBFcB3y9xUwpFWGvidL9vN7lp2yWJdVcVRpHIzWDDqNn4DocyNI4jZU6PncQ0%7EtfIHRZiO5UKREtAWiZ2fKqvAo94ew2gdASWN6q3sLlJxNe9IDiAg87OtOgxuvDnXzVV%7E0_Ka6a2tune7tCkQMlFyXzV%7E73QWEL0Aov4dhmTLT248p68SlXMsiz5Ws0iLPw0wF%7E_Wc6DU4IzKOiJwjYwyZQEbIJjIWXnTf3IAQ6ASEYdsC_pkZ7eMpQJ8B7YBcBNIc6B3IXwR_F9gMIHey%7EwKfOXfLO3MtTyz4AbZLbJc%3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined}}}\uc2  by around 100 employees under Trump, according to estimates from the staff\u8217\'20\'19s union and the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite employee concerns about capacity, the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2026 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrlawwatch.com/2025/06/17/president-trumps-budget-goes-to-work-against-enforcement-agencies-with-significant-cuts-to-dol-and-nlrb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 budget request }}}\uc2 sought a reduction by $14m to the previous year. In the agency\u8217\'20\'19s budget request, they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tcf.org/content/commentary/why-doesnt-the-trump-nlrb-want-workers-to-know-their-rights/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated}}}\uc2  a strategic goal of the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cimprove public awareness\u8221\'20\'1D of its mission and activities.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 In an interview with the Guardian, William Cowen, acting general counsel of the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , and the agency\u8217\'20\'19s highest-ranking official, disputed claims it has been \u8220\'20\'1Ccrippled\u8221\'20\'1D by the lack of a quorum, and cast the rollback of policies designed to strengthen workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights as a matter of priorities.\par \par \uc2 Cowen, a veteran \uc2 NLRB\uc2  official promoted by Trump after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/28/gwynne-wilcox-trump-labor-board"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 firing of Jennifer Abruzzo}}}\uc2 , who served under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe loss of the quorum did not have a serious impact on what the agency could do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked what he would say to \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  workers who are still waiting for almost a year on the status of their union, Cowen appeared to walk back his remarks. \u8220\'20\'1CI wasn\u8217\'20\'19t saying it was unimportant that the board doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have a quorum, and it is particularly important, especially to those people who have a case that\u8217\'20\'19s waiting for the board\u8217\'20\'19s quorum to decide,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not a good place to be in, because the board has to decide. My only point is that that\u8217\'20\'19s less than 5% of all the cases that come through the front door.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also characterized {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/news-outreach/news-story/gc-25-05-rescission-of-certain-general-counsel-memoranda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rescissions}}}\uc2  of several Biden-era policies \u8211\'20\'13 including steps to improve compensation for workers found to have had their rights violated, and curtail non-compete agreements \u8211\'20\'13 as necessary, given the lack of resources at the agency. Announcing the move in February, Cowen had said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe unfortunate truth is that if we attempt to accomplish everything, we risk accomplishing nothing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn pursuing so many things all simultaneously, we overloaded our system,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a weird historic case intake, and as well as historic staffing lows. It\u8217\'20\'19s so sort of high volume, low capacity. And so the combination of those two things put us into a situation where we had a serious backlog of cases, and it was taking significantly longer than is typical to process cases.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He acknowledged the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  could use more staff, but likened the decisions he has made since taking charge of the agency to that of a family. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a reality \u8230\'20\'26 like any homeowner knows, or family knows \u8230\'20\'26 that you have a certain amount of money, and you can therefore do a certain amount of things, and you can\u8217\'20\'19t always go to Disney World. You know with the resources you have.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot that any of this is Disney World,\u8221\'20\'1D added Cowen. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s our challenge, as the managers of this agency, to be able to maintain operations with the resources we have.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As far as Cowen\u8217\'20\'19s concerned, the fifth circuit intervention \u8211\'20\'13 and the potential impact \u8211\'20\'13 is \u8220\'20\'1Cfar more challenging\u8221\'20\'1D than the lack of quorum. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t have hearings in order to set cases up for the board to hear,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 While Cowen argued the paralysis of the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top court has had no \u8220\'20\'1Cserious impact\u8221\'20\'1D on its ability to function, his direct predecessor is of a different view.\par \par \uc2 Without quorum at the board, Abruzzo warned Congress in June, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe issue is that there\u8217\'20\'19s too many employers out there abusing the processes, and then pushing it to the board by appealing when a union wins an election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The appeal \u8220\'20\'1Cthen gets stuck\u8221\'20\'1D, she noted, \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause there\u8217\'20\'19s no quorum\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Even when quorum is restored with Trump appointees, Ellen Dichner, former chief counsel to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  chair, warned the agency is likely to rescind {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/bidens-nlrb-restoring-rights/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decisions}}}\uc2  issued under Biden , such as a ban on captive audience meetings held by employers to deter unionization.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a very, very hostile climate for workers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dichner. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I think labor is seeing, and will continue to see, is a fundamental attack on workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights, and the rights of workers to organize, and the ability of workers to achieve collective bargaining agreements.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some states have tried to fill in the void as the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  enforcement dwindles under Trump. New York and California passed laws this year \u8211\'20\'13 challenged by the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to grant state labor agencies authority to oversee private sector union elections and ULP charges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe current president is attempting to take a wrecking ball to public and private sector employees\u8217\'20\'19 fundamental right to join a union and collectively bargain for fair wages, benefits and safe working conditions,\u8221\'20\'1D said California assemblymember Tina McKinnor. \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia will not sit idly as its workers are systematically denied the right to organize due to employer intransigence or federal inaction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As Trump officials continue to bulldoze established norms, the supreme court is expected to rule on the constitutionality of the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 ; the firing of Wilcox; and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scotusblog.com/2025/12/trump-v-slaughter-an-explainer/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case}}}\uc2  involving Trump\u8217\'20\'19s firing of former \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  commissioner \uc2 Rebecca Slaughter\uc2  that will determine the independence of federal agencies like the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe potential loss of independence at the agency is a huge pivot point for its operations,\u8221\'20\'1D said McFerran, the former \uc2 NLRB\uc2  chair, who expects the supreme court to \u8220\'20\'1Cscale back or eviscerate\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s independence. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the agency does start operating in a fundamentally more politicized way, I think people will have to find other ways to get their labor disputes resolved, because they\u8217\'20\'19ll lose trust in the board altogether.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House did not respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 With the future of the US labor movement in the balance, workers like those in Philadelphia are waiting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  has more than enough money and profit to be able to share that wealth with the workers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dupree. \u8220\'20\'1CA union is the main way for us to get more of the profit of our labor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251214elce001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
