\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Computer maker \uc2 HP\uc2  to cut up to 6,000 jobs by 2028 as it turns to AI\b0\par\par\uc2 Julia Kollewe \par \uc2 771 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 November 2025\par 15:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US firm says plan to speed up product development and improve customer satisfaction would save $1bn a yearBusiness live \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates\par \par \uc2 Up to 6,000 jobs are to go at \uc2 HP\uc2  worldwide in the next three years as the US computer and printer maker increasingly adopts AI to speed up product development.\par \par \uc2 Announcing a lower-than-expected profit outlook for the coming year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hp.com/us-en/newsroom/press-releases/2025/hp-inc-reports-fiscal-2025-full-year-and-fourth-quarter-results.html#:~:text=Reports%20Fiscal%202025%20Full%20Year%20and%20Fourth%20Quarter%20Results,-November%2025%2C%202025&text=HP%20Inc.%20and%20its%20subsidiaries,from%20the%20prior%2Dyear%20period."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HP said it would cut}}}\uc2  between 4,000 and 6,000 jobs by the end of October 2028. It has about 56,000 employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we look ahead, we see a significant opportunity to embed AI into \uc2 HP\uc2  to accelerate product innovation, improve customer satisfaction and boost productivity,\u8221\'20\'1D said the California company\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive, \uc2 Enrique Lores\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He said teams working on product development, internal operations and customer support would be affected by the job cuts. He added that this would lead to $1bn (\u163\'00\'A3749m) savings a year by 2028, although the cuts would cost an estimated $650m.\par \par \uc2 News of the job cuts came as a leading educational research charity warned that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/nov/25/ai-could-replace-3m-low-skilled-jobs-by-2035-research-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 up to 3m low-skilled jobs could disappear in the UK}}}\uc2  by 2035 because of automation and AI. The jobs most at risk are those in occupations such as trades, machine operations and administrative roles, the National Foundation for Educational Research said.\par \par \uc2 In the US, about 40% of jobs could be replaced by AI, in sectors ranging from education and healthcare to business and legal, according to a report by the \uc2 McKinsey Global Institute\uc2  released this week.\par \par \uc2 AI agents and robots could automate more than half of US work hours using technology that is available today, the US consultancy\u8217\'20\'19s analysis found. It estimated that $2.9tn of economic value could be unlocked in the US by 2030.\par \par \uc2 Most roles at risk are in legal and administrative services, with tasks such as data entry, financial processing and drafting documents likely to be handled by AI systems, although people will still be needed to design, supervise and verify. Dangerous, physical jobs such as machine operation could be replaced by robots.\par \par \uc2 HP\uc2  had already cut between 1,000 and 2,000 staff in February as part of a restructuring plan.\par \par \uc2 It is the latest in a run of companies to cite AI when announcing cuts to workforce numbers. Last week the law firm \uc2 Clifford Chance\uc2  revealed it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/nov/21/increased-ai-use-law-firm-clifford-chance-cuts-london-jobs-10-per-cent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reducing}}}\uc2  business services staff at its London base by 10% \u8211\'20\'13 about 50 roles \u8211\'20\'13 attributing the change partly to the adoption of the new technology.\par \par \uc2 The head of PwC also publicly cut back on plans to hire 100,000 people between 2021 and 2026, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthe world is different\u8221\'20\'1D and AI had changed its hiring needs.\par \par \uc2 Klarna\uc2  said last week that AI-related savings had helped the buy now, pay later company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/nov/18/buy-now-pay-later-klarna-ai-helped-halve-staff-boost-pay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost halve its workforce over the past three years}}}\uc2  through natural attrition, with departing staff replaced by technology rather than by new staff members, hinting at further role reductions to come.\par \par \uc2 Several US technology companies have announced job reductions in recent months as consumer spending cooled amid higher prices and a government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 Executives across industries are hoping to use AI to speed up software development and automate customer service. Cloud providers are buying large supplies of memory to meet computing demand from companies that build advanced AI models, such as \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  and \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , leading to an increase in memory costs.\par \par \uc2 The push by big tech companies to build out AI infrastructure has triggered price increases for dynamic random access memory and NAND semiconductors \u8211\'20\'13 two commonly used types of memory chips \u8211\'20\'13 amid high competition in the server market.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  have said that soaring prices for memory chips, driven by rising demand from datacentres, could push up costs and dent profits at \uc2 HP\uc2  and rivals such as \uc2 Dell\uc2  and \uc2 Acer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMemory costs are currently 15% to 18% of the cost of a typical PC, and while an increase was expected, its rate has accelerated in the last few weeks,\u8221\'20\'1D Lores said.\par \par \uc2 HP\uc2  posted better-than-expected revenues of $14.6bn for its fourth quarter. Demand for AI-enabled PCs continues to increase, and they made up more than 30% of \uc2 HP\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shipments in the fourth quarter to 31 October.\par \par \uc2 However, it forecast between $2.90 and $3.20 in adjusted net earnings per share for the coming year, below analysts\u8217\'20\'19 forecasts of $3.33. It said the outlook reflected added costs from US trade tariffs.\par \par \uc2 HP\uc2  shares fell as much as 6% after announcing the job cuts.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251126elbq00338\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
