\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US added 119,000 jobs in September in report delayed by federal shutdown\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 612 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 November 2025\par 19:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 31\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Unemployment rate hits 4.4%, its highest level since 2021, and government has said no October report will be issued\par \par \uc2 The US jobs market added 119,000 jobs in September, according to the latest monthly jobs report, which was delayed by six weeks due to the shutdown of the federal government.\par \par \uc2 Amid heightened uncertainty surrounding the strength of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2 , the much-anticipated reading was higher than the 51,000 jobs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://groundworkcollaborative.org/news/some-thoughts-on-the-labor-market/#:~:text=As%20Kolko%20convincingly%20shows%2C%20this,breakthrough%20is%20coming%20anytime%20soon."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected}}}\uc2  by analysts to be added in September.\par \par \uc2 The unemployment rate, meanwhile, ticked up from 4.3% to 4.4%: its highest level since 2021. And a previous estimate for jobs growth in August was downgraded \u8211\'20\'13 revealing an unexpected decline in the US workforce.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  (\uc2 BLS\uc2 ) revised down previous readings for July and August, which had already raised fears that growth in the labor market had stalled in recent months.\par \par \uc2 The agency now estimates that the US economy added 72,000 jobs in July, down from 79,000, and shed 4,000 jobs in August, down from growth of 22,000.\par \par \uc2 Trading on Wall Street was volatile. Boosted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/nov/19/nvidia-earning-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strong results from chipmaker Nvidia}}}\uc2 , US markets rose initially. The benchmark S&P 500 was up 1.7% during the morning session in New York, while the technology-focused Nasdaq Composite climbed 2.1%.\par \par \uc2 However, the rally later fizzled as investor jitters resurfaced. By early afternoon the S&P was down 0.7% and the Nasdaq was down 0.9%. \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  was also down 0.9%.\par \par \uc2 September\u8217\'20\'19s jobs report was initially scheduled to be released in October, only to be delayed by the shutdown. ADP\u8217\'20\'19s unofficial private sector jobs report for September {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/jobs/u-s-lost-32-000-jobs-in-september-says-payroll-processor-06528340?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  a loss of 29,000 jobs; its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adp-ri-nrip-static.adp.com/artifacts/us_ner/20251105/ADP_NATIONAL_EMPLOYMENT_REPORT_Press_Release_2025_10%20FINAL.pdf?_ga=2.201770387.360261356.1763064270-1666485656.1763064270"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  for October pointed to an increase of 42,000 jobs.\par \par \uc2 The complete official jobs report for October will not be released, the \uc2 BLS\uc2  said on Wednesday, as a result of the prolonged shutdown, during which data collection and processing was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.friendsofbls.org/updates/2025/11/12/2025-government-shutdown-faqs-on-bls-data"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not conducted}}}\uc2 . Official data on the number of jobs created or lost in October will be released alongside the full report for November, in mid-December, according to the \uc2 BLS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With policymakers at the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  due to convene for their latest interest rate-setting meeting in the coming weeks, Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s data release strengthened expectations that they will probably sit on their hands and keep rates on hold.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Vanden Houten\uc2 , lead economist at \uc2 Oxford Economics\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe September jobs report may be backward looking but offers reassurance that the labor market wasn\u8217\'20\'19t crumbling before the government shutdown. There is nothing in the data to warrant a change to our forecast for the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to leave rates unchanged at the December meeting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sagging job numbers incited Donald Trump to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/09/us-created-fewer-jobs-march-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fire}}}\uc2  the \uc2 BLS\uc2  commissioner Erika McEntarfer in August, following a weak July jobs report, as Trump made baseless claims the numbers were \u8220\'20\'1Crigged\u8221\'20\'1D to make him and Republicans look bad.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Elizabeth Warren, the Massachusetts Democratic senator, said: \u8220\'20\'1CAfter sitting on it for weeks, Donald Trump finally released the September jobs report showing the unemployment rate is up. Businesses have announced a record number of layoffs, and hiring has slowed since Trump took office. It\u8217\'20\'19s not surprising that he\u8217\'20\'19s now refusing to release the October jobs report, despite the administration\u8217\'20\'19s legal obligation to publish employment data each month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump says he wants lower interest rates, but is withholding the very data the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  needs to make that decision next month. And it\u8217\'20\'19ll be working families who will pay the price.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251120elbk00439\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
