\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18No contract, no coffee\u8217\'20\'19: what to know about the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers\u8217\'20\'19 strike in 65 US cities\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,188 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 November 2025\par 18:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 2,000 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  employees are on the picket line as politicians like Zohran Mamdani back striking workers\par \par \uc2 Unionized Starbucks workers are threatening to expand a US strike against the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest coffee chain into \u8220\'20\'1Cthe largest and longest\u8221\'20\'1D in the company\u8217\'20\'19s history \u8211\'20\'13 and urging customers to steer clear.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has said the vast majority of its cafes remain open, and expressed disappointment that Starbucks Workers United launched the strike.\par \par \uc2 Negotiations over the first ever union contract for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers in the US broke down in recent months. Both sides have blamed the other.\par \par \uc2 Prominent politicians including Zohran Mamdani, the New York City mayor-elect, have backed the striking workers.\par \par \uc2 Why are \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers striking?\par \par \uc2 Since 13 November, unionized baristas at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  have been on strike. More than 2,000 workers are now on the picket line across 65 cities around the US.\par \par \uc2 The open-ended unfair labor practice strike was launched on \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Cred cup day\u8221\'20\'1D, which typically hails the start of the lucrative holiday trading season at the coffee chain.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and Starbucks Workers United, the union, have been bargaining over the chain\u8217\'20\'19s first union contract. But these talks stalled over economic elements of the contract. Each side has blamed the other.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks Workers United has also filed dozens of unfair labor practice charges with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  throughout its organizing campaign, including one in December, alleging that the chain had failed to bargain in good faith, and undermined the representative status of the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  to succeed. My livelihood depends on it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dachi Spoltore, a striking barista from Pittsburgh. \u8220\'20\'1CI know that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 success has to include and prioritize people like me who make the coffee, open the stores and keep the customers coming back. We\u8217\'20\'19re proud of our work, but we\u8217\'20\'19re tired of being treated like we\u8217\'20\'19re disposable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why we\u8217\'20\'19re taking this major step. We\u8217\'20\'19re confident and clear-eyed in what we need to win a contract and resolve the legal issues. We\u8217\'20\'19re risking a lot: our jobs, our livelihoods, our economic security. This might be a game to \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , but it isn\u8217\'20\'19t a game for us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 How many \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers are in the union?\par \par \uc2 Starbucks Workers United represents 11,000 baristas at more than 550 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores. Its organizing drive has become one of the highest-profile unionization efforts in a generation in the US.\par \par \uc2 The first \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  store {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/dec/09/starbucks-workers-unionize-buffalo-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  to unionize, by 19 to 8, in Buffalo, New York, in December 2021, setting the stage for a wave of mobilization that swept hundreds more stores across the nation.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  had actively fought unionization for decades, insisting its stores would operate best when executives at the company were able to work directly with its employees.\par \par \uc2 During a \uc2 US Senate\uc2  committee hearing in March 2023, its longtime CEO \uc2 Howard Schultz\uc2  defended \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 response to the union organizing campaign and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/mar/29/starbucks-howard-schultz-faces-bernie-sanders-at-union-busting-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responded}}}\uc2  to allegations of union busting by saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThese are allegations, and \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has not broken the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What has \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said about the strike?\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has blamed the union for the lack of progress in negotiations and claimed the strike hasn\u8217\'20\'19t affected operations.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , Jaci Anderson, said: \u8220\'20\'1CDespite Workers United\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to cause disruption, more than 99% of our coffeehouses remained open and our partners [employees] delivered the strongest Reusable Red Cup Day in company history building on the previous Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s holiday launch which was the biggest sales day ever for the company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe anticipate a bright holiday season and are eager to welcome customers to enjoy their favorite holiday beverage and sit and stay in one of our 17,000 locations across the US.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Anderson expressed disappointment \u8220\'20\'1Cthat Workers United, who only represents around 4% of our partners, has voted to authorize a strike instead of returning to the bargaining table\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen they\u8217\'20\'19re ready to come back, we\u8217\'20\'19re ready to talk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Any contract \u8220\'20\'1Cneeds to reflect the reality that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  already offers the best job in retail, including more than $30 an hour on average in pay and benefits for hourly partners\u8221\'20\'1D, she said.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s going on at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is under pressure to turn its business around.\par \par \uc2 In October, the coffee chain issued a press release declaring that it had delivered sales growth for the first time in seven quarters. That growth was just 1%.\par \par \uc2 A sharp rise in coffee prices and softening demand have hit the firm. Its shares have fallen 10% so far this year.\par \par \uc2 It has also reshuffled its top ranks several times in recent years. Schultz, who built \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  over several decades as CEO, abruptly returned to the role in 2022 after initially stepping down years earlier. He was succeeded by \uc2 Laxman Narasimhan\uc2  the following year, who was ousted after 16 months and replaced by \uc2 Brian Niccol\uc2 , former CEO of \uc2 Chipotle Mexican Grill\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Niccol has pledged to revive the chain\u8217\'20\'19s fortunes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/feb/24/starbucks-corporate-employee-lay-offs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unveiling}}}\uc2  job {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/25/starbucks-store-closures-lay-offs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cuts}}}\uc2  and store closures as part of an internal plan dubbed \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.starbucks.com/stories/2025/how-back-to-starbucks-is-reshaping-every-aspect-of-the-coffeehouse-experience/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Back to Starbucks}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on the strike?\par \par \uc2 Starbucks Workers United claims most of the 95 stores hit by the action have been forced to close due to insufficient staffing. The action is taking place across more than 65 cities.\par \par \uc2 On 19 November, the union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SBWorkersUnited/status/1991242397083160889"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set up }}}\uc2 a blockade at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 distribution center in York, Pennsylvania, the company\u8217\'20\'19s largest distribution center on the US east coast.\par \par \uc2 The union is threatening to escalate the campaign, dubbed \u8220\'20\'1Cno contract, no coffee\u8221\'20\'1D, by adding more stores if they don\u8217\'20\'19t receive new proposals and make progress with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in contract negotiations.\par \par \uc2 About 92% of Starbucks Workers United members voted to authorize an open-ended unfair labor practices strike, according to the union. \u8220\'20\'1CUnion baristas are prepared to make this the largest, and longest strike in company history during the critical holiday season,\u8221\'20\'1D it said in a November memo.\par \par \uc2 Why are politicians getting involved?\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the strike, a wave of lawmakers \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sanders.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/Starbucks-Letter_Senate.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 US senators }}}\uc2 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://laborcaucus.house.gov/media/in-the-news/more-than-100-lawmakers-push-starbucks-to-resume-union-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 82 congressional representatives }}}\uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 signed letters to Niccol, the current \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  CEO, demanding that the company reach a contract with the union. No Republicans signed either letter.\par \par \uc2 New York City\u8217\'20\'19s mayor-elect Zohran Mamdani also weighed in. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers across the country are on an Unfair Labor Practices strike, fighting for a fair contract,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/zohran-mamdani-boycott-starbucks-strike-2025-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on social media. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile workers are on strike, I won\u8217\'20\'19t be buying any \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , and I\u8217\'20\'19m asking you to join us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Katie Wilson, mayor-elect of Seattle, where \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is based, also made a similar call. \u8220\'20\'1CI am not buying \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and you should not either,\u8221\'20\'1D she said at a Starbucks Workers United {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kuow.org/stories/seattle-mayor-elect-katie-wilson-joins-striking-baristas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally}}}\uc2 , shortly after winning the close mayoral race. \u8220\'20\'1CBaristas are the heart and soul of this company, and they deserve better than empty promises and corporate union busting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is your home town, and mine. Seattle is making some changes right now. And I urge you to do the right thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251119elbj0048w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
