\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 UK is worst-performing market for \uc2 JD Sports\uc2  as youth unemployment hits sales\b0\par\par\uc2 Sarah Butler and Richard Partington \par \uc2 538 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 November 2025\par 16:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lack of spare cash among under-25s feeds slide in sales with annual profits to be at lower end of expectations\par \par \uc2 Unemployment among young people in the UK is hitting sales growth and profits at \uc2 JD Sports\uc2 , the owner of the trainer and sportwear chain has said, amid warnings about the high number of under-25s not in work, education or training.\par \par \uc2 The UK was the worst-performing market for \uc2 JD Group\uc2 , which also owns Blacks, Go Outdoors and a number of US and European sports chains.\par \par \uc2 R\u233\'00\'E9gis Schultz\uc2 ,the chief executive, said JD was experiencing \u8220\'20\'1Cpressures on our core customer demographic, including rising unemployment levels, as well as near-term volatility around consumer sentiment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His comments came as official figures on Thursday showed the number of 16- to 24-year-olds who are not in education, employment or training (Neet) remains stubbornly close to the highest level in a decade.\par \par \uc2 Despite a modest decline in the three months to September to 946,000, down from 948,000 in the previous quarter, campaigners said the figures from the \uc2 Office for National Statistics\uc2  showed Britain was at risk of failing a whole generation of young people.\par \par \uc2 The figures mean one in eight young people are Neet amid a rapid increase in unemployment more broadly, with the official jobless rate at 5%, the highest level since the Covid pandemic. Last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/nov/15/half-of-all-uk-jobs-shed-since-labour-came-to-power-are-among-under-25s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian revealed}}}\uc2  that almost half of all jobs shed since Labour came to power were among the under-25s.\par \par \uc2 Barry Fletcher, the chief executive of the Youth Futures Foundation, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a long-term problem that continues to negatively shape the lives of too many across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The squeeze on spare cash for young people contributed to a 3.3% slide in sales at established \uc2 JD Group\uc2  stores in the three months to 1 November. Sales were also down in the US and EU \u8211\'20\'13 by 1.7% and 1.1% respectively \u8211\'20\'13 amid similar pressures as well as a lack of new product launches to draw in shoppers and the slowdown in the trend for women\u8217\'20\'19s vintage trainers.\par \par \uc2 The company has also suffered from a heavy reliance on \uc2 Nike\uc2 , which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/oct/23/just-redo-it-inside-nikes-plans-to-put-the-swoosh-back-into-its-sales"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been struggling}}}\uc2  to spur consumer interest recently with critics pointing to a lack of new ideas.\par \par \uc2 JD said annual profits would now be at the lower end of expectations, at about \u163\'00\'A3853m, compared with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/jan/14/jd-sports-cuts-profit-forecast-price-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 once-hoped-for \u163\'00\'A31bn}}}\uc2 . It was \u8220\'20\'1Ctaking a pragmatic approach\u8221\'20\'1D to its outlook for this financial year, due to \u8220\'20\'1Cincrementally weaker macro and consumer indicators in recent weeks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Aarin Chiekrie, an equity analyst at the broker \uc2 Hargreaves Lansdown\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CTrading across the UK remains particularly weak, with recent changes to employer taxes and minimum wages bringing a handful of extra costs and challenges.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The weak numbers came as another youth brand, Dr Martens, said consumers were \u8220\'20\'1Ccautious right now\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Clooking for deals\u8221\'20\'1D right across Europe and in the US. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/nov/20/markets-rally-nvidia-results-ai-bubble-us-jobs-report-ftse-pound-dollar-business-live-news?page=with%3Ablock-691eea9c8f08d30400d99745#block-691eea9c8f08d30400d99745"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 British bootmaker said}}}\uc2  it was putting up prices on some items in the US in January to offset the impact of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s import tariffs, which amounted to between \u163\'00\'A37m and \u163\'00\'A39m.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251120elbk0053e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
