\par\par \uc2 Media\par \b \uc2 The ABC has been attacked in \uc2 News Corp\uc2  outlets for its editing of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Capitol speech. Did it do the same as the BBC?\b0\par\par\uc2 Amanda Meade Media correspondent \par \uc2 1,202 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 November 2025\par 20:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 News Corp\uc2  commentators have lined up to accuse the ABC of unethical practice over a 2021 Four Corners program. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Trump said, and what it saidFollow our Australia news live blog for latest updatesSign up for Guardian Australia\u8217\'20\'19s free weekly media newsletter here\par \par \uc2 Sky News Australia and The Australian have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theaustralian.com.au/inquirer/i-predicted-the-abc-would-distort-trumps-speech-and-it-took-15-minutes-to-prove-it/news-story/87511ae8ca60ec3f881b2f0d3eb6bc45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused the ABC of distorting}}}\uc2  a speech by Donald Trump on the day of the attack on the US Capitol, 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 Their commentator \uc2 Chris Kenny\uc2  called the treatment of the speech in a Four Corners episode an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.skynews.com.au/australia-news/politics/almost-identical-sky-news-host-chris-kenny-exposes-abc-committing-same-journalistic-sin-as-bbc-in-doctoring-footage-of-president-donald-trump/news-story/5a13ddca1c58deb7b3a62dd9b9a9cb64"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Calmost identical act of deception\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  as the edit of the BBC\u8217\'20\'19s Panorama program that led to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2025/nov/09/tim-davie-expected-to-resign-bbc-director-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resignation of the British public broadcaster\u8217\'20\'19s director general and head of news}}}\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday the ABC\u8217\'20\'19s managing director, \uc2 Hugh Marks\uc2 , is due to appear at the \uc2 National Press Club\uc2 , where he may face questions over similarities or otherwise between the two programs.\par \par \uc2 So what are the words under debate, and does the ABC have a case to answer?\par \par \uc2 What did the two broadcasters do?\par \par \uc2 Both Panorama and Four Corners used excerpts from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/02/10/966396848/read-trumps-jan-6-speech-a-key-part-of-impeachment-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech}}}\uc2  at the Ellipse before the storming of the Capitol building on 6 January 2021. While the BBC spliced together two sentences almost an hour apart, the ABC edited a single grab, omitting some repetition and a complete sentence between two statements.\par \par \uc2 The BBC edit\par \par \uc2 The episode of Panorama in question was broadcast shortly before the 2024 US election. The edit was highlighted in a dossier from a former external adviser to the BBC\u8217\'20\'19s editorial standards committee that was leaked to the UK\u8217\'20\'19s Daily Telegraph.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech was edited by Panorama to put together two sentences that were said 54 minutes apart, making it appear as though he was telling his supporters they would walk to the US Capitol and \u8220\'20\'1Cfight like hell\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The edit suggested Trump told the crowd: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to walk down to the Capitol and I\u8217\'20\'19ll be there with you, and we fight. We fight like hell.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The word \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D is used throughout the speech, but not directly after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s suggestion of walking to the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 The BBC has acknowledged its program wrongly edited grabs from the speech and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2025/nov/13/bbc-apologises-to-donald-trump-over-edit-of-speech-for-panorama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has apologised}}}\uc2 . Its chair, \uc2 Samir Shah\uc2 , said the editing of two clips from separate parts of the speech gave the impression \u8220\'20\'1Cof a direct call for violent action\u8221\'20\'1D from Trump.\par \par \uc2 The Four Corners program\par \par \uc2 Reported by \uc2 Sarah Ferguson\uc2 , Downfall \u8211\'20\'13 The Last Days of President Trump was broadcast on the ABC on 1 February 2021 and is still {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iview.abc.net.au/video/NC2103H001S00"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 available on iView}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ferguson spoke to multiple witnesses and used footage taken by rioters to explore the motivation for the attack.\par \par \uc2 Four Corners used a single grab of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech from which 10 seconds were edited \u8211\'20\'13 the sentences struck through below.\par \par \uc2 An ABC analysis in response to \uc2 News Corp{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theaustralian.com.au/business/media/abc-faces-fresh-scrutiny-over-cuts-to-trump-january-6-speech-coverage-of-middle-east/news-story/4cc8a8d3371802f1f0d557df25dd518c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims last week}}}\uc2  concluded it was a minor edit that did not mislead audiences as to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s meaning. The quote also reflects accurately the broader message Trump conveyed to the crowd over the speech, which lasted more than an hour.\par \par \uc2 What have the critics of the ABC claimed?\par \par \uc2 Kenny, The Australian\u8217\'20\'19s associate editor who first made the allegations against Four Corners on his Sky News program, believes the words removed by the ABC left the impression {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theaustralian.com.au/inquirer/i-predicted-the-abc-would-distort-trumps-speech-and-it-took-15-minutes-to-prove-it/news-story/87511ae8ca60ec3f881b2f0d3eb6bc45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump had urged the violence}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFour Corners pretended to convey to audiences what Trump encouraged protesters to do at the Capitol that day. Yet in his only direct advice to protesters, the president urged cheering on and peaceful patriotism,\u8221\'20\'1D Kenny said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey have clipped up the speech to suit their narrative rather than reality, and the true meaning of what Donald Trump was saying that day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Inconveniently for Kenny\u8217\'20\'19s argument, he himself {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theaustralian.com.au/commentary/washington-riots-donald-trump-knows-exactly-what-he-is-doing/news-story/7919b5ad99af157e4e7f34b7fd7fb8df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on 7 January 2021}}}\uc2  that Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cfomented and encouraged\u8221\'20\'1D the lawlessness and that \u8220\'20\'1Cno excuse ought be offered for any protester breaking the law nor any leader inciting them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Over more than a week, the Murdoch platforms have assembled known ABC critics to back up their claim of systemic bias at the broadcaster, and in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theaustralian.com.au/commentary/editorials/heads-have-rolled-at-the-bbc-where-is-accountability-at-the-abc/news-story/8814e59846805cb36e1051060830ddfa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 editorial suggested}}}\uc2  ABC leaders follow the BBC\u8217\'20\'19s lead and resign.\par \par \uc2 The Liberal senator Sarah Henderson called for a Senate inquiry into the editorial failings of the public broadcaster; the former ABC director Joe Gersh, columnist Tom Switzer, former Liberal leader \uc2 Alexander Downer\uc2  and founding editor of Quillette, Claire Lehmann, all bought in to the narrative.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/article/2024/aug/28/weekly-beast-email-austrailan-media-diary-free-newsletter-subscribe-sign-up?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up to get Guardian Australia\u8217\'20\'19s weekly media diary as a free newsletter}}}\par \par \uc2 How has the ABC responded?\par \par \uc2 The ABC rejects Kenny\u8217\'20\'19s claim that the ABC committed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe same journalistic sin\u8221\'20\'1D as the BBC, saying the way it quoted Trump reflected accurately the broader message conveyed to the crowd over the hour-long speech.\par \par \uc2 The managing director, Marks, the news director, Justin Stevens, and the ABC Ombudsman, Fiona Cameron, quickly rejected the allegation by \uc2 News Corp\uc2 , saying the edit in the Four Corners program did not change the meaning of that section of the speech and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.abc.net.au/about/media-centre/statements-and-responses/abc-statement-on-downfall/106000406"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not mislead}}}\uc2  the audience.\par \par \uc2 Stevens told his team in an email: \u8220\'20\'1CThe opportunistic attempt to seek to engineer a similar crisis here to the BBC\u8217\'20\'19s is transparent and doesn\u8217\'20\'19t stack up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Does the \uc2 News Corp\uc2  allegation against the ABC carry weight?\par \par \uc2 Alan Sunderland, a former editorial director of the ABC, said it was the job of news reporters to select newsworthy elements from speeches that are relevant and significant, in a way that does not misrepresent those original speeches.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not the job of news reporters to report on every comment made or every issue raised, but to select the newsworthy elements in ways that do not mislead,\u8221\'20\'1D he told Guardian Australia.\par \par \uc2 Sunderland said a 2021 editorial in The Australian, much like Four Corners, published edited, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theaustralian.com.au/commentary/editorials/trump-presidency-dying-in-futile-assault-on-democracy/news-story/b0c17f066efcd00c65991484227d464f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 selected elements of the speech}}}\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Csummarised their impact by saying \u8216\'20\'18it would be hard to imagine a more incendiary act by an incumbent US President than to exploit passions that were running so high\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNeither source suggested that the president had deliberately and specifically urged or instructed protestors to invade the Capitol building and commit acts of violence, but both chose selected, edited elements of the speech to provide a sense of its impact and import. In my view, neither did so in a way which was misleading or inaccurate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Monday the ABC\u8217\'20\'19s Media Watch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.abc.net.au/mediawatch/episodes/bbc/106019728"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 devoted the program to the BBC crisis}}}\uc2  and came to the same conclusion: there was no basis for the claim the ABC was similarly guilty of deceptive editing.\par \par \uc2 The host, Linton Besser, said: \u8220\'20\'1CRather, it seems, this was a naked attempt to draw the ABC into a public broadcasting crisis 17,000km away, which smeared without foundation some of the ABC\u8217\'20\'19s finest reporting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kenny returned fire on Tuesday, saying the Media Watch analysis was as \u8220\'20\'1Cethically challenged and intellectually barren as the original sin\u8221\'20\'1D. He issued his own fighting words: \u8220\'20\'1CIt will not be the end of the matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251118elbi003mo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
