\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Workers at US landscape company sue Trump ally over human-trafficking raid\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 667 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 November 2025\par 17:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Employees at the Utah company \uc2 Rubicon\uc2  are filing a lawsuit against former state attorney general Sean Reyes\par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 Rubicon\uc2 , a landscape company that was subjected to a televised human-trafficking raid led by Trump ally and former Utah attorney general Sean Reyes, filed a federal complaint on Tuesday alleging Reyes and his office \u8220\'20\'1Cviolated the law to attack a Utah company for political purposes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The workers are seeking recompense after alleging that Reyes and other officials at the Utah office of the attorney general used false information to file a case against the company that caused enormous damage but was later dismissed.\par \par \uc2 The suit follows a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sltrib.com/news/politics/2025/10/28/utah-company-sues-utah-ags-office/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similar action}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Rubicon\uc2  and its parent company, which is seeking $1bn in damages and alleges officials \u8220\'20\'1Cconspired to manufacture bogus criminal charges to falsely inflate the public perception of the severity of human trafficking in Utah\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Reyes is a longtime Trump ally. During Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://web.archive.org/web/20231103114326/https://www.nytimes.com/2017/04/28/us/politics/sean-reyes-utah-attorney-general-ftc.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considered}}}\uc2  to head the \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2 . In 2020, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sltrib.com/news/politics/2020/08/27/sean-reyes-will-speak-gop/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 praised}}}\uc2  Trump at the Republican National Convention as a \u8220\'20\'1Cwarrior against human trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/03/16/trump-ally-sean-reyes-mitt-romney-primary-00017741"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 served }}}\uc2 as Utah co-chair for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign and was reportedly encouraged by Trump to run for Senate in 2024.\par \par \uc2 On 20 November 2023, officials with the Utah attorney general office\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/UtahAG/status/1922400345080185016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secure strike force}}}\uc2  raided \uc2 Rubicon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s offices, accompanied by a local Fox News affiliate crew, and charged the company with more than 50 crimes related to human trafficking.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuits allege none of the crimes or allegations were true, but were filed under false pretenses days after the Utah legislature approved an audit of Reyes\u8217\'20\'19s office amid questions about his ties to Tim Ballard, the founder of an anti-trafficking organization Operation Underground Railroad (OUR). Several {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/nov/15/salt-lake-city-tim-ballard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women are suing}}}\uc2  Ballard over sexual assault allegations, though Ballard has denied the allegations and the Salt Lake City district attorney declined to file criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was known and foreseeable that when government agents submitted materially false and misleading affidavits, and then invited the news media to film the raid, that the businesses employing Utah citizens would be crippled and their employees would suffer serious financial harm,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawsuit filed by workers said.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit alleges the raid was conducted after the audit of Reyes and his ties to Ballard.\par \par \uc2 The charges against \uc2 Rubicon\uc2  were dismissed in 2024 by the attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office after a judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/rubicon-sues-former-ag-sean-174252273.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  they were filed prematurely and many of the warrants were obtained through false information.\par \par \uc2 Dario Benitez, an employee at \uc2 Rubicon\uc2  and one of the plaintiffs in the lawsuit, said he was in \u8220\'20\'1Cdisbelief\u8221\'20\'1D when the raid and charges were filed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRubicon workers were hit very hard,\u8221\'20\'1D Benitez said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe company was a very fast-growing business and never had any layoffs. Because of the actions of the Utah [attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office], the company had to do four different rounds of layoffs. Some of those employees laid off still have not found work, others struggled to find new jobs. Employees who were able to keep their jobs suffered pay reductions, including loss of bonuses and significant salary reductions. To date, salaries and bonuses have not been restored.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Benitez noted because of the raid, the company lost over 50% of its contracts, resulting in layoffs or reduced hours, forcing workers to get second jobs to make ends meet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe goal of this filing is to correct the record and us as individuals to move forward with our lives,\u8221\'20\'1D added Scott Bennion, an employee at Scandia, \uc2 Rubicon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s parent company, in a press release on the lawsuit. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen accusations are made without the evidence to support them, the impact does not simply disappear. Restoring accuracy is part of restoring trust.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Utah attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office and Reyes did not respond to multiple requests for comment. They had declined to comment on the initial lawsuit filed by \uc2 Rubicon\uc2  and its parent company.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251118elbi003bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
