\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Whatever it takes\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers launch US strike and call for boycott\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 721 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 November 2025\par 16:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Unfair labor practice strike on \u8216\'20\'18red cup day\u8217\'20\'19 in over 40 cities comes amid stagnant negotiations with coffee chain\par \par \uc2 More than a thousand \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers have commenced a strike in more than 40 cities across the US on Thursday amid stagnant negotiations with the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest coffee chain over a first union contract.\par \par \uc2 On the company\u8217\'20\'19s annual \u8220\'20\'1Cred cup day\u8221\'20\'1D, hailing the start of the lucrative holiday season, Starbucks Workers United is launching an unfair labor practice (ULP) strike, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nocontractnocoffee.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rallies}}}\uc2  planned in locations including New York City; Philadelphia, Pennsylvania; Chicago, Illinois; Columbus, Ohio; and Anaheim, California.\par \par \uc2 About 65 stores are initially affected. Organizers plan to expand the strike to more locations should executives hold firm \u8211\'20\'13 and want customers to steer clear of the chain as part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nocontractnocoffee.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign}}}\uc2  dubbed \u8220\'20\'1Cno contract, no coffee\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cdisappointed\u8221\'20\'1D that Workers United had voted to strike, rather than continue bargaining, but insisted the \u8220\'20\'1Cvast majority\u8221\'20\'1D of stores would be unaffected by the action. The company stands accused of \u8220\'20\'1Cstonewalling\u8221\'20\'1D at the table by union officials.\par \par \uc2 Since the first \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  store {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/28/starbucks-workers-buffalo-ny-organizing-union-first-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to unionize in 2021}}}\uc2 , more than 650 have followed, in the face of vehement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/28/starbucks-workers-buffalo-ny-organizing-union-first-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposition from the chain\u8217\'20\'19s management}}}\uc2 . Contract negotiations broke down earlier this year, following the union\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sbworkersunited.org/starbucks-baristas-overwhelmingly-reject-starbucks-insufficient-union-contract-offer/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejection}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 economic offer.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks Workers United announced last week that workers had voted to authorize an open-ended ULP strike with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sbworkersunited.org/strike-authorization/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 92% voting}}}\uc2  in favor. The union had spent months demanding that managers consider new proposals to improve staffing and pay, and resolve hundreds of unfair labor practice charges filed by the union against \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  throughout its organizing campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have not been given meaningful proposals to finalize this contract since the announcement of the strike authorization vote,\u8221\'20\'1D Jasmine Leli, a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  barista for three years and strike captain from Buffalo, New York, told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CThe baristas are prepared to do whatever it takes to get this finalized contract.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Striking baristas are asking that customers \u8220\'20\'1Cdo not buy at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  while workers are on strike\u8221\'20\'1D, Leli added, to help \u8220\'20\'1Cwin the fair contract that we have spent many, many months negotiating with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve waited long enough,\u8221\'20\'1D said Leli. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are so close to finishing this contract, and we need them to just finish it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The beginning of the strike coincides with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.starbucks.com/stories/2025/starbucks-holiday-2025/?gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=23164838535&gbraid=0AAAAADoJV5syQJpRe9R8h0O24oTALMCol&gclid=CjwKCAiA_dDIBhB6EiwAvzc1cA189eDUqMiV2K37Goiv3E7EMAtFbO3GPuz1G4D3-9t6RcSVOuNhABoC91oQAvD_BwE#redcupday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 red cup day}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, a promotion in which customers receive a reusable red holiday cup with the purchase of a holiday drink. It is typically one of the company\u8217\'20\'19s biggest sales days of the year.\par \par \uc2 The chain is scrambling to turn around its US business and win back customers, after several years of sluggish sales. In September it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/25/starbucks-store-closures-lay-offs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced plans}}}\uc2  to shut more than 100 cafes across North America and lay off about 900 corporate staff.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnion baristas mean business and are ready to do whatever it takes to win a fair contract and end \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 unfair labor practices,\u8221\'20\'1D said Michelle Eisen, a Starbucks Workers United spokesperson and veteran barista of 15 years. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  to succeed, but turning the company around and bringing customers back begins with listening to and supporting the baristas who are responsible for the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  experience.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  keeps stonewalling, they should expect to see their business grind to a halt. The ball is in \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , Jaci Anderson, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are disappointed that Workers United, who only represents around 4% of our partners, has voted to authorize a strike instead of returning to the bargaining table. When they\u8217\'20\'19re ready to come back, we\u8217\'20\'19re ready to talk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Any contract \u8220\'20\'1Cneeds to reflect the reality that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  already offers the best job in retail, including more than $30 an hour on average in pay and benefits for hourly partners\u8221\'20\'1D, added Anderson. \u8220\'20\'1CThe facts show people like working at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 . Partner engagement is up, turnover is nearly half the industry average, and we get more than 1m million job applications a year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur customers can be assured that our partners will be ready to serve them at the vast majority of our more than 10,000 company operated coffeehouses and nearly 7,000 licensed locations throughout the holiday season, regardless of the union\u8217\'20\'19s plans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251113elbd002jt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
