\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Utah\u8217\'20\'19s oldest LGBTQ+ bar closes amid workers\u8217\'20\'19 union push: \u8216\'20\'18We feel extremely disposable\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 988 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2025\par 12:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers at the SunTrapp \u8211\'20\'13 opened in 1973 in Salt Lake City \u8211\'20\'13 claim the shuttering was a \u8216\'20\'18stunt\u8217\'20\'19 to prevent unionization\par \par \uc2 Salt Lake City\u8217\'20\'19s oldest and longest-running LGBTQ+ bar has closed, with workers claiming the shuttering was a \u8220\'20\'1Cstunt\u8221\'20\'1D to prevent unionization.\par \par \uc2 The SunTrapp, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sltrib.com/artsliving/food/2025/11/01/historic-lgbtq-bar-closes-slc/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widely considered}}}\uc2  the oldest LGBTQ+ bar in Utah was founded in 1973 and is one of the few safe havens for the community. It shut on 31 October after workers pushed to unionize.\par \par \uc2 Workers who spoke with the Guardian allege the owner of the bar engaged in numerous unfair labor practices after they submitted a letter requesting voluntary recognition of the union with Communications Workers of America Local 7765 in late September.\par \par \uc2 In a Republican dominated state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.safehome.org/data-lgbtq-state-safety-rankings/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ranked }}}\uc2 as one of the least safe states in the US for the LGBTQ+ community, workers called the bar \u8220\'20\'1Ca really special place\u8221\'20\'1D and a safe haven for the community. The bar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ebar.com/story/158171"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had to increase security}}}\uc2  after the Charlie Kirk assassination that occurred in Utah in September heightened concerns over threats toward the community.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a really special place where you can go and be judgment free,\u8221\'20\'1D Natalie Jankowski, a lead bartender at the SunTrapp, told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a lot of older queer people, older trans people, who feel comfortable coming there and nowhere else. We have a lot of Mormons who just left Mormonism who want to have their first drink, judgment free, come there, and we get a lot of people who are questioning their sexuality and they just want to talk to the bar staff about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jankowski explained she had worked at the bar through previous closures under different owners, and had watched as staff concerns went unheard.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI watched them make mistakes here and there, not be willing to hear out the queer staff that they were employing to try and bring the bar up, and then they lost the bar. And as staff, we were kind of watching that same thing happen again,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe staff has very good reason to believe that this is a stunt. I also don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s fair to tell a group of young queer people who have been part of this community longer than the owner to just leave and get a new job if we don\u8217\'20\'19t like it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Morgan Sturgill, another bartender at SunTrapp, explained the unionization drive stemmed from the close-knit community of staff at the bar and the collective drive for improvements and a desire to have a voice on policy implementations and accountability for management.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe all cared about it so much, and just wanted it to be a place that everybody had a voice to be able to change policy, to be able to have a say in how things were run,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sturgill. \u8220\'20\'1CThe owner has refused to really talk with us at all and have any sort of conversation with us about it, and is just refusing to acknowledge that the demands we are setting out are completely reasonable. She just wants to prevent unionization at all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Beltsazzar Valenzuela, who worked as a barback, bartender and security at the bar, noted \u8220\'20\'1Call of us were customers at some point before we started working there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re asking for accountability for the most part. That\u8217\'20\'19s the biggest thing, is accountability,\u8221\'20\'1D Valenzuela said. \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like a good faith conversation would have resolved this in like 10 minutes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The owner, Mary Peterson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DPFVoR7EuNl/?img_index=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2  many of the workers after they sought to unionize, then rehired them. She {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/reel/810277761759966"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stated }}}\uc2 in a video post on social media that she had to hire them back as she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t initially aware it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t legal to fire them for unionizing.\par \par \uc2 She also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sltrib.com/artsliving/2025/09/26/suntrapp-lgbtq-bar-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  the bar, which employs around two dozen workers, was \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo small\u8221\'20\'1D to unionize, though there are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.findlaw.com/legalblogs/small-business/can-small-business-workers-unionize/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no legal exceptions}}}\uc2  barring workers at small employers from unionizing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI did fire them because I felt like they were a threat to the business. I thought that they were coming after me saying, you know, unionize or we\u8217\'20\'19re going to take you out, which ultimately is happening to me now,\u8221\'20\'1D said Peterson.\par \par \uc2 Workers claim the owner then began {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/photo/?fbid=122095581165084420&set=pb.61582532605531.-2207520000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 implementing}}}\uc2  new policies they say were designed to entrap workers to justify firing them, such as changing the drink menu and strictly enforcing late policies. They began an unfair labor practice strike in early October after a security guard and union supporter at the bar was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/suntrappworkersunite?igsh=dnBibjFlYXVqYWJl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2 . The union has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dailyutahchronicle.com/2025/11/03/suntrapp-shuts-doors-following-monthlong-workers-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  on the bar to rescind the firing and its policies enacted after the union went public, and allow a fair union election to proceed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe started handing out people\u8217\'20\'19s final warning, final written warnings for stuff that they had never been approached about. She started enacting some policies that were meant to trap us,\u8221\'20\'1D added Jankowski.\par \par \uc2 Due to the government shutdown, the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/search/case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 website}}}\uc2  has been down, halting the formal union election process and the filing and processing of unfair labor practice charges.\par \par \uc2 The union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DPE43MnEnNv/?img_index=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alluded }}}\uc2 to the closure several weeks ago, citing it as a common union-busting tactic.\par \par \uc2 Then on 31 October, the bar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/photo?fbid=759003117188664&set=pcb.759003180521991"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced }}}\uc2 its closure, claiming \u8220\'20\'1Cthe financial impact of consistent protests\u8221\'20\'1D caused the closure, and noted a \u8220\'20\'1Cpath forward\u8221\'20\'1D for the bar remains unclear.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI personally feel that the pseudo closure of the Trap, is a way to fear monger an already marginalized community who is in distress and in fear,\u8221\'20\'1D said Yara Al-Badri, the social media marketer and event planner for the bar. \u8220\'20\'1CWe live in a world where queer people feel extremely unsafe, especially right now, in this political climate, and we feel extremely disposable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Peterson and the SunTrapp did not respond to multiple requests for comment from the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251109elb9001jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
