\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Students and faculty at over 100 US universities protest against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attacks\b0\par\par\uc2 Alice Speri \par \uc2 735 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2025\par 21:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Student, national and local groups across US organized day of action to condemn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s assault on academic freedom\par \par \uc2 Students, faculty and staff at more than 100 campuses across the US rallied against the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s assault on higher education on Friday \u8211\'20\'13 the first in a planned series of nationwide, coordinated protests that organizers hope will culminate in large-scale students\u8217\'20\'19 and workers\u8217\'20\'19 strikes next May Day and a nationwide general strike {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/autoworkers-uaw-shawn-fain-may-2028-national-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in May 2028}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The day of action was organized under the banner of Students Rise Up, a network of students including both local groups and national organizations such as Sunrise Movement and Campus Climate Network. Students were joined by faculty and educational workers\u8217\'20\'19 unions like the American Association of University Professors and Higher Education Labor United.\par \par \uc2 Protesters called on university administrators and elected officials to denounce the president\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/23/us-college-campuses-trump-funding-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 months-long effort}}}\uc2  to force US universities to abide by its ideological priorities and urged them to reject Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/02/trump-university-funding-compact"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compact}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, which would give universities preferential access to federal funding in exchange for a commitment to advance the administration\u8217\'20\'19s conservative agenda. Only one university, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/11/new-college-of-florida-rightwing-takeover"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New College of Florida}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a public school that state legislators have turned into a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/29/ron-desantis-florida-university-new-college-woke-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bastion of conservatism}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 has so far accepted it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUniversities should be a place of learning, not propaganda machines,\u8221\'20\'1D Alicia Colomer, managing director at Campus Climate Network, said ahead of the protests. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why students, workers and alumni around the country are taking action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the day unfolded, hundreds of students across the country walked out of classes, unfurled banners and rallied on campuses, often joined by faculty and other staff. In addition to denouncing the compact, they called for a more affordable education and for the protection of all students \u8211\'20\'13 from transgender to international ones.\par \par \uc2 At the \uc2 University of Kansas\uc2 , about 70 students demanded administrations divest from weapons manufacturers and Israel, refuse to collaborate with ICE, safeguard gender-affirming housing and meet faculty\u8217\'20\'19s demands for fair contracts. At \uc2 Duke University\uc2 , in North Carolina, students and professors held signs demanding the university stand with immigrants, pay its workers a $25 hourly wage, and protect trans and international students. At Brown University in Rhode Island \u8211\'20\'13 one of the first institutions to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/30/brown-university-trump-administration-agreement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reach a settlement}}}\uc2  with the Trump administration earlier this year \u8211\'20\'13 passersby were invited to endorse a banner listing a series of demands by dipping their hands in paint and leaving their print, while a group of faculty members nearby lectured about the history of autocracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump came to our community thinking we could be bullied out of our freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D said Simon Aron, a sophomore and co-president of Brown Rise Up. \u8220\'20\'1CHe was wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In New York City, students and faculty from multiple campuses gathered by the midtown headquarters of the investment firm \uc2 Apollo Global Management\uc2  to protest against its CEO, \uc2 Marc Rowan\uc2 , a billionaire Trump donor and key architect of the compact whom they say \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://psc-cuny.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/11.7-Flyer_11.3.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has no business making policy for higher education}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 They cited Rowan\u8217\'20\'19s involvement with the online \uc2 University of Phoenix\uc2 , which they described as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe largest single producer of student debt in the country\u8221\'20\'1D and his role in paving the way for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/nov/05/university-anitisemitism-investigations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ongoing abuse of civil rights legislation}}}\uc2  to target universities over students and faculty\u8217\'20\'19s criticism of Israel.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Apollo\uc2  did not respond to a request for comment but the firm {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2025/11/06/business/apollo-tells-nyc-workers-to-stay-home-as-it-braces-for-protest-over-marc-rowans-trump-support/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly instructed}}}\uc2  staff to stay home on Friday in anticipation of the protest. In a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/10/opinion/trump-compact-universities-rowan.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times op-ed}}}\uc2 , Rowan defended the compact, writing that American higher education was \u8220\'20\'1Cbroken\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Ccourse correction must come from the outside\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Amy Offner, a history professor at the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2 , told the Guardian that the campaign against Rowan is part of a broader effort to protect US higher education from the influence of ultra-wealthy individuals. \u8220\'20\'1CBillionaires should not control what can be taught and studied in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The protests marked the first time that students, faculty and staff have staged such a large-scale response. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is only one way forward in saving higher education and democracy writ large and that is students, faculty, staff united,\u8221\'20\'1D Todd Wolfson, the president of the \uc2 AAUP\uc2 , said on a call with protest organizers last week. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to become a new political force.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251107elb7005mt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
