\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Workers decry Trump officials as \u8216\'20\'18out of control\u8217\'20\'19 as longest shutdown drags on\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 956 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 November 2025\par 15:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Key figures accused of harassment, bullying and attacks as US employees work without pay to keep services running\par \par \uc2 As the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-federal-government-shutdown-2025/2025/nov/03/all"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US federal shutdown}}}\uc2  enters its second month, government workers are accusing the Trump administration of being \u8220\'20\'1Cout of control\u8221\'20\'1D and bullying people who are \u8220\'20\'1Csimply trying to do their best\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The shutdown surpassed 35 days this week, beating the previous record set under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first presidential term. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://federalnewsnetwork.com/government-shutdown/2025/10/feds-told-shutdown-furloughs-extended-to-late-november/#:~:text=Congress%20failed%20to%20pass%20a,a%20partisan%20or%20political%20message."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 About 700,000 federal employees}}}\uc2  are furloughed without pay, and about 700,000 additional federal workers have been working without pay through the shutdown.\par \par \uc2 Affected workers say the shutdown has been a continuation of attacks they have experienced under the Trump administration, from mass firings \u8211\'20\'13 many of which have been overturned or blocked in federal courts \u8211\'20\'13 to drastic budget cuts, pushes to take early retirements or resignation buyouts, and threats of withholding back pay for workers furloughed during the shutdown.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s already been a chaotic year,\u8221\'20\'1D said Micah Niemeier-Walsh, American Federation of Federal Government Employees (AFGE)local 3840 vice president, who works at the \uc2 National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health\uc2  (\uc2 Niosh\uc2 ). She was initially fired along with most employees at the agency, but reinstated in May after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ohsonline.com/articles/2025/05/16/niosh-employees-reinstated-after-legal-ruling-and-political-pressure-halt-layoffs.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political pressure }}}\uc2 to overturn the firings and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.assp.org/news-and-articles/niosh-reinstatements-a-critical-step-forward-for-worker-safety"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court intervened}}}\uc2  to block most of the firings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor many agencies, like the one that I am employed by, we\u8217\'20\'19ve been effectively shut down for many months already because of the reductions in force that have already happened, and all of the attacks that we\u8217\'20\'19ve been seeing on the federal workforce,\u8221\'20\'1D said Niemeier-Walsh.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s become out of control, and I really hope that this shutdown is a wake-up call of how bad things have gotten.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In November, furloughed government employees received furlough extension notices, although many notices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govexec.com/pay-benefits/2025/10/employees-are-receiving-renewed-furlough-notices-shutdown-enters-second-month-time-without-back-pay-guarantees/409227/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not contain assurances}}}\uc2  they would receive back pay once the government reopens. Denial of back pay has been a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2025/10/07/trump-memo-furloughed-federal-workers-backpay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threat repeatedly made}}}\uc2  by the Trump administration during the shutdown, along with firings during the shutdown, which were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/15/federal-worker-firings-blocked-judge-government-shutdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked}}}\uc2  in a federal court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have never, ever, ever, ever, ever thought that we would have our government attacking government employees,\u8221\'20\'1D said Omar Algeciras, who works at the Department of Labor. \u8220\'20\'1C I think this is the epitome of harassment, bullying and attacks on people that are simply trying to do their best to provide a service or services to American workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s treatment of federal workers and their unions has put significant pressure and mental health burdens on federal workers who provide services to the American public, said Algeciras, vice-president of \uc2 AFGE\uc2  Local 2391.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is unprecedented, it\u8217\'20\'19s unnecessary and I really do think that it\u8217\'20\'19s very disheartening and saddening to see and to have to talk to some of our members and remind them that they need to take a moment for themselves, not to focus on what\u8217\'20\'19s being said,\u8221\'20\'1D added Algeciras. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re having to take care of our union members, we\u8217\'20\'19re having to take care of our co-workers, because it\u8217\'20\'19s not coming from the top down any more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 AFGE\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/27/afge-union-government-shutdown-federal-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  for an end to the government shutdown, avoiding assigning blame to Republicans or Democrats for the shutdown and its prolongation.\par \par \uc2 As the stalemate to end the government shutdown continues into November, Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/government-shutdown-could-become-longest-ever-as-trump-says-he-wont-be-extorted-by-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 affirmed}}}\uc2  he has no plans to negotiate with Democrats, with the shutdown adding to the stress and anxieties federal employees have already endured under the administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to cull their workforce.\par \par \uc2 Russell Vought\uc2 , the White House office of management and budget director, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eenews.net/articles/russ-vought-wanted-feds-in-trauma-its-happening/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  before the administration took office he wanted to put federal workers \u8220\'20\'1Cin trauma\u8221\'20\'1D and for them to be viewed as \u8220\'20\'1Cvillains\u8221\'20\'1D, and he has attempted to use the shutdown to further those efforts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor myself and my members, they\u8217\'20\'19ve been going through this chaos and stress and anxiety since February of, from one day to the next, not knowing if they\u8217\'20\'19re going to have a job,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tandy Zitkus, \uc2 AFGE\uc2  Local 898 president and a furloughed worker at the \uc2 Occupational Safety and Health Administration (Osha)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince February, there\u8217\'20\'19s been a constant threat every day when you get up and go to work, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unfortunately nothing new. It\u8217\'20\'19s become a norm for the federal worker.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers have been forced to budget as best they can around missed paychecks, from filing for unemployment and waiting on those benefits, deciding whether to visit food banks and requesting deferments on bills, said Zitkus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s overwhelming. It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to stay positive,\u8221\'20\'1D Zitkus said. \u8220\'20\'1CFederal workers serve the people. They\u8217\'20\'19re not politicians, and so there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of frustration being expressed to me by my members of: why is this going on, why is there a political fight going on that affects us? We\u8217\'20\'19re civil servants, and we serve the American people, and we want to be able to continue to do that and be paid.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Abigail Jackson, the White House deputy secretary, placed the shutdown blame solely on Democrats and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/04/government-shutdown-republican-lies-healthcare-immigrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeated the misleading claim}}}\uc2  that Democrats are pushing for healthcare for undocumented immigrants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only reason the government was shut down at all, let alone for this long, is because the Democrats decided to hold the American people hostage to push their radical, far-left policy agenda of free healthcare for illegal aliens,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican families have missed paychecks and benefits because of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 irresponsible behavior. President Trump wants the government reopen \u8211\'20\'13 the Democrats can choose to reopen it at any point, and they should do so immediately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251106elb6002uz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
