\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers hold strike vote amid anger over pay and conditions\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 903 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2025\par 15:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Union says world\u8217\'20\'19s largest coffee chain engaged in bad faith bargaining and stonewalled over contract\par \par \uc2 Unionized {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/starbucks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks}}}\uc2  workers across the US are casting their votes on whether to hold a strike amid anger over pay and conditions at the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest coffee chain, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/the-fight-to-unionize-starbucks-by-the-numbers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allegations}}}\uc2  it breached labor laws by engaging in bad faith bargaining.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has faced a rapid wave of mobilization since 2021. Starbucks Workers United, a union representing baristas at the chain, has won elections at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unionelections.org/data/starbucks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 650}}}\uc2  of its locations in 45 states and the District of Columbia, representing more than 12,000 workers.\par \par \uc2 Butit has yet to obtain a contract. Starbucks Workers United claims company management started to \u8220\'20\'1Cmajorly stonewall\u8221\'20\'1D the union; \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  claims the union walked away from the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 A strike authorization vote called by Starbucks Workers United began last Friday, 24 October, and will continue until Sunday 2 November. About 70 pickets have been planned in 60 cities across the US.\par \par \uc2 Many \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  baristas say they are struggling to make ends meet. Sabina Aguirre, a barista in Columbus, Ohio, said she made less than $16 an hour. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not sustainable for a day-to-day life,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I didn\u8217\'20\'19t have help with my rent, I would be homeless right now. That\u8217\'20\'19s the reality of my situation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s also the reality of the situation for a majority of the people I work with. Most \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers that I talk to on a day-to-day basis are one or two paychecks away from homelessness, and that shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be the reality of people who are working at a job that claims to support their workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Late last year, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/23/starbucks-workers-strike-nationwide-closures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held}}}\uc2  five days of escalating strikes at stores across the US ahead of Christmas to demand finalizing a first union contract. But the action that workers are currently considering could pave the way for even larger strike actions, hitting more store locations nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll the way back in 2021, workers organized around issues like needing better wages, better take-home pay, better hours, so they can actually make their ends meet, access the benefits they need and have better staffing so the floor can run better,\u8221\'20\'1D said Silvia Baldwin, a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  barista in Philadelphia. \u8220\'20\'1CSince then, the company has also egregiously violated labor law, so workers are organizing around the company to actually making right those violations and making workers whole. Those are still the main issues that workers are fired up about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Baldwin, a bargaining delegate, said negotiating with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in 2024 for a period of months rendered some progress. Tentative agreements were reached covering 80-90% of the contract, she claimed, until they reached economic issues and settling unfair labor practice charges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe company really started to take a turn into bad faith bargaining,\u8221\'20\'1D added Baldwin. \u8220\'20\'1CThe CEO regime changed. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/sep/07/starbucks-brian-niccol-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brian Niccol was brought in}}}\uc2 . And around that same time the presidential election took place, Trump came into office, and the company began to majorly stonewall our bargaining committee and put forward proposals that were just extremely unserious.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Unionized workers at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Care highly motivated, highly engaged, love doing their job and want it to be as good as it should be\u8221\'20\'1D, Baldwin said, and they can tell \u8220\'20\'1Cthe company exactly what it\u8217\'20\'19s going to take to turn things around. If \uc2 Brian Niccol\uc2  wants to actually fix this company, you should listen to our union.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It would take less than one average day\u8217\'20\'19s sales to finalize the contract, the union has claimed. Niccol, the CEO, had a total compensation over the past year of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/sep/07/starbucks-brian-niccol-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $97.8m}}}\uc2 , whereas the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/sep/07/starbucks-brian-niccol-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 median annual salary}}}\uc2  for a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  employee in 2024 was $14,674.\par \par \uc2 The company has been under pressure for months, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sbworkersunited.org/starbucks-union-baristas-secure-effects-bargaining-wins-following-companys-store-closure-announcement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  earlier this year a slate of store closures around the US, including 59 union stores, as part of{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/25/starbucks-store-closures-lay-offs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  cost-cutting restructuring}}}\uc2  due to lagging sales.\par \par \uc2 If authorized, the strike will be closely watched throughout the US labor movement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s clear that bargaining has stalled. Thousands of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers have voted to unionize, and they aren\u8217\'20\'19t yet protected by a binding contract,\u8221\'20\'1D Rebecca Givan, a labor law professor at \uc2 Rutgers University\uc2 , said. \u8220\'20\'1CA strong showing in their strike-authorization vote will tell \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  management that these workers are serious about taking action if a contract isn\u8217\'20\'19t agreed soon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemonstrating that this national, dispersed campaign can lead to first contracts will send a message to workers nationwide that they can organize and win material gains, backed up with an enforceable contract.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , Jaci Anderson, claimed the firm\u8217\'20\'19s transformation campaign, known as Back to \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , was working.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWorkers United, which represents around 4% of our partners, chose to walk away from the bargaining table. If they\u8217\'20\'19re ready to come back, we\u8217\'20\'19re ready to talk. Any agreement needs to reflect the reality that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  already offers the best job in retail,\u8221\'20\'1D Anderson wrote in an email. \u8220\'20\'1CHourly partners {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.starbucks.com/press/2025/were-ready-to-talk-if-workers-united-is/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earn}}}\uc2  more than $30 an hour on average in pay and benefits and we\u8217\'20\'19re investing over $500m to put more partners in stores during busy times.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe facts show people like working at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 . Partner engagement is up, turnover is nearly half the industry average and we get more than 1m job applications a year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251031elav002e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
