\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 CDC employees on chaos of being fired, rehired and fired again: \u8216\'20\'18stuck in limbo\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Melody Schreiber \par \uc2 1,201 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2025\par 12:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Americans\u8217\'20\'19 health in jeopardy as agency plunged into tumult and inefficiency even after court ruled firings illegal\par \par \uc2 As layoff notices swept through the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)\uc2  on 10 October, Aryn Melton Backus thought she would be safe this time.\par \par \uc2 Then she received the email: she was part of a major reduction in force (RIF) during the \uc2 US government\uc2  shutdown. It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the first time she\u8217\'20\'19d been fired from the CDC by email, nor the second.\par \par \uc2 Backus has been terminated and then reinstated three times this year.\par \par \uc2 Her experience demonstrates the inefficiencies and tumult at US health agencies as leaders continue cutting into the workforce and ending programs vital for Americans\u8217\'20\'19 health.\par \par \uc2 The latest round of shutdown RIFs is illegal, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/publication/federal-employee-unions-file-expanded-lawsuit-challenging-trump-administrations-illegal-shutdown-firings/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees (AFGE)\uc2 , which is among the unions representing federal workers that are suing the government to stop the layoffs. A quarter of the CDC has now been cut by multiple rounds of layoffs.\par \par \uc2 Some employees who had to work without pay through the shutdown received RIF notices; others who were furloughed learned they would never return to their jobs. Employees who were supposed to be protected from RIFs by an ongoing lawsuit received them anyway. The human resources department at CDC was brought back from unpaid furlough in order to process about 1,300 layoffs \u8211\'20\'13 and then their own, as the entire HR department was eliminated.\par \par \uc2 Some of the gutted departments are required by law to continue their work, despite having no employees. The ethics office and the institutional review board (\uc2 IRB\uc2 ) were also ended, which means the CDC will no longer have oversight on ethical violations and research protocols.\par \par \uc2 The entire library staff at the CDC, an integral part of research and recommendations, was terminated. The Washington office, which developed policy briefings and provided information to Congress members, was eliminated as well.\par \par \uc2 The National Center for Chronic Disease Prevention and Health Promotion, the national health and nutrition examination survey, and the staff focused on suicide prevention also suffered layoffs.\par \par \uc2 The multiple cuts across the agency mean the CDC is not able to carry out much of its work, even as some employees remain, said Karen Remley, who previously ran the National Center on Birth Defects and Developmental Disabilities and was a state health official in Virginia.\par \par \uc2 In April, for instance, the entire team behind the Pregnancy Risk Assessment Monitoring System (Prams) was cut, which means a critical tool for understanding maternal and child health is now missing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t take out Prams and keep the registry and have all that work happen,\u8221\'20\'1D Remley said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis artificial separating and splitting really means the work on the local level stops.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, CDC employees have endured attacks and harassment.\par \par \uc2 On 8 August, a gunman fired 500 rounds of ammunition at the CDC headquarters, killing David Rose, an officer, and traumatizing agency employees and their families.\par \par \uc2 Health agency employees have been doxed, with their identities and personal information revealed. Matthew Buckham, Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s acting chief of staff, was co-founder of the group that maintains a \u8220\'20\'1CDEI Watch List\u8221\'20\'1D targeting \uc2 HHS\uc2  employees. The agency has also been roiled by high-profile {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/sep/17/rfk-jr-senate-hearing-cdc-susan-monarez"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 departures}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the highest level of leadership in the CDC, there are no public health or medical professionals left to help guide CDC recommendations,\u8221\'20\'1D said Abigail Tighe, a former CDC employee and founding member of the National Public Health Coalition, which held a recent press conference where Backus and other former CDC employees spoke.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBillions in contracts and direct funding to state and local public health agencies has been canceled or clawed back, and the American people are cued up to suffer. It is hard to succinctly put into words what the decimation of the CDC means for everyday Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The first round of layoffs at CDC came on Valentine\u8217\'20\'19s day. Probationary employees \u8211\'20\'13 who were in the first year or two of their jobs, either because they had been recently hired or had moved to new positions \u8211\'20\'13 along with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/20/trump-fired-health-employees"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 established senior employees}}}\uc2  received notices.\par \par \uc2 A judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.cand.444883/gov.uscourts.cand.444883.261.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  in September that the probationary terminations went too far and some of the employees were reinstated and placed on administrative leave.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, RIF notices went out on 1 April, eliminating entire offices such as the office on smoking and health, where Backus worked. She didn\u8217\'20\'19t even receive the notice at first because her access to the CDC network, including email, had been cut off.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit specifically prevents employees like Backus from being reorganized into new offices or terminated from the agency, she said. That\u8217\'20\'19s why she thought she would be safe this time \u8211\'20\'13 but she still received a third layoff notice. That notice was rescinded after less than 24 hours. About 700 employees were reinstated, while 600 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/14/cdc-job-cuts-partial-reversal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remain terminated}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI still remain on administrative leave, unable to do my job,\u8221\'20\'1D Backus said. \u8220\'20\'1CMy situation just highlights the chaos and confusion that federal employees have experienced over the past year. I\u8217\'20\'19m stuck in limbo, following court cases, gathering information, and trying to figure out what my next steps should be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Charlotte Kent, former editor-in-chief of the Morbidity and Mortality Weekly Report (MMWR), said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have so many people who, if they\u8217\'20\'19ve been [un-RIFed], have been on administrative leave. We have the inefficiency of so many government resources, our taxpayer dollars, going to fight the illegal activities that have been done by the administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The MMWR was among the departments completely gutted and then reinstated \u8211\'20\'13 which was particularly surprising, because the highly regarded scientific journal was specifically included in the president\u8217\'20\'19s budget request for the first time this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo have it cut at this point is just shocking,\u8221\'20\'1D Kent said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like being in a strange game where there\u8217\'20\'19s no rules,\u8221\'20\'1D said one former CDC employee who was RIFed on 10 October and spoke anonymously to avoid reprisal from the Trump administration. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s honestly like Squid Games \u8211\'20\'13 we don\u8217\'20\'19t know what\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen next.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 John Brooks, who retired last year from the CDC after 26 years and served as the chief medical officer for several emergency responses, said the RIFs demonstrated a \u8220\'20\'1Cstunning level of incompetency\u8221\'20\'1D. Firing the CDC Washington staff means \u8220\'20\'1CCongress no longer has a means of direct access to the agency it funds when it needs information or briefings\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/government-shutdown-live-updates-as-military-poised-to-miss-first-paychecks-next-week/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  says about 700 of the terminations were a coding error.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is clear to us that this was not a coding error,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tighe. \u8220\'20\'1CThis RIF was carried out just as all the other ones have been, where they fire as many people as they think they can get away with, there\u8217\'20\'19s public outcry, there\u8217\'20\'19s outcry from congressional members and then they bring back the things that they think people cannot get over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She called the firings \u8220\'20\'1Can intentional attack on the American people and the public\u8217\'20\'19s health\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur country is on an uncertain and frankly frightening path,\u8221\'20\'1D Tighe said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe would love to see Congress step in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251031elav0030f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
