\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: US to limit refugee numbers to 7,500 with priority for white South Africans\b0\par\par\uc2 Jem Bartholomew \par \uc2 1,028 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2025\par 11:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US refugee groups say move \u8216\'20\'18lowers our moral standing.\u8217\'20\'19 Plus, unionized \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers to vote on strikes over pay and conditionsDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration is going to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/30/trump-refugee-restrictions-white-south-africans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrict the number of refugees}}}\uc2  it admits into the US next year to the token level of just 7,500 \u8211\'20\'13 and those spots will mostly be filled by white South Africans.\par \par \uc2 The low number represents a dramatic decrease from last year\u8217\'20\'19s ceiling, set under the Biden administration, of 125,000 people fleeing war and persecution.\par \par \uc2 The announcement swiftly drew criticism from a large range of refugee organizations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince the US Refugee Program was created in 1980, it has admitted over 2 million people fleeing ethnic cleansing and other horrors. Now it will be used as a pathway for white immigration,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Aaron Reichlin-Melnick\uc2 , senior fellow at the \uc2 American Immigration Council\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * What reason has been given for prioritizing white South Africans? The Trump administration has repeatedly claimed that the South African government is implementing anti-white policies through a new land expropriation law. The South African government has called the claims false.\par \par \uc2 California officials investigate after second shooting by ICE agents in a week\par \par \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE)\uc2  agents were involved in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/30/ice-agents-southern-california-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a shooting in southern California on Thursday}}}\uc2 , prompting a federal investigation.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  said in a statement that ICE officers were conducting a vehicle stop in Ontario when another driver, who was not the target, approached. Officers ordered the driver to leave the area, according to the statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the driver began to pull away, the car stopped and attempted to run officers over by reversing directly at them without stopping,\u8221\'20\'1D Tricia McLaughlin, the DHS\u8217\'20\'19s assistant press secretary, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 * What was the other shooting by ICE agents in LA recently? Last week, federal agents shot an LA man who livestreams immigration enforcement operations on social media. Officials said at the time that Carlitos Ricardo Parias, a TikTok creator with a large following, had attempted to ram federal agents\u8217\'20\'19 vehicles after agents surrounded him and boxed in his car.\par \par \uc2 Hurricane Melissa death toll nears 50 as Jamaica relief efforts intensify and storm heads north\par \par \uc2 The death toll from Hurricane Melissa has reached 49 as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/oct/30/hurricane-melissa-bermuda-leaving-devastation-jamaica"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the storm continues to tear through the Caribbean}}}\uc2 , heading past Bermuda, and workers in Jamaica ramped up efforts to clear roads and reach people in isolated and cut-off areas.\par \par \uc2 Tropical storm conditions were occurring on Bermuda late on Thursday, as the category 2 storm moved past the western side of the territory, packing maximum sustained winds of 100mph (155km/h). The storm is moving in a north-easterly direction at a speed of 38mph (61km/h).\par \par \uc2 * What do we know about the\par \par \uc2 number of deaths so far? In Haiti the death toll has risen to 30, with another 20 missing, the civil defence agency said on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a sad moment for the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Haiti\u8217\'20\'19s head of the transitional presidential council, Laurent Saint-Cyr. In Jamaica the death toll rose to 19, and search and rescue efforts were continuing, said the information minister, Dana Morris Dixon.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 * New York\u8217\'20\'19s governor,\par \par \uc2 Kathy Hochul\par \par \uc2 , has declared a state of emergency to raise $65m to help food pantries, with federal funding for the national food stamps program {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/oct/30/donald-trump-xi-jinping-meeting-live-updates?page=with%3Ablock-690389558f084e5a6d1989cc#block-690389558f084e5a6d1989cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to expire}}}\uc2  on Saturday due to the government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 * The UK\u8217\'20\'19s Prince Andrew will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2025/oct/30/prince-andrew-leave-royal-lodge-windsor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripped}}}\uc2  of his royal titles, Buckingham Palace has announced, amid ongoing allegations of his friendship with child sexual abuse offender \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Russian commanders are executing or deliberately sending to their deaths soldiers who refuse to fight in Ukraine,\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/oct/30/russian-army-chiefs-torturing-and-executing-soldiers-who-refuse-to-fight-in-ukraine-report-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  a new investigation by the independent outlet Verstka.\par \par \uc2 * In the Netherlands,\par \par \uc2 Geert Wilders\par \par \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 far-right Freedom party is almost certain to be excluded from the next Dutch government, after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/oct/30/geert-wilders-faces-shutout-centrists-dutch-election-netherlands"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 general election}}}\uc2  in which his support slumped while liberal-progressives {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/oct/30/rob-jetten-anti-wilders-yes-we-can-candidate-next-dutch-pm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made gains}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: $14,674 median salary for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  employee is 0.015% of CEO\u8217\'20\'19s $97.8m pay\par \par \uc2 Unionized Starbucks workers are voting over strikes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/oct/31/starbucks-workers-strike-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amid anger over pay and conditions}}}\uc2  and allegations the company breached labor laws. Figures show that the median annual salary for a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  employee in 2024 was $14,674 \u8211\'20\'13 representing 0.015% of the $97.8m total compensation received by its chief executive, \uc2 Brian Niccol\uc2 , over the past year.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: The least frightening films ever \u8211\'20\'13 ranked!\par \par \uc2 Halloween season is packed with scary movie lists. But what about the least frightening films ever? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2025/oct/30/the-least-frightening-films-ever-ranked"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stuart Heritage ranks the serene and the relaxing}}}\uc2 , from My Dinner with Andre (1981) to Before Sunset (2004) to David Lynch\u8217\'20\'19s The Straight Story (1999), in which an old man drives a lawnmower across middle America to visit his dying brother.\par \par \uc2 Climate check:\par \par \uc2 ex-\uc2 EPA\uc2  head urges resistance to Trump attacks on climate action \u8211\'20\'13 \u8216\'20\'18We won\u8217\'20\'19t become numb\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Gina McCarthy, the former \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  head who now co-chairs America Is All In, which is sending more than 100 subnational leaders to the \uc2 UN\uc2  climate summit in Brazil next month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/oct/30/resist-trump-attacks-climate-action"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2  yesterday that US cities and states \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not allow our country to become numb or debilitated by those who are standing in the way of progress\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: \u8216\'20\'18I dressed up as a superhero for Halloween \u8211\'20\'13 and then saved a man\u8217\'20\'19s life\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 On Halloween night in 2020, Christopher Lee Taylor dressed up as the superhero Homelander, with a stars and stripes cape. Driving to a house party, \u8220\'20\'1CI saw flames shooting out of another house,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2025/oct/31/experience-i-dressed-up-as-a-superhero-for-halloween-and-then-saved-a-mans-life"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he says}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe kids were both staring from the back seat. \u8216\'20\'18Don\u8217\'20\'19t worry,\u8217\'20\'19 I said, \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19ll be right back\u8217\'20\'19, and took off towards the burning house.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251031elav002gz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\pic