\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Radio Free Asia\uc2  suspends news operations amid cuts and \uc2 US government\uc2  shutdown\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 716 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2025\par 09:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 RFA\uc2  will begin closing overseas bureaus, as well as laying off and paying severance to staff members, with the hope that it could return in the future\par \par \uc2 Radio Free Asia (RFA)\uc2  has said it is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rfa.org/english/about/releases/2025/10/29/rfa-suspends-remaining-editorial-operations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspending its news operations}}}\uc2  due to the \uc2 US government\uc2  shutdown and the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2025/mar/18/chinese-state-media-celebrates-trumps-cuts-to-voice-of-america-and-radio-free-asia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cuts to government-funded news services}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 RFA\uc2  has been forced to suspend all remaining news content production \u8211\'20\'13 for the first time in its 29 years of existence,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bay Fang, \uc2 RFA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s president and CEO, in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2025/mar/18/chinese-state-media-celebrates-trumps-cuts-to-voice-of-america-and-radio-free-asia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chinese state media celebrates Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cuts to Voice of America and Radio Free Asia}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn an effort to conserve limited resources on hand and preserve the possibility of restarting operations should consistent funding become available, \uc2 RFA\uc2  is taking further steps to responsibly shrink its already reduced footprint,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 RFA\uc2  was founded nearly three decades ago to report on China and other Asian countries without independent media.\par \par \uc2 It has been operating with a skeleton staff the past few months, primarily producing a few stories online as the administration sought to choke off its funding. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s team has contended that operations like \uc2 RFA\uc2 , \uc2 Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty\uc2  and Voice of America are poorly run and a waste of government resources.\par \par \uc2 Long a thorn in Beijing\u8217\'20\'19s side, \uc2 RFA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s closure comes after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/30/trump-and-xi-meet-in-south-korea-for-crunch-talks-on-trade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US president met Chinese leader Xi Jinpin}}}\uc2 g on a trip to Asia.\par \par \uc2 Radio Free Asia\uc2  will begin shutting down overseas bureaus, laying off and paying severance to staff members, most of whom have been on unpaid leave since last March, Fang said, leaving open the possibility that the organisation could restart operations in the future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHowever drastic these measures may seem, they position \uc2 RFA\uc2 , a private corporation, for a future in which it would be possible to scale up and resume providing accurate, uncensored news for people living in some of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most closed places,\u8221\'20\'1D Fang said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/15/pentagon-press-reporting-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pentagon reporters have now turned in their badges \u8211\'20\'13 but plan to keep reporting}}}\par \par \uc2 With its own journalists and contractors in Asia, \uc2 RFA\uc2  has reported aggressively on stories some governments don\u8217\'20\'19t want to see \u8211\'20\'13 the repression of Uyghurs in China, the aftermath of the 2021 military coup in Myanmar and the plight of defectors in North Korea. The outlet had been growing; visitors to its website increased 20% between 2023 and 2024.\par \par \uc2 Shutting the broadcaster, which produced news in multiple Asian languages, \u8220\'20\'1Cis a gift to dictators like Xi Jinping\u8221\'20\'1D especially \u8220\'20\'1Cat a time when Beijing has worked quite assiduously to control what stories can and can\u8217\'20\'19t get told the country\u8221\'20\'1D, said \uc2 Sophie Richardson\uc2 , co-executive director of the Network of Chinese Human Rights Defenders.\par \par \uc2 Nicholas Burns\uc2 , the US ambassador to China under president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , wrote on X that shuttering \uc2 RFA\uc2  was a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor mistake\u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1Cwill prevent us from telling the truth to the Chinese people and countering Beijing\u8217\'20\'19s propaganda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 RFE/Radio Liberty, similar to \uc2 RFA\uc2  as a private corporation funded by the government, said its own news services were staying up, \u8220\'20\'1Cand we plan to continue reaching our audiences for the foreseeable future\u8221\'20\'1D, the organisation said this week. It operates in eastern Europe, central Asia and the Middle East. The service had launched its own lawsuit against the administration.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/feb/24/donald-trump-usaid-funding-cuts-myanmar-impact-journalists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We have nothing now\u8217\'20\'19: Myanmar\u8217\'20\'19s exiled media face existential crisis after Trump severs aid}}}\par \par \uc2 RFE/Radio Liberty says it received its last federal funding in September. It is operating on reserves, and has taken cost-cutting steps like cutting contracts with freelancers, reducing programming and placing some staff members on partially paid leave.\par \par \uc2 It was not immediately clear why the two organisations are taking different approaches. While having the same governing and funding structure, \uc2 RFA\uc2  and RFE/Radio Liberty are headquartered in North America and Europe respectively, and are governed under different labour laws.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/30/voice-of-america-lay-offs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Voice of America, }}}\uc2 which has concentrated on providing news about the United States to audiences in other countries, had been operating on a very limited basis since its funding was cut off and has essentially stopped due to the government shutdown. Some employees have sued to block the administration\u8217\'20\'19s plans.With Associated Press and Agence France-Presse\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251031elav002be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
