\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 DeSantis urges Florida universities to stop hiring foreign visa workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Marina Dunbar \par \uc2 492 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 October 2025\par 19:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Governor tells universities to end use of H-1B visas, though legal experts say states lack authority over federal program\par \par \uc2 Florida governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , is urging the state\u8217\'20\'19s universities to stop hiring international employees through the H-1B visa program.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis said he wants the Florida board of governors \u8220\'20\'1Cto pull the plug\u8221\'20\'1D on the practice. Nearly 400 foreign nationals are currently employed at Florida\u8217\'20\'19s public universities under the H-1B visa program, reported the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.orlandosentinel.com/2025/10/29/desantis-wants-florida-universities-to-pull-the-plug-on-h-1b-staff-from-foreign-countries/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Orlando Sentinel}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUniversities across the country are importing foreign workers on H-1B visas instead of hiring Americans who are qualified and available to do the job,\u8221\'20\'1D said DeSantis in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flgov.com/eog/news/press/2025/governor-ron-desantis-directs-florida-board-governors-crack-down-h-1b-visa-abuse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not tolerate H-1B abuse in Florida institutions. That\u8217\'20\'19s why I have directed the Florida Board of Governors to end this practice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how such a move could be carried out. States do not have authority to revoke federal visas, and \uc2 US Citizenship and Immigration Services\uc2  regulations prohibit firing employees based on immigration status.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Donald Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/sep/19/trump-h1b-visa-100000-fee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised the H-1B}}}\uc2  visa fee from $215 to $100,000, a decision likely to face legal challenges. He also issued a proclamation alleging \u8220\'20\'1Csystematic abuse\u8221\'20\'1D of the program.\par \par \uc2 The H-1B program permits employers to hire skilled foreign professionals for specialized positions that are difficult to fill with US workers. Across Florida, more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uscis.gov/tools/reports-and-studies/h-1b-employer-data-hub"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7,200 people}}}\uc2  hold H-1B visas.\par \par \uc2 The program has caused friction among Trump supporters. Some, such as \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , argue it\u8217\'20\'19s essential for US innovation, while others, including DeSantis, contend it enables companies to replace Americans with lower-paid foreign labor.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis cited positions filled by workers from China, Argentina and Canada, arguing these roles were taken from qualified Floridians in favor of \u8220\'20\'1Ccheap labor\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 University of Florida\uc2  is one of the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest users of the H-1B program, employing more than 150 staff members under the visa, according to an Orlando Sentinel review of federal data. Other universities also rely heavily on the program, including the \uc2 University of South Florida\uc2  with 72 employees and \uc2 Florida State University\uc2  with 69, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tampabay.com/news/education/2025/10/29/desantis-h1b-visas-universities-doge/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tampa Bay Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Educators note that most H-1B visa holders at these institutions work in departments such as computer science, engineering, physics and chemistry. About 60% of people who earned PhDs in computer science from US universities in 2023 were temporary visa holders, not citizens or permanent residents, reported the Sentinel.\par \par \uc2 Donald Landry, the \uc2 University of Florida\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interim president, said during the news conference that the university will embrace DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s review of H-1B visas. \u8220\'20\'1COccasionally, some bright light might be good enough for the faculty, and then we will try and retain the person into whom we\u8217\'20\'19ve invested so much,\u8221\'20\'1D Landry said, according to the Tampa Bay Times. \u8220\'20\'1CBut that\u8217\'20\'19s the exception that proves the rule.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251029elat005se\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
