\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Leader of top federal worker union calls for end of \uc2 US government\uc2  shutdown\b0\par\par\uc2 Joseph Gedeon in Washington \par \uc2 677 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 October 2025\par 14:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Hundreds of thousands of employees remain unpaid as second-longest US shutdown stretches into fourth week\par \par \uc2 The head of America\u8217\'20\'19s largest federal workers union says it is time to end the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-federal-government-shutdown-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 government shutdown}}}\uc2 , now the second-longest in US history, as hundreds of thousands of employees {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/25/federal-workers-government-shutdown-pay-anxiety"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 miss another round of paychecks}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , who leads the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees\uc2  representing more than 800,000 workers, avoided assigning blame to either party in the Monday morning letter but said lawmakers must stop playing politics and pass a stopgap funding measure to reopen the government, its closure now eclipsing the four-week mark.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBoth political parties have made their point, and still there is no clear end in sight,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelley wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/article/its-past-time-to-end-this-shutdown/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CToday I\u8217\'20\'19m making mine: it\u8217\'20\'19s time to pass a clean continuing resolution and end this shutdown today. No half measures, and no gamesmanship.\u8221\'20\'1D NBC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/afge-largest-federal-workers-union-end-shutdown-rcna239767"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported}}}\uc2  the letter.\par \par \uc2 A \u8220\'20\'1Cclean\u8221\'20\'1D continuing resolution is a temporary spending bill that keeps the government running at current funding levels without attaching other political demands. Republicans say they have offered that in their measure, but Democrats argue the bill shortchanges key services and are using their power in the Senate to push for a deal on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/sep/30/government-shutdown-healthcare-medicaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 health insurance subsidies}}}\uc2  that expire at year\u8217\'20\'19s end.\par \par \uc2 Because of this stalemate, hundreds of thousands of federal and Washington DC government employees are either working without pay or furloughed. The union represents workers across nearly every federal agency, from \uc2 Transportation Security Administration\uc2  (TSA) officers and army nurses to food safety inspectors and veterans affairs staff, many of whom are now lined up at food banks after missing their second paycheck, Kelley said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are patriotic Americans \u8211\'20\'13 parents, caregivers, and veterans \u8211\'20\'13 forced to work without pay while struggling to cover rent, groceries, gas and medicine because of political disagreements in Washington,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelley said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is unacceptable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the crisis extends beyond federal workers: roughly 42 million Americans who receive food assistance through the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/26/food-benefits-federal-shutdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 face losing their benefits}}}\uc2  as soon as 1 November if the shutdown continues, after the \uc2 US agriculture department\uc2  warned states it would run out of money to pay for the program.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats have blocked a Republican-backed continuing resolution 12 times, demanding commitments on extending Affordable Care Act health subsidies. Three Democrats and one independent who caucus with the party have broken ranks to support the measure, but it remains short of the 60 needed to advance. The Republican senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/27/rand-paul-trump-military-airstrikes-venezuela"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rand Paul}}}\uc2  is the sole Republican to defect on the measure.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 AFGE\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/publication/trumpvance-administrations-use-of-employees-emails-to-send-partisan-political-messages-challenged-by-largest-federal-worker-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/15/federal-worker-firings-blocked-judge-government-shutdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suing}}}\uc2  the Trump administration over mass layoffs organized during the shutdown and over partisan emails sent from government accounts without employees\u8217\'20\'19 knowledge.\par \par \uc2 Kelley called for three immediate steps: reopening the government under a continuing resolution, ensuring full back pay for all affected workers, and addressing policy disputes through normal legislative debate rather than shutdown tactics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the folks who serve this country are standing in line for food banks after missing a second paycheck because of this shutdown, they aren\u8217\'20\'19t looking for partisan spin,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re looking for the wages they earned. The fact that they\u8217\'20\'19re being cheated out of it is a national disgrace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The shutdown reaches the one-month mark this week, with no negotiations scheduled between the parties.\par \par \uc2 The House minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://democraticleader.house.gov/media/press-releases/leader-jeffries-cnn-we-are-demanding-our-republican-colleagues-sit-back-down"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN on Sunday}}}\uc2  that he and the Senate minority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , requested a meeting with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  to discuss the shutdown before he went out of the country but had been rebuffed. The president has said he will only meet with Democrats after they vote to reopen the government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA strong America requires a functioning government \u8211\'20\'13 one that pays its bills, honors its commitments, and treats its workforce with respect by paying them on time,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelley wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CThe government belongs to all of us. Let\u8217\'20\'19s open it back up and keep America moving forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251027elar003ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
