\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US Boeing workers continue midwest strike after rejecting latest contract offer\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 643 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 October 2025\par 11:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Nearly three-month strike includes 3,200 machinists at plants where military aircraft and weapons are developed\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/boeing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boeing}}}\uc2  workers at three midwest plants where military aircraft and weapons are developed voted on Sunday to reject the company\u8217\'20\'19s latest contract offer and to continue a strike that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/03/boeing-st-louis-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 started almost three months ago}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The strike by about 3,200 machinists at the plants in Mascoutah, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/illinois"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Illinois}}}\uc2 , and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/missouri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri}}}\uc2  cities of St Louis and St Charles is smaller in scale than a walkout last year by 33,000 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers who assemble commercial jetliners but threatens to complicate the aerospace company\u8217\'20\'19s progress in regaining its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/jan/28/boeing-2024-annual-loss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 financial footing}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Boeing\uc2  claimed they listened to their employees \u8211\'20\'13 the result of today\u8217\'20\'19s vote proves they have not,\u8221\'20\'1D Brian Bryant, the president of the \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers\uc2 , said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s corporate executives continue to insult the very people who build the world\u8217\'20\'19s most advanced military aircraft \u8211\'20\'13 the same planes and military systems that keep our servicemembers and nation safe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  said it was disappointed by the result and noted the vote had been a close one. The company said in a statement that it was increasingly hearing from workers \u8220\'20\'1Cwho want to cross the picket line\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cunderstand the value of our offer\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The five-year offer was largely the same as offers previously rejected by union members. The company reduced the ratification bonus but added $3,000 in \uc2 Boeing\uc2  shares that vest over three years and a $1,000 retention bonus in four years. It also improved wage growth for workers at the top of the pay scale in the fourth year of the contract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe union\u8217\'20\'19s statement is misleading since the vote failed by the slimmest of margins, 51% to 49%,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s statement read. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are turning our focus to executing the next phase of our contingency plan in support of our customers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The machinists\u8217\'20\'19 union acknowledged the vote was close but said in a message to members that \u8220\'20\'1Cvery few\u8221\'20\'1D workers had crossed the picket line.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur solidarity remains strong, and the company\u8217\'20\'19s claim otherwise is wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D the union said.\par \par \uc2 Union leaders have pressed the planemaker for higher retirement plan contributions and a ratification bonus closer to the $12,000 that \uc2 Boeing\uc2  gave to union members {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/13/boeing-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on strike}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/05/boeing-workers-end-strike-walkout-seattle-portland-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last year}}}\uc2  in the company\u8217\'20\'19s commercial airplane division in the Pacific north-west. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  has argued that workers\u8217\'20\'19 demands exceed the cost of living in the midwest.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s vote, the union told its members that it did not recommend approval of the company\u8217\'20\'19s latest offer, which it said \u8220\'20\'1Chad no meaningful improvements\u8221\'20\'1D to retirement benefits and wage increases for workers with more seniority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s well past time for \uc2 Boeing\uc2  to stop cheaping out on the workers who make its success possible and bargain a fair deal that respects their skill and sacrifice,\u8221\'20\'1D Bryant said.\par \par \uc2 Negotiations escalated over the summer in the days leading up to the strike, with the workers rejecting an earlier proposed agreement that included a 20% wage hike over the life of the five-year contract.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  quickly countered with a modified agreement that did not boost the proposed pay raises but did remove a scheduling provision affecting the workers\u8217\'20\'19 ability to earn overtime pay. Workers rejected that offer too and went on strike the next morning. They also voted against revised terms in September.\par \par \uc2 The company has said that it was prepared for a strike, with a contingency plan in place \u8220\'20\'1Cto ensure our non-striking workforce can continue supporting our customers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Boeing Defense, Space & Security\uc2  business accounts for more than one-third of the company\u8217\'20\'19s revenue. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is set to report its third-quarter earnings on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251027elar002bl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
