\par\par \uc2 Stage\par \b \uc2 Broadway musicians union reaches tentative deal to avoid strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Anna Betts \par \uc2 372 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 October 2025\par 14:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Strike was set to begin later on Thursday if union did not reach agreement on new contract with Broadway League\par \par \uc2 The union representing Broadway musicians reached a tentative deal on a new contract early on Thursday morning, avoiding a potential strike that had been set to begin later that day and would have threatened many top shows in New York.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.local802afm.org/2025/10/broadway-musicians-announce-tentative-agreement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 , the American Federation of Musicians Local 802 said it had reached the tentative agreement with the Broadway League \u8211\'20\'13 the trade association representing theater owners, producers and operators \u8211\'20\'13 around 4.30am on Thursday, preventing a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrike scheduled to begin later today\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis three year agreement provides meaningful wage and health benefit increases that will preserve crucial access to healthcare for our musicians while maintaining the strong contract protections that empower musicians to build a steady career on Broadway,\u8221\'20\'1D said the union\u8217\'20\'19s president, Bob Suttmann.\par \par \uc2 Details of the tentative agreement are not yet known. \uc2 The Broadway League\uc2  did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The union had been preparing to strike if a deal was not{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Local_802_AFM/status/1980667025212256567"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reached by }}}\uc2 Thursday. Last week, Local 802 members {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.local802afm.org/2025/10/broadway-bargaining-update-updated-oct-1-2025/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted overwhelmingly }}}\uc2 to authorize a strike if negotiations stalled, and earlier this week, the union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Local_802_AFM/status/1980667025212256567/photo/2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned }}}\uc2 that \u8220\'20\'1Cif we do not have a new contract by Thursday morning, we are prepared to strike immediately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Local 802 has been negotiating the new contract with the Broadway League since 31 August, when the previous musicians\u8217\'20\'19 contract expired, according to the union.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnewyork.com/broadway/broadway-musicians-strike-thursday/6407201/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2  reported that the strike would have affected every Broadway production that uses musicians \u8211\'20\'13 except Ragtime, which operates under a different contract with Lincoln Center. AFM Local 802 describes itself as the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest local union of professional musicians in the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s announcement comes less than a week after the \uc2 Actors Equity Association\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the union which represents more than 51,000 professional actors and stage managers working in live theatre \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://actorsequity.org/news/PR/2025/10/18/actors-equity-and-broadway-league-reach-tentative-agreement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached its own tentative agreement}}}\uc2  with the Broadway League.\par \par \uc2 Al Vincent Jr, Actors\u8217\'20\'19 Equity\u8217\'20\'19s executive director, said that the deal \u8220\'20\'1Csaves the Equity-League Health Fund while also making strides in our other priorities including scheduling and physical therapy access\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251023elan004bl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
