\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Key US nuclear agency to send 80% of workforce home as shutdown drags on\b0\par\par\uc2 Joseph Gedeon in Washington \par \uc2 516 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 October 2025\par 08:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 About 1,400 staff at \uc2 NNSA\uc2 , which manages America\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear weapons stockpile, to be furloughed on Monday\par \par \uc2 The agency that maintains the US nuclear arsenal will be sending home 80% of its workforce as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-federal-government-shutdown-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 government shutdown}}}\uc2  drags through its 17th day and into the weekend, now the longest full funding lapse in US history.\par \par \uc2 House armed services committee chair Mike Rogers said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/atrupar/status/1979192882696171884"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Friday press conference }}}\uc2 that the \uc2 National Nuclear Security Administration\uc2  has now exhausted its carryover reserves.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were just informed last night that the \uc2 National Nuclear Security Administration\uc2 , the group that manages our nuclear stockpile, that the carryover funding they\u8217\'20\'19ve been using is about to run out,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rogers, a Republican from Alabama. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are not employees that you want to go home. They\u8217\'20\'19re managing and handling a very important strategic asset for us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NNSA\uc2 , which operates as part of the department of energy, does not directly control operational nuclear weapons \u8211\'20\'13 a Pentagon responsibility \u8211\'20\'13 but plays a strategic role in keeping warheads secure and functional without conducting explosive tests. The agency also runs non-proliferation programs aimed at preventing nuclear materials from reaching hostile nations or terrorist organizations.\par \par \uc2 Around 1,400 \uc2 NNSA\uc2  employees will be furloughed without pay starting on Monday, leaving only 375 staff members designated as essential to continue working, according to an agency notice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2025/10/17/top-nuclear-weapons-agency-to-furlough-most-staff-amid-shutdown-00613640"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained by Politico}}}\uc2 . A department of energy spokesperson confirmed the approximate workforce numbers.\par \par \uc2 The spokesperson also said that \uc2 NNSA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office of secure transportation, which is responsible for transporting government-owned nuclear material across the country, is funded through 27 October, and added that Chris Wright, the energy secretary, will be at the \uc2 NNSA\uc2  site in Las Vegas on Monday to \u8220\'20\'1Cfurther discuss the impacts of the shutdown on America\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear deterrent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Under the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.energy.gov/sites/default/files/2025-09/DOE%20Lapse%20Plan%20September%202025.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agency\u8217\'20\'19s 2025 contingency protocols}}}\uc2  in the event of a shutdown, the skeleton crew on duty will focus exclusively on hyperspecific safety operations: monitoring nuclear materials, maintaining unique equipment, ensuring reactor safety for navy vessels, and continuing international nonproliferation work it deems essential for security.\par \par \uc2 But most scientific research, stockpile maintenance, and global security programs will be suspended, potentially creating delays in sensitive national defense projects that need rigid and consistent oversight.\par \par \uc2 The current impasse has now become the longest complete government-wide shutdown in US history, surpassing a 16-day funding lapse in 2013. Previous lengthier shutdowns affected only portions of the federal government.\par \par \uc2 Speaker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mike-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Johnson}}}\uc2  blamed Senate Democrats for the crisis, saying earlier this week the country is \u8220\'20\'1Cbarreling toward one of the longest shutdowns in American history, unless Democrats drop their demands\u8221\'20\'1D. Republican leaders are also now worried about potential {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/08/government-shutdown-airports-delays"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 airport disruptions}}}\uc2  during the upcoming Thanksgiving travel period if the stalemate continues.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of thousands of federal employees, including congressional and agency staffers, remain either {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/15/trump-federal-workers-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 furloughed}}}\uc2  or working {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/17/trump-government-shutdown-ice-worker-pay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 without pay}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The subheading of this article was amended on 19 October 2025. The \uc2 National Nuclear Security Administration\uc2  is the \uc2 NNSA\uc2  not the NNAS.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251017elah0060p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
