\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge temporarily blocks firings by Trump administration during shutdown\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 457 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 October 2025\par 19:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Judge says White House office of management and budget took advantage of government shutdown in firing workers\par \par \uc2 A federal court has granted a temporary injunction blocking the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s firings of federal employees during the government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 The ruling by Judge Susan Illston of the US district court\u8217\'20\'19s northern district of California came in response to a lawsuit filed by labor unions representing federal workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am inclined to grant the plaintiff\u8217\'20\'19s motion,\u8221\'20\'1D said Illston during a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.cand.uscourts.gov/CEO/cfd.aspx?7133"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court hearing}}}\uc2  on the injunction request. \u8220\'20\'1CThe evidence suggests that the office of management and budget, OMB, and the office of personnel management, OPM, have taken advantage of the lapse in government spending, in government functioning to assume that all bets are off, that the laws don\u8217\'20\'19t apply to them any more, and that they can impose the structures that they like on the government situation that they don\u8217\'20\'19t like, and I find, I believe, that the plaintiffs will demonstrate, ultimately, that what\u8217\'20\'19s being done here is both illegal and is in excess of authority and is arbitrary and capricious.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Justice department attorney Elizabeth Hedges said she was not prepared to discuss the merits of the case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs of now, the [temporary restraining order] is in effect,\u8221\'20\'1D Illston said.\par \par \uc2 The ruling comes as \uc2 Russ Vought\uc2 , the White House OMB director, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/albamonica/status/1978518149122138582"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on The Charlie Kirk Show that more cuts were coming, claiming the firings could be \u8220\'20\'1Cnorth of 10,000\u8221\'20\'1D workers.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Trump administration announced \u8220\'20\'1Creductions in force\u8221\'20\'1D across seven federal agencies, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/15/trump-federal-workers-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 4,100 workers}}}\uc2  affected, citing the shutdown as justification for the firings.\par \par \uc2 Unions representing federal employees \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees (AFGE)\uc2  and the \uc2 American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees\uc2  (\uc2 AFSCME\uc2 ) \u8211\'20\'13 filed a lawsuit on 30 September, before the shutdown, in response to threats from the Trump administration that it would conduct reductions in force.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/publication/trump-administrations-plan-for-mass-firing-of-federal-workers-during-government-shutdown-violates-law-unions-say/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit }}}\uc2 alleges that the OMB, through Vought, violated the law by making firing threats and instructing federal employees to carry out work related to the firings during the shutdown.\par \par \uc2 The unions filed for an injunction to block the firings. No prior government shutdown has resulted in mass layoffs of federal workers before.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn [the] \uc2 AFGE\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 93 years of existence under several presidential administrations \u8211\'20\'13 including during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term \u8211\'20\'13 no president has ever decided to fire thousands of furloughed workers during a government shutdown,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , president of the \uc2 AFGE\uc2 , in a statement on the firings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 AFGE\uc2  is currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/publication/trump-administrations-plan-for-mass-firing-of-federal-workers-during-government-shutdown-violates-law-unions-say/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenging}}}\uc2  President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s illegal, unprecedented abuse of power and we will not stop fighting until every reduction-in-force notice is rescinded.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251015elaf0060q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
