\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Panic as US federal workers scramble to find out if they\u8217\'20\'19ve been fired: \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t have email access\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 978 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 October 2025\par 15:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Education department staff say they can\u8217\'20\'19t access work emails amid the shutdown to check for layoff notices\par \par \uc2 Federal workers are scrambling to figure out if they still have a job after the Trump administration launched a fresh wave of layoffs amid a federal government shutdown, prompting widespread confusion and panic.\par \par \uc2 A hearing is scheduled to take place on Wednesday after labor unions sued to block the latest firings, setting the stage for another legal battle over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to drastically cut back the federal workforce.\par \par \uc2 About 4,200 federal employees across seven agencies were laid off on Friday, the administration has said, although 700 firings at the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)\uc2  were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/14/cdc-job-cuts-partial-reversal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swiftly reversed}}}\uc2  over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 It remains unclear if Trump, who told reporters that \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot\u8221\'20\'1D of government workers would be fired, plans to go further. The federal workforce has already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/sep/28/us-mass-resignation-federal-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shed hundreds of thousands of staff}}}\uc2  on his watch this year.\par \par \uc2 As unions seek to establish the extent of the latest layoffs, workers at the Department of Education said that they do not have access to their work email accounts during the shutdown \u8211\'20\'13 so cannot check to see if they have received \u8220\'20\'1Creduction in force\u8221\'20\'1D (RIF) notices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy co-worker in the office of special education programs was RIF\u8217\'20\'19ed. She had access to her government email and found out,\u8221\'20\'1D an employee at the education department, who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation, said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe rest of us are in a panic. I think I may have been fired and I don\u8217\'20\'19t have a way to find out. They sent the RIF notices to our official government emails which we don\u8217\'20\'19t have access to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another education department employee said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have email access due to the shutdown. Some have received permission to check. I have not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They later were able to access their email, where they received an update to a reduction in force from earlier in the year that was halted by court challenges, with a revised separation date of 3 November.\par \par \uc2 The first employee criticized the timing of the firings, which were conducted the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dignitymemorial.com/obituaries/washington-dc/gregory-corr-12538119"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 day before the funeral}}}\uc2  of the office\u8217\'20\'19s longtime division director, Greg Corr, who had recently retired after 38 years there. The majority of employees in the special education and rehabilitative services department, which houses the office of special education programs, were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/13/special-education-department-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  to have been fired as part of the reduction in force.\par \par \uc2 A copy of a reduction in force notice at the education department seen by the Guardian claimed that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe continued lapse in funding\u8221\'20\'1D made it \u8220\'20\'1Cnecessary\u8221\'20\'1D to implement the layoffs and cited a separation date of 9 December. No previous government shutdowns have resulted in a reduction in force.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is what they do to folks with a combined 1,000 years of experience working to improve the lives of children with disabilities on the day before our director\u8217\'20\'19s funeral,\u8221\'20\'1D the first employee said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat kind of humanity is this?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump is wrong to suggest the agencies targeted by these layoffs are \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrat-orientated\u8221\'20\'1D, they argued, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a \u8216\'20\'18Democrat\u8217\'20\'19 program. This is special education.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The administration presented a reduction in force at the education department in March, but state attorneys general and unions sued to block the effort to dismantle it. A preliminary injunction to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://democracyforward.org/updates/educators-professors-school-districts-unions-win-historic-effort-to-block-trump-administration-attempt-to-dismantle-department-of-education/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 block those firings}}}\uc2  was granted by a federal court in May. The supreme court allowed the firings to proceed in a brief, unsigned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scotusblog.com/2025/07/supreme-court-clears-the-way-for-trump-administration-to-massively-reduce-the-size-of-the-department-of-education/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 order }}}\uc2 issued in July that provided no explanation, while the legal challenge to the closure of the department is ongoing in court.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wbaltv.com/article/education-department-layoffs-impact-schools/69019401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 4,100 employees}}}\uc2  worked at the education department when Trump took office. Between a previous reduction in force and these latest firings, staffing at the agency is now under 2,000.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis administration is using the same playbook that led to the termination of 1,500 staff in March to further illegally dismantle the Department of Education without any regard for the impacts on the American public, and we are tired of it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rachel Gittleman, president of \uc2 AFGE\uc2  local 252, a union representing education department workers.\par \par \uc2 Gittleman, an employee at the department herself, received a reduction in force notice in March. \u8220\'20\'1CThese RIFs will double down on the harm to K-12 students, students with disabilities, first generation college students, low-income students, teachers and local education boards, which are already feeling the impacts of a hamstrung Department from the March RIF,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The notices have increased anxiety and fear of other federal employees at agencies that have not been slated for cuts during the shutdown, where many workers are already either furloughed or working without pay.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur staffing levels are pretty low, so it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to comprehend how much more cuts are going to be made and who,\u8221\'20\'1D Imelda Avila-Thomas, president of \uc2 AFGE\uc2  local 2139, and a Department of Labor employee, said. Approximately 75% of staff at the department have been furloughed, but the agency has not enacted a reduction in force yet. \u8220\'20\'1CThat chaos is so debilitating on everybody\u8217\'20\'19s mental health, physical health and just in general it\u8217\'20\'19s demoralizing,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CMorale is already low, and then we have this happening. I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to say anybody is safe, I think we all understand that\u8217\'20\'19s not a thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House deferred comment to the office of management and budget, which did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 The Department of Education responded with an out of office message stating \u8220\'20\'1Cdue to the lapse in appropriations, we are currently in furlough status. We will respond to emails once government functions resume.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251015elaf002mn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
