\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Instability and whiplash\u8217\'20\'19 as CDC slashes 1,300 jobs before reinstating half\b0\par\par\uc2 Melody Schreiber \par \uc2 700 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 October 2025\par 15:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Trump administration says 700 notices were sent in error, while former top CDC officer says \u8216\'20\'18they didn\u8217\'20\'19t think through what they were doing\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 More than a thousand employees at the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)\uc2  received notice that they were losing their jobs on Friday in a move that erased entire offices and was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/13/firings-cdc-employees-reversed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 partially reversed}}}\uc2  over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 It caused \u8220\'20\'1Cinstability and whiplash\u8221\'20\'1D, said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/04/cdc-rfk-jr-infectious-disease-testimony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Debra Houry}}}\uc2 , former chief medical officer at the CDC.\par \par \uc2 About 700 reduction in force (RIF) notifications were sent to employees in error, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/11/health/cdc-layoffs-measles.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  says, though there does not seem to be public evidence of an error. Another 600 terminated employees have not been reinstated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt seems like they just took a sledgehammer to the agency versus a scalpel,\u8221\'20\'1D Houry said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact they brought half back already just shows they didn\u8217\'20\'19t think through what they were doing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The entire staff of the Morbidity and Mortality Weekly Report (MMWR), a highly respected epidemiology journal, were terminated and then reinstated. So were employees working on global health and suicide prevention, as well as \u8220\'20\'1Cdisease detectives\u8221\'20\'1D and staff at the National Center for Immunization and Respiratory Diseases.\par \par \uc2 But the entire human resources department is still gone, which will affect operations of the entire agency.\par \par \uc2 The Washington office is still cut, which \u8220\'20\'1Cmakes it difficult to communicate with Congress\u8221\'20\'1D, since they were the main channel for congressional inquiries, Houry said.\par \par \uc2 Staff with the CDC\u8217\'20\'19s institutional review board, which reviews the design of studies, and the ethics office, which oversees all conflicts and interests for CDC leaders and advisory committee members, were also let go.\par \par \uc2 In the next 30 days, some science protocols will be up for renewal by the institutional review board.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ll have to be shut down,\u8221\'20\'1D Houry said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Center for Health Statistics\uc2  was hit hard, with cuts to the staff working on nutrition surveys and electronic health records, and employees in the science office were laid off. The program offering assistance to employees was also cut. These workers provided mental health support, especially amid waves of layoffs and after a mass shooting two months ago that killed a police officer, David Rose, and shook the agency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is no longer available,\u8221\'20\'1D Houry said.\par \par \uc2 Many people from the data office and the Center for Forecasting and Outbreak Analytics were also terminated, which will affect the CDC\u8217\'20\'19s ability to inform the public about outbreaks.\par \par \uc2 Houry is not convinced that the rescinded notices were a coding error; she believes the jobs may have been reinstated after public outcry.\par \par \uc2 In the past, a few people were laid off by accident because they had recently changed jobs or there was an error in how their jobs were coded, so they accidentally received automated termination notices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt usually doesn\u8217\'20\'19t impact hundreds of people,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you do look at what has been reinstated so far, it does seem like it was the things that had the most attention to it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 HHS\uc2  did not respond to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s questions by press time about why some CDC employees received notice they were being reinstated and whether officials had documentation of an error.\par \par \uc2 Since the start of the Trump administration, thousands of people have left the CDC because of terminations, retirements, layoffs and job changes. Leaders asked their employees to report when they received notices, because they were not informed or part of the process.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe cuts this weekend just didn\u8217\'20\'19t seem like there was any thought behind it,\u8221\'20\'1D Houry said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe capacity to respond to an outbreak or to communities is hampered.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Measles, for example, continues spreading across the country in the worst outbreak in three decades \u8211\'20\'13 and if it continues for the next few months, the US will lose its elimination status.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe really need Congress to ask questions about how these RIFs happened, particularly when these are for appropriated [budget] lines. The CDC really needs congressional public support at this point,\u8221\'20\'1D Houry said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe CDC takes care of the public. We need the public to take care of the CDC.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251014elae002mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
