\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Majority of special education staff in US education department laid off \u8211\'20\'13 report\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 356 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 October 2025\par 13:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Layoffs \u8216\'20\'18decimating\u8217\'20\'19 office responsible for protecting rights of infants, children and youth with disabilities, says worker\par \par \uc2 The majority of staff in the education department handling special education has been laid off, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 Friday\u8217\'20\'19s total of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/10/federal-workers-pay-government-shutdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 466 layoffs}}}\uc2  across the education department also affected the Office of Special Education and Rehabilitative Services, which oversees programs that support millions of children and adults with disabilities nationwide, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2025/10/13/nx-s1-5572489/trump-special-education-department-funding-layoffs-disabilities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  sources speaking to various outlets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite extensive efforts to minimize impact on employees and programs during the ongoing government shutdown, the continued lapse in funding has made it necessary to implement the RIF [reduction in force],\u8221\'20\'1D according to a letter issued to workers that CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/trump-government-shutdown-news-10-13-25?post-id=cmgp4qh9500003b6ngdv0qpgk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reviewed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has contacted the education department for comment.\par \par \uc2 One department employee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2025/10/13/nx-s1-5572489/trump-special-education-department-funding-layoffs-disabilities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  NPR: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is decimating the office responsible for safeguarding the rights of infants, toddlers, children and youth with disabilities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/30/voice-of-america-lay-offs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 500 workers at Voice of America and other broadcasters to be laid off}}}\par \par \uc2 Similarly, the National Association of State Directors of Special Education said that if the layoffs were true, \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is significant risk that not only will federal funding lapse, but children with disabilities will be deprived\u8221\'20\'1D of free and proper education, K-12 Dive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.k12dive.com/news/special-education-OSEP-OSERS-federal-rifs-Government-shutdown/802662/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chad Rummel, executive director of the Council for Exceptional Children, told the outlet: \u8220\'20\'1CThe rumored near elimination of the Office for Special Education Programs is absolutely devastating to the education of people with disabilities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEliminating federal capacity to support Idea is harmful to people with disabilities, their families, and the professionals who serve them, and it runs counter to everything our members work toward every day,\u8221\'20\'1D Rummel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.k12dive.com/news/special-education-OSEP-OSERS-federal-rifs-Government-shutdown/802662/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2 , referring to the Individuals with Disabilities Education Act which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ed.gov/laws-and-policy/individuals-disabilities/idea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ensures}}}\uc2  a free and appropriate public education to eligible children with disabilities throughout the country.\par \par \uc2 In March, the education department announced layoffs of 1,300 employees, or nearly 50% of the department\u8217\'20\'19s workforce, which the education secretary, Linda McMahon, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ed.gov/about/news/press-release/us-department-of-education-initiates-reduction-force"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described}}}\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant step toward restoring the greatness of the United States education system\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251013elad0050o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
