\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 After uproar, \uc2 Pete Hegseth\uc2  clarifies Qatari air force facility in Idaho is not a foreign base \u8211\'20\'13 live\b0\par\par\uc2 Robert Mackey (now); Shrai Popat, Lucy Campbell and Tom Ambrose (earlier) \par \uc2 7,716 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 October 2025\par 01:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Earlier, Pentagon chief shared that location would host \u8216\'20\'18contingent of Qatari F-15s and pilots\u8217\'20\'19White House announces federal worker layoffs as government shutdown nears third week\par \par \uc2 2.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump claims that inhaler that costs $645 will be offered at 654% discount\par \par \uc2 At one point during an event on lower drug prices for US consumers on Friday, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  pointed to a chart in the Oval Office which indicated that an inhaler made by the British pharmaceutical company \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  would soon be available, from the new \uc2 US government\uc2  website TrumpRx, at a 654% discount.\par \par \uc2 No one asked what this could possibly mean, but the math here is exceedingly unclear. As numerous reporters have noted, it is just mathematically impossible to offer a discount of more than 100% of the price on any item, without giving it away for free and providing a payment to the consumer.\par \par \uc2 According to a White House fact sheet, the drug Bevespi Aerosphere, an inhaler used to treat chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), \u8220\'20\'1Cwill be made available to patients purchasing directly at a discount equal to 654% of the deal price.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 No explanation of the calculation was provided.\par \par \uc2 Curiously, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sanders.senate.gov/press-releases/news-chairman-sanders-baldwin-lujan-markey-launch-help-committee-investigation-into-efforts-by-pharmaceutical-companies-to-manipulate-the-price-of-asthma-inhalers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter}}}\uc2  from Bernie Sanders, the Vermont senator, and three colleagues sent last year to \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  asked why a similar product, the Breztri Aerosphere inhaler, costs $645 in the US but just $49 in the UK.\par \par \uc2 A visit to the website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://trumprx.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TrumpRx}}}\uc2  offered no details, just a promise that it would be in operation in January 2026 and a large photograph of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , seated in the Oval Office, apparently during his first term, before the painting of Andrew Jackson was swapped out for one of \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 , and a lot of gold trim was added.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 2.57am BST\par \par \uc2 2.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump got Covid vaccine booster on Friday, and his doctor says he has the heart of a 65-year-old\par \par \uc2 Shortly before appearing with his vaccine-skeptic health secretary on Friday, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was vaccinated against both Covid and the flu, according to a letter from the president\u8217\'20\'19s doctor.\par \par \uc2 Sean Barbabella, a \uc2 US Navy\uc2  captain and osteopathic physician, seemed to suggest that Trump received at least one more vaccine, without specifying against what illness, during his visit to Walter Reed Medical Center earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 The doctor also wrote that Trump\u8217\'20\'19 underwent an evaluation that included advanced imaging and laboratory testing, but cast the tests as routine and suggested that he is in \u8220\'20\'1Cexceptional health.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Unlike {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/WhiteHouse/status/1911440308803432686"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in April}}}\uc2 , when Trump underwent what was described then as \u8220\'20\'1Chis annual physical examination\u8221\'20\'1D, no test results were released.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHis cardiac age \u8211\'20\'13 a validated measure of cardiovascular vitality via ECG \u8211\'20\'13 was found to be approximately 14 years younger than his chronological age\u8221\'20\'1D of 79, the doctor added.\par \par \uc2 There was no mention of the persistent bruising on his right hand, no update on his chronic venous insufficiency and no word on whether a cognitive test was administered, or passed with flying colors.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 2.37am BST\par \par \uc2 1.55am BST\par \par \uc2 After uproar, Hegseth clarifies that Qatari air force facility in Idaho is not a foreign base\par \par \uc2 The secretary of defense, \uc2 Pete Hegseth\uc2 , was forced to issue a clarification on social media on Friday evening, hours after he publicly signed what he called \u8220\'20\'1Ca letter of acceptance\u8221\'20\'1D to build a Qatari air force facility in Idaho.\par \par \uc2 Sitting alongside Qatar\u8217\'20\'19s defense minister, Sheikh Saoud bin Abdulrahman bin Hassan bin Ali al-Thani, at the Pentagon on Friday morning, Hegseth said that the location \u8220\'20\'1Cwill host a contingent of Qatari F-15s and pilots\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In the aftermath of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/VE5vaWuZCkQ?si=gn4KH77aoRdY6x7d&t=23"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the televised event}}}\uc2 , it was widely reported that the United States had accepted the building of a foreign military base on its territory, which triggered a backlash from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s base, particularly those motivated by the anti-Muslim animus he expressed most vociferously in the run-up to the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 Among those most outraged was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s influential outside adviser, the extremist podcaster Laura Loomer, who is notorious for her anti-Muslim racism.\par \par \uc2 Loomer voiced her objections, laced with virulent Islamophobia, in dozens of posts on the platform X, including one in which she embedded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/LauraLoomer/status/1976668333539021140"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video of Trump, in 2017}}}\uc2 , calling the nation of Qatar \u8220\'20\'1Ca funder of terrorism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Another influential podcaster, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/trump-admin-sparks-maga-fury-with-qatari-air-force-base-in-us-betrayed-10862415"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Newsweek}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CThere should never be a military base of a foreign power on the sacred soil of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bannon was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chief strategist in 2017 when he implemented his promised Muslim ban by barring entry to the US by citizens of seven nations with Muslim majorities, prompting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2017/01/28/protesters-demand-release-refugees-jfk-trumps-muslim-ban-sows-chaos/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mass protests at airports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The uproar over plans to build a Qatari air force facility in Idaho led Hegseth to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/PeteHegseth/status/1976769302867898706"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post}}}\uc2  what he called an \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant clarification\u8221\'20\'1D on social media later on Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CThe US military has a long-standing partnership w/ Qatar, including today\u8217\'20\'19s announced cooperation w/ F-15QA aircraft,\u8221\'20\'1D the former Fox weekend anchor installed as defense secretary wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CHowever, to be clear, Qatar will not have their own base in the United States \u8211\'20\'13 nor anything like a base. We control the existing base, like we do with all partners.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 2.08am BST\par \par \uc2 12.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Department of Housing and Urban Development\uc2  confirms layoffs\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the \uc2 Department of Housing and Urban Development\uc2  has confirmed that layoffs of federal workers are under way during the government shutdown. \u8220\'20\'1CHUD is implementing a reduction in force to align our programs with the Administration\u8217\'20\'19s priorities and the appropriations available to the department,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 1.43am BST\par \par \uc2 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump once agains shares his imaginary tale that stores in Portland, Oregon, are all made of plywood\par \par \uc2 For at least the third time in recent weeks, the president of the United States publicly stated his firm belief in the entirely imaginary claim that very few stores remain in business in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/03/portland-oregon-living-hell-tiktok-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the thriving city}}}\uc2  of Portland, Oregon, and the few that continue to operate are constructed entirely of plywood, to make them easier to rebuild after serial arson attacks and looting, which are not, in fact, happening.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPortland, Oregon, I mean, every time I look at that place, the place is burning down. There\u8217\'20\'19s fires all over the place,\u8221\'20\'1D Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/atrupar/status/1976776133887549815"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2  in the Oval Office, where he made the same wildly false claim last month to justify his desire to deploy federal troops to the city.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen a store owner, there\u8217\'20\'19s very few of them left, but when a store owner rebuilds his store, they build it out of plywood. They don\u8217\'20\'19t put up storefronts anymore. They just put wood up, because they know it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be ripped down,\u8221\'20\'1D the president insisted, as his health secretary, \uc2 FDA\uc2  commissioner and Medicare administrator looked on but said nothing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd then I hear how wonderful it is. It\u8217\'20\'19s not wonderful, it\u8217\'20\'19s a disaster,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump continued, apparently referring to the vision of the city as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/06/oregon-republicans-protest-photo-south-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a fiery hellscape}}}\uc2  common in rightwing media that he has confused with reality.\par \par \uc2 The president made the same false claim {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/i/status/1976017694437597246"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Wednesday}}}\uc2 , during a roundtable with conservative influencers who exaggerate the impact of protests in Portland, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/live/D3urjiwp_wQ?si=UEUmx8kzTMKT1OFV&t=2862"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on 25 September}}}\uc2 , two days before declaring that troops were needed in the \u8220\'20\'1Cwar ravaged\u8221\'20\'1D city.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s almost an insurrection, that place,\u8221\'20\'1D he concluded, perhaps hinting that he is ready to invoke the Insurrection Act to deploy military forces to the city where protesters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/pdxfrontline/status/1975758838881263811?s=46&t=2JPvQfh1uSZDbpdbm2Dw4g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dancing in inflatable costumes}}}\uc2  have made a mockery of his claims on multiple nights this week.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 1.43am BST\par \par \uc2 11.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump claims his threat to 'obliterate' \uc2 Hamas\uc2  sealed deal to end Gaza war and bring peace 'to the entire Middle East'\par \par \uc2 Hours after not winning the Nobel peace prize he had openly campaigned for, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said that his threats of violence against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  had convinced the Palestinian militants to agree to a deal to exchange Israeli hostages for Palestinian prisoners and had led to an end to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s US-backed offensive in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Trump also continued to make grand claims about the Gaza deal, claiming to reporters in the Oval Office on Friday that it would bring peace \u8220\'20\'1Cto the entire Middle East\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Asked what guarantees he had given \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to persuade them that Israel will not simply restart its bombing campaign in Gaza once the Israeli hostages have been exchanged for Palestinian prisoners, Trump suggested his own threat to obliterate the militant group had been decisive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat did I do, with respect to them? Well, you know, I spoke a little bit tough, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what would happen, you have to speak tough. That\u8217\'20\'19s a tough world, that\u8217\'20\'19s a tough, as they say, neighborhood. And they\u8217\'20\'19re tough people, they\u8217\'20\'19re very tough people. And they\u8217\'20\'19re smart people. They\u8217\'20\'19re good negotiators, you know, they\u8217\'20\'19ve got a lot of things going. They put that to good use, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to be very, very successful,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/atrupar/status/1976773491027288141"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the president said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut they knew the retribution would be tremendous, unsustainable. It would\u8217\'20\'19ve been unsustainable. It would have been complete obliteration, and they didn\u8217\'20\'19t want that. And nobody wants it at this point. They want to get on with, you know, rebuilding the entire Middle East. It\u8217\'20\'19s not only Gaza, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be the entire Middle East. They\u8217\'20\'19re going to be able to live in peace,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump continued.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, we have some little hotspots, but they\u8217\'20\'19re very small, you know the ones I\u8217\'20\'19m talking about,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said to the reporter whose question he did not actually address. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re very small, they\u8217\'20\'19ll be very easy to put out. Those fires are going to be put out very quickly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.30am BST\par \par \uc2 10.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump starts announcement on drug prices with 2020 election lie, promises impossible 1,000% discounts\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just started an Oval Office announcement on a deal with the British-based drug maker \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2 , for a \u8220\'20\'1Cmost-favored-nation\u8221\'20\'1D drug-pricing model aimed at making prescription medicines more affordable, by boasting that he would have struck the deal sooner, but \u8220\'20\'1Cwe were interrupted by a rigged election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump went on to repeat the wildly false claim that the discounted prices for American consumers would reduce the price of prescription drugs by up to 1,000%.\par \par \uc2 As Daniel Dale of CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/09/23/politics/fact-check-drug-prices-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has explained}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CCutting drug prices by more than 100% would mean that Americans would get paid to acquire their medications rather than paying for them.\u8221\'20\'1D A health economist, Timothy McBride, told the network Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims are \u8220\'20\'1Cjust not logical\u8221\'20\'1D, since a 500% price reduction would mean that a drug that now costs $100 would be available for free, with consumers given a $400 rebate.\par \par \uc2 The actual deal includes cutting prices for the government\u8217\'20\'19s Medicaid health plan for low-income Americans and discounted prices through a \u8220\'20\'1CTrumpRx\u8221\'20\'1D website, the president said.\par \par \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief executive \uc2 Pascal Soriot\uc2  stood near Trump in the gold-clad Oval Office as the president made the announcement.\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  previously agreed to drop prescription drug prices in the Medicaid program for lower-income Americans to what it charges in other developed countries in exchange for relief from tariffs threatened by Trump.\par \par \uc2 Americans currently pay by far the most for prescription medicines, often nearly three times more than in other developed nations, and Trump has been pressuring drugmakers to lower their prices to what patients pay elsewhere or face stiff tariffs.\par \par \uc2 Last month, he threatened 100% tariffs on drugmakers, increasing pressure on the pharmaceutical industry to agree to price cuts and shift manufacturing to the US.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.28am BST\par \par \uc2 10.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump threatens additional 100% tariff on imports from China, and export controls on software\par \par \uc2 Writing on his social media platform, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/115351840469973590"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that, in response to what he called China\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinarily aggressive position on Trade\u8221\'20\'1D and new export restrictions, he intends to \u8220\'20\'1Cimpose a Tariff of 100% on China, over and above any Tariff that they are currently paying\u8221\'20\'1D starting on 1 November.\par \par \uc2 The same day, he adds, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe will impose Export Controls on any and all critical software\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That date is after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s planned meeting with Chinese leader Xi Jinping.\par \par \uc2 Our colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/10/trump-china-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Callum Jones has more}}}\uc2  on the latest friction in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trade war with China.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.26am BST\par \par \uc2 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 The wave of layoffs at federal agencies has reportedly reached the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  (IRS) now, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/LisaDNews/status/1976750735011262863"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  the \uc2 PBS\uc2  correspondent Lisa Desjardins.\par \par \uc2 9.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Criminal charges against \uc2 John Bolton\uc2  could be filed next week - report\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors in Maryland could seek criminal charges next week against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former national security adviser \uc2 John Bolton\uc2 , report the Pulitzer prize-winning reporter Carol Leonnig and her colleague Ken Dilanian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/msnbc/news/criminal-charges-bolton-expected-early-week-rcna236926"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for MSNBC}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A grand jury in Maryland has been hearing evidence related to claims that Bolton, a former ally of Trump turned harsh critic, improperly kept classified national security information in his Maryland home.\par \par \uc2 The journalists also report that Ed Martin, a Republican operative who served briefly as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s acting US attorney in the District of Columbia now running the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CWeaponization Working Group\u8221\'20\'1D, has met multiple times with the Trump-appointed acting US attorney in Maryland, Kelly Hayes, on the Bolton case.\par \par \uc2 An indictment on Bolton for illegally retaining classified documents would be the third of a Trump critic in recent weeks, and would echo the indictment of New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Tish James, in accusing critics of the president of committing crimes he was indicted for after his first term.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been chatting to Jessica Roth, a former federal prosecutor in the southern district of New York, about the indictment of Letitia James.\par \par \uc2 Roth said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely distressing\u8221\'20\'1D to see prosecutions brought against the president\u8217\'20\'19s perceived political enemies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t say that I was surprised that the department [under attorney general Pam Bondi] pursued these charges against Tish James,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CThat doesn\u8217\'20\'19t lessen my distress \u8230\'20\'26 particularly in light of what had been longstanding Department of Justice policy not to pursue an indictment unless prosecutors were convinced that they would be able to prove a case beyond a reasonable doubt at trial.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lindsey Halligan, the handpicked and newly installed US attorney for the eastern district of Virginia, has pursued the charges against James and former \uc2 FBI\uc2  director \uc2 James Comey\uc2 , and Roth notes that we could see a wider effort to bring charges against the president\u8217\'20\'19s adversaries in districts throughout the country that are now run by Trump-friendly prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 Much like the charges brought against Comey, Roth underscored that the crimes that James is being accused of are very difficult to prove \u8220\'20\'1Ceven under the best stances\u8221\'20\'1D because they require proof of \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminal intent as opposed to an honest mistake or negligence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Multiple agencies confirm reductions in force are under way\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has independently confirmed that reductions in force (RIFs) are under way at the following departments and agencies:\par \par \uc2 * Department of Education\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  (specifically the \uc2 Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 * Department of the Treasury\par \par \uc2 Certain agencies haven\u8217\'20\'19t immediately responded to the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s request for comment, but other media outlets have reported layoffs are expected at the following:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\par \par \uc2 * Department of Energy\par \par \uc2 * Department of the Interior\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Department of Housing and Urban Development\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 HHS\uc2  confirms layoffs, saying department had become 'bloated bureaucracy' under Biden\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) confirmed to the Guardian that employees across \u8220\'20\'1Cmultiple divisions\u8221\'20\'1D have received reduction-in-force notices. \uc2 HHS\uc2  spokesperson Andrew Nixon said this was \u8220\'20\'1Ca direct consequence of the Democrat-led government shutdown\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He added that \uc2 HHS\uc2  under the Biden administration \u8220\'20\'1Cbecame a bloated bureaucracy, growing its budget by 38% and its workforce by 17%\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Nixon said that all employees receiving RIF notices were \u8220\'20\'1Cdesignated non-essential by their respective divisions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 HHS\uc2  continues to close wasteful and duplicative entities, including those that are at odds with the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s Make America Healthy Again agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal worker union calls mass layoffs during government shutdown 'disgraceful'\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees (AFGE)\uc2 , the largest union representing federal government workers, has condemned the mass layoffs announced by the White House budget office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is disgraceful that the Trump administration has used the government shutdown as an excuse to illegally fire thousands of workers who provide critical services to communities across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , the union\u8217\'20\'19s president.\par \par \uc2 AFGE\uc2  has already filed a lawsuit in federal court challenging the firings, and a hearing is set for Thursday, 16 October. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not stop fighting until every reduction-in-force notice is rescinded,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelley added.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Department of Education confirms layoffs will happen\par \par \uc2 The Department of Education has also confirmed to the Guardian that their employees will be affected by the reductions in force.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House budget office says layoffs are 'substantial'\par \par \uc2 An office of management and budget (OMB) spokesperson told the Guardian that the reductions in force that have begun are \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantial\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The official didn\u8217\'20\'19t confirm an exact number, but we\u8217\'20\'19re bringing you the latest as we hear from different agencies and departments about how they stand to be affected.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Treasury department confirms that RIFs have begun\par \par \uc2 A treasury department spokesperson confirms to the Guardian that mass layoffs, or reductions in force, have started. They did not comment on the scale of the firings.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has returned from his visit to Walter Reed medical center for his \u8220\'20\'1Csemi-annual physical\u8221\'20\'1D. He didn\u8217\'20\'19t take questions from reporters on his way back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re due to hear from him at 5pm ET in the Oval Office for an announcement about lowering the cost of drug prices.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 DHS says layoffs will happen at cybersecurity agency\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  spokesperson has told the Guardian that reductions in force (RIFs) will happen at the \uc2 Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency\uc2  (\uc2 CISA\uc2 ) while the government shutdown continues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDuring the last administration \uc2 CISA\uc2  was focused on censorship, branding and electioneering. This is part of getting \uc2 CISA\uc2  back on mission,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to host summit on Gaza with world leaders during Egypt visit \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  plans to hold a summit of world leaders on Gaza, during his visit to Egypt next week, according to \uc2 Axios\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Citing four sources with knowledge of the plans, \uc2 Axios\uc2  reports that the summit is being organized by Egyptian president Abdul Fattah al-Sisi, who has already reached out to several European and Arab leaders with invitations. According to a US official, Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  will not be present, and the meeting will likely take place on Tuesday in Sharm-el-sheikh, but could be moved to Monday, according to \uc2 Axios\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 sources.\par \par \uc2 A reminder that Trump is set to address Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Knesset on Monday, before travelling to Egypt.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here's a recap of the day so far\par \par \uc2 * The White House announced layoffs of federal workers are to come as the government shutdown continues. In an ominous post on social media, budget chief \uc2 Russ Vought\uc2  wrote that \u8220\'20\'1Creductions in force\u8221\'20\'1D (laying off federal workers) have begun, as the shutdown enters its 10th day.\par \par \uc2 * On Capitol Hill, the impasse continues, as House speaker Mike Johnson said the lower chamber won\u8217\'20\'19t return until the Senate decides to \u8216\'20\'18turn the lights back on\u8217\'20\'19. Republican leadership continued to lambast Democrats, blaming them for the shutdown and saying that a separate bill to keep members of the military paid was redundant since the House-passed legislation \u8211\'20\'13 which has stalled in the upper chamber seven times \u8211\'20\'13would reopen the government. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have voted so many times to pay the troops. We\u8217\'20\'19ve already done it. We did it in the house three weeks ago, the ball is in the court of Senate Democrats right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson added.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Massachusetts Institute of Technology\uc2  (MIT)\par \par \uc2 has become the first of nine universities to reject an agreement that would exchange adoption of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s higher education agenda for favorable treatment and funding. \uc2 Sally Kornbluth\uc2 , the MIT president, wrote to the Trump administration to say that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe university has already freely met or exceeded many of the standards outlined in the proposal, but that she disagrees with other requirements it demands, including those that would restrict free expression\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * We\u8217\'20\'19re waiting to hear the ruling from a federal court in San Francisco, over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s deployment of troops to Portland, Oregon. Three appellate judges heard arguments on Thursday and seemed more likely to rule in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s favor than the decision by a federal judge in Chicago, who blocked troops from deploying to the windy city. The administration has said it plans to appeal the ruling.\par \par \uc2 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 One note on the announced layoffs of government workers. A federal judge will actually hear arguments next week over the legality of the reductions in force during the shutdown. This comes after the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees (AFGE)\uc2  sued the administration over the layoff threat earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 AFGE\uc2  is the largest union representing federal workers.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 US government\uc2  workforce cuts have begun, OMB chief says\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s White House budget chief, \uc2 Russ Vought\uc2 , just ominously posted on X that \u8220\'20\'1Creductions in force\u8221\'20\'1D (laying off federal workers) have begun, as the government shutdown enters its 10th day. He offered no further details, but we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you more as soon as we get it.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 5.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 MIT becomes first university to reject White House offer for special funding treatment\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Massachusetts Institute of Technology\uc2  (MIT) has become the first university to reject an agreement that would exchange adoption of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s higher education agenda for favorable treatment and funding.\par \par \uc2 The administration\u8217\'20\'19s proposal \u8211\'20\'13 the \u8220\'20\'1CCompact for Academic Excellence in Higher Education\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 was sent to nine universities and set out a list of requirements including a cap international student enrollment, freezing tuition for five years, adhering to definitions of gender and creating a more \u8220\'20\'1Cwelcoming\u8221\'20\'1D environment on campuses for conservatives. Doing so would give the institutions preferential access to federal funding.\par \par \uc2 Sally Kornbluth\uc2 , the MIT president, wrote to the Trump administration to say that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe university has already freely met or exceeded many of the standards outlined in the proposal, but that she disagrees with other requirements it demands, including those that would restrict free expression\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She added:\par \par \uc2 The other eight colleges are the \uc2 University of Arizona\uc2 , Brown University, \uc2 Dartmouth College\uc2 , the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2 , the \uc2 University of Southern California\uc2 , the \uc2 University of Texas\uc2 , \uc2 Vanderbilt University\uc2  and the \uc2 University of Virginia\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Updated at 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 National guard troops seen on Memphis streets as Trump faces legal challenges\par \par \uc2 National guard troops were seen patrolling in Memphis for the first time on Friday, as part of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s controversial federal taskforce, amid fierce legal challenges as he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/09/trump-national-guard-troops-chicago-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was blocked}}}\uc2  from sending troops to Chicago and a court ruling is awaited in Portland, Oregon.\par \par \uc2 At least nine national guard troops began their Tennessee patrol at the \uc2 Bass Pro Shops\uc2 , an outdoor gear chain, located at the Pyramid, a commercial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wreg.com/news/whats-the-deal-with-the-bass-pro-shops-pyramid-in-memphis/#:~:text=Where%20did%20the%20Pyramid%20come,Pyramid%20Arena%20opened%20in%201991."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landmark}}}\uc2  in Memphis. They were being escorted by a Memphis police officer and posed for photos with visitors who were standing outside.\par \par \uc2 It was unclear how many {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/06/california-oregon-national-guard-trump-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federalized troops}}}\uc2  were on the ground or were expected to arrive later.\par \par \uc2 During an NAACP Memphis forum on Wednesday, Memphis\u8217\'20\'19s police chief, Cerelyn \u8220\'20\'1CCJ\u8221\'20\'1D Davis, had said she hoped guard personnel would help direct traffic and have a presence in \u8220\'20\'1Cretail corridors\u8221\'20\'1D, but not be used to operate checkpoints or anything similar \u8211\'20\'13 the kind of situation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/washington-dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington}}}\uc2  DC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/11/trump-washington-dc-crime"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experienced}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Memphis authorities did not request federal troops but Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor,Bill Lee, supports the move by the White House.Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 US immigration enforcement using military hardware and tactics on civilians\par \par \uc2 Even without the national guard, law enforcement agencies of the federal government have been using military hardware and tactics on civilian targets.\par \par \uc2 At a low-rent apartment complex on Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s south shore, people started hearing the boots hit the roof around one in the morning. The oh-dark-thirty {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/usimmigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration}}}\uc2  enforcement raid in the early hours of 1 Octoberfeatured an air assault from helicopters. Officers went door to door in the building, using charges to blow the hinges off doors and flashbang grenades to clear apartments. They hauled men, women and children from the building in zip ties and often little else, ostensibly to capture undocumented gang members.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cwbchicago.com/2025/10/exclusive-tiktoks-show-south-shore-building-in-ruin-long-before-ice-raided-it-this-week.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 troubled}}}\uc2  apartment building at 7500 S South Shore Drive hadn\u8217\'20\'19t passed an annual inspection since 2022. With the remains of doors and furniture and the bloodied, scattered belongings of former tenants in tatters, it may struggle to pass another.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo many of these people remain without shelter or a place to live because it essentially rendered their homes and that entire apartment complex uninhabitable,\u8221\'20\'1D said Colleen Connell, executive director of the American Civil Liberties Union of Illinois. She described the apartment raid as a military-style attack. Days afterward, the building looked like a war zone, which may be the point. of George\u8217\'20\'19s report below.\par \par \uc2 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says there is 'no reason' to still meet with president Xi, weighing tariff increase\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said that there is now \u8220\'20\'1Cno reason\u8221\'20\'1D to meet with China\u8217\'20\'19s president, Xi Jingping, at the Apec summit in South Korea.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he was surprised to learn that China has been sending letters to countries worldwide saying it planned to impose \u8220\'20\'1Cexport controls\u8221\'20\'1D on \u8220\'20\'1Cevery element of production\u8221\'20\'1D related to rare earths. \u8220\'20\'1CI have always felt that they\u8217\'20\'19ve been lying in wait, and now, as usual, I have been proven right,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 The president concluded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/115350455734003647"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his post on Truth Social}}}\uc2  by saying that the US is now calculating a \u8220\'20\'1Cmassive increase\u8221\'20\'1D of tariffs on Chinese products coming into the US. According to the \uc2 Peterson Institute for International Economics\uc2 , average US tariffs on Chinese exports now stand at over 57%.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 First lady says that she has had an 'open channel' with Putin regarding displaced Ukrainian children\par \par \uc2 At the White House, first lady Melania Trump is now addressing reporters.\par \par \uc2 She said that in recent months, following a letter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/16/melania-trump-vladimir-putin-letter-donald"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she wrote }}}\uc2 to Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , she has had an \u8220\'20\'1Copen channel\u8221\'20\'1D with the Kremlin leader about children of Ukraine displaced by the ongoing war.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEight children have been rejoined with their families during the past 24 hours,\u8221\'20\'1D the first lady said. \u8220\'20\'1CThree were separated from their parents and displaced to the Russian Federation because of frontline fighting. The other five were separated from family members across borders because of the conflict.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump didn\u8217\'20\'19t take any questions from reporters after delivering her short speech.\par \par \uc2 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The president will arrive at Walter Reed medical center shortly for what\u8217\'20\'19s being described as a \u8220\'20\'1Csemi-annual physical\u8221\'20\'1D despite already having his yearly check-up in April. \u8220\'20\'1CI think I\u8217\'20\'19m in great shape, but I\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told reporters in the Oval Office on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 This comes as he prepares to travel to Israel on Sunday, as the first phase of a plan to end the war in Gaza gets under way. Yesterday, Trump said that he expects Israeli hostages to be released by Monday or Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 A White House official confirms to the Guardian that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement in the Oval Office at 5pm ET will be about lowering drug prices.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson says House will come back when Senate Democrats 'turn the lights back on'\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson said the only end in sight for the House to return to legislative work is when \u8220\'20\'1CSenate Democrats turn the lights back on\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Republican speaker said that returning to work was ultimately now up to the upper chamber. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have done the work in the House,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson added. \u8220\'20\'1C[Democrats] are the ones blocking the checks, not Republicans, all these questions should be directed to them and not to us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Again, Johnson said that the need to bring a separate bill to the House floor, to keep members of the military paid during the shutdown, is redundant. He maintains that the GOP-written continuing resolution, which passed the House, would allow troops to keep their paycheck.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have voted so many times to pay the troops. We\u8217\'20\'19ve already done it. We did it in the house three weeks ago, the ball is in the court of Senate Democrats right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson holds press conference as shutdown enters tenth day\par \par \uc2 As the shutdown enters its 10th day, Friday marks the first day federal workers across the US will receive a partial paycheck. House speaker Mike Johnson is holding a press conference, once again, blaming Democrats for the lapse in government funding.\par \par \uc2 This comes after the Senate failed, for the seventh time, to pass a stopgap bill to reopen the government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats don\u8217\'20\'19t, don\u8217\'20\'19t appear to be in any rush to end this pain,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is beyond the pale, what \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is doing right now, it\u8217\'20\'19s sickening. It\u8217\'20\'19s sickening to hear him say it\u8217\'20\'19s better for him and his party when it\u8217\'20\'19s so terrible for real Americans. Millions of people are experiencing real pain because these political games.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 My colleagues {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/oct/10/gaza-ceasefire-plan-israel-donald-trump-hamas-palestine-benjamin-netanyahu-middle-east-latest-news#top-of-blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are covering the latest developments}}}\uc2  in the Middle East, as the first phase of the plan to end the war between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  takes effect.\par \par \uc2 Israeli troops have begun to withdraw to a redeployment line, and Palestinians have started to return to home from southern Gaza. As Aneesa Ahmed notes, thousands of officers are also set to be deployed for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Israel on Monday, according to Israeli police.\par \par \uc2 Officers will be stationed along key points of the president\u8217\'20\'19s planned journey. As part of the president\u8217\'20\'19s short trip, he\u8217\'20\'19s set to address the Knesset on Monday. This would mark the first visit there by a US president in almost two decades, Aneesa reports. You can follow along here.\par \par \uc2 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tariffs caused a Chinese exit from the soybean market, leaving midwestern farmers are waiting for a solution\par \par \uc2 At the Purfeerst farm in southern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/minnesota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota}}}\uc2 , the soybean harvest just wrapped up for the season. The silver grain bins are full of about 100,000 bushels of soybeans, which grab about $10 a piece.\par \par \uc2 This year, though, the fate of the soybeans, and the people whose livelihoods depend on selling them, is up in the air: America\u8217\'20\'19s soybean farmers are stuck in the middle of a trade war between the US and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China}}}\uc2 , the biggest purchaser of soybean exports, used to feed China\u8217\'20\'19s pigs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are gonna have to find a home for them soybeans some time soon,\u8221\'20\'1D said Matt Purfeerst, a fifth-generation farmer on the family\u8217\'20\'19s land. \u8220\'20\'1CThey won\u8217\'20\'19t stay in our bins for ever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 No other country comes close to purchasing as many American soybeans as China \u8211\'20\'13 last year, it was more than $12bn worth. This year, the country has not purchased a single dollar, cutting off the country that makes up about half of US soybean exports.\par \par \uc2 While Trump has said he intends some sort of payment to go to soybean farmers hurt by tariffs, an announcement of a specific plan is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/the-shutdown-is-delaying-trumps-farm-bailout-farmers-say-it-wont-be-enough-even-when-it-happens-163341304.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on hold}}}\uc2  while the government is shut down. He said in a Truth Social post last week that he\u8217\'20\'19d be meeting with the Chinese president soon and \u8220\'20\'1Csoybeans will be a major topic of discussion\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The White House cast blame on Democrats for the government shutdown for the delay in a response to the Guardian on Wednesday, erroneously claiming they were prioritizing healthcare for migrants over farmers. of Rachel\u8217\'20\'19s report from Faribault, Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 2.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate advances annual defense policy bill as shutdown continues\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday, the Senate approved the annual defense policy bill, known as the National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA), which funds the military in 2026.\par \par \uc2 In a 77-20 vote, the upper chamber advanced the legislation which confers more than $900bn in defense spending. There had been a gridlock for over a month, after lawmakers were unable to agree on a series of amendments.\par \par \uc2 The bill now heads to armed services committees in both the House and the Senate to hammer out the details and differences in both pieces of legislation. A reminder that the lower chamber passed their version in September.\par \par \uc2 1.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaker Johnson defends decision to stave off vote on separate bill to keep service members paid throughout shutdown\par \par \uc2 As the shutdown enters its 10th day, and both chambers are out of session today, House speaker Mike Johnson has defended not passing a separate bill that would keep members of the military paid throughout the shutdown.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans have voted to OPEN the government and get our troops, Border Patrol, TSA, and veterans PAID,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said, before blaming Democratic leadership for refusing to pass the House-passed continuing resolution. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is terrified of a challenge from the Marxist left \u8211\'20\'13 so he and the Democrats voted to CLOSE the government-and to STOP PAYCHECKS from being issued.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This comes as other Republicans in Congress have pushed for specific legislation that would keep providing paychecks to troops. A reminder, that service members are due to go without their first paycheck on 15 October, if the Senate is unable to advance a short-term funding bill.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 1.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 1.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll hear from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at 10am E\par \par \uc2 T today, when he heads to Walter Reed\par \par \uc2 medical\par \par \uc2 center for his \u8220\'20\'1Csemi-annual\u8221\'20\'1D physical exam.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be keeping an ear out for any reaction he has to the indictment of Letitia James, his longtime political adversary.\par \par \uc2 Later we\u8217\'20\'19ll also hear from the first lady, Melania Trump. She\u8217\'20\'19ll make an announcement in the White House grand foyer.\par \par \uc2 Trump will also make an announcement at 5pm ET in the Oval Office, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you the latest as it happens.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 1.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 12.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israeli police preparing for Trump visit on Monday\par \par \uc2 Israeli police said on Friday that they are preparing for a visit by US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to Israel on Monday.\par \par \uc2 More to follow.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 12.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House says Nobel committee places 'politics over peace' as Trump misses out again\par \par \uc2 The White House on Friday criticized the Nobel Prize committee\u8217\'20\'19s decision to award the peace prize to a Venezuelan opposition leader instead of\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump will continue making peace deals, ending wars, and saving lives. He has the heart of a humanitarian, and there will never be anyone like him who can move mountains with the sheer force of his will,\u8221\'20\'1D White House spokesperson \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  said in a post on X.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Nobel Committee proved they place politics over peace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 1.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 12.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Senate\uc2  remained deadlocked on legislation to end the government shutdown on Thursday, as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  reiterated his threat to make Democrats pay for the funding lapse that has closed federal agencies and furloughed workers nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The Senate took its seventh round of votes on competing Democratic and Republican proposals to restart the funding, but neither won enough bipartisan support to clear the 60-vote threshold for advancement in the chamber. In a sign that neither party had budged from its demands, no senators changed their votes from when the bills were last considered in recent days.\par \par \uc2 Government funding lapsed last Wednesday, and Republicans are insisting Senate Democrats approve a bill to continue operations through 21 November, which has already cleared the House of Representatives. But Democrats say any government funding deal must be paired with an extension of premium tax credits for Affordable Care Act health plans, which expire at the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 They are also demanding that funding for public media outlets be restored and cuts to the Medicaid health insurance program for poor and disabled Americans are reversed.\par \par \uc2 Congress\u8217\'20\'19s Republican leaders have refused to negotiate over their demands until the government is reopened, and during a cabinet meeting at the White House, Trump repeated his threat to single out Democratic-led states and cities for retaliation, if their lawmakers do not back down.\par \par \uc2 11.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  has accused {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his administration of turning the Department of Justice into \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonal attack dogs against their political enemies\u8221\'20\'1D, after New York attorney general Letitia James was indicted for fraud in Virginia.\par \par \uc2 Calling the move \u8220\'20\'1Coutrageous\u8221\'20\'1D, Schumer was among those labelling the move as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s latest effort to weaponize the department to punish political rivals.\par \par \uc2 James first attracted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ire after she led a civil fraud case against the president and his business that resulted in a $500m fine \u8211\'20\'13 a fine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/21/trump-civil-fraud-case-appeal-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently overturned by an appellate court}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Senator Adam Schiff said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cexceedingly dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D to have a justice department that responds to the president\u8217\'20\'19s orders to target his political enemies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut I can tell you this,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CThose of us on the president\u8217\'20\'19s enemies list \u8211\'20\'13 and it is a long and growing list \u8211\'20\'13 will not be intimidated. We will not be deterred. We will do our jobs. We will stand up to this president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 11.35am BST\par \par \uc2 The sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office for metro Phoenix spent millions of dollars budgeted for compliance costs in a racial profiling case over \uc2 Joe Arpaio\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s immigration crackdowns on things that had little or nothing to do with a court-ordered overhaul of the agency, according to an expert\u8217\'20\'19s report.\par \par \uc2 The report released on Wednesday criticized the use of compliance money by the Maricopa county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office to fund personnel costs and tasks, either in part or in full, that are not connected to the overhaul.\par \par \uc2 It also pointed out inappropriate spending: $2.8m for surplus body-worn camera licenses that went beyond the court\u8217\'20\'19s orders; $1.5m in renovations in the relocation of an internal affairs office; over $1.3m to buy 42 vehicles; and an $11,000 golf cart to bring staff from headquarters to the internal affairs operation, even though the department was leasing parking space at the latter location.\par \par \uc2 For over a decade, Maricopa county taxpayers have picked up the bill for remedying constitutional violations found in a 2013 profiling verdict over then sheriff Arpaio\u8217\'20\'19s traffic patrols targeting immigrants.\par \par \uc2 The racial profiling case centered on 20 large-scale traffic patrols launched by Arpaio that targeted immigrants from January 2008 through October 2011. That led to the profiling verdict and expensive court-ordered overhauls of the agency\u8217\'20\'19s traffic patrol operations and, later, its internal affairs unit.\par \par \uc2 The county says $323m has been spent so far on legal expenditures, a staff that monitors the sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s department\u8217\'20\'19s progress and the agency\u8217\'20\'19s compliance costs. The county has said the total is expected to reach $352m by July 2026.\par \par \uc2 11.18am BST\par \par \uc2 US to send 200 troops to Israel to support and monitor ceasefire deal, reports say\par \par \uc2 US troops have been sent to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  as part of the peace deal approved on Thursday to support and help monitor the ceasefire, according to multiple news reports.\par \par \uc2 Senior {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ShelbyTalcott/status/1976414785177571689?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Etweet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US officials told reporters }}}\uc2 that 200 troops will initially be on the ground with a \u8220\'20\'1Ccivil-military coordination center\u8221\'20\'1D operated by US Central Command to help facilitate the flow of humanitarian aid as well as logistical and security assistance into the territory wracked by two years of war, the Associated Press reported, citing two officials who confirmed the report on the condition of anonymity to discuss details not authorized for release.\par \par \uc2 Reuters and \uc2 ABC News\uc2  also reported on military troops being sent to Israel.\par \par \uc2 The troops are part of a broader team that also includes partner nations, non-governmental organizations and private-sector entities there to help monitor the peace deal and the transition to a civilian government in Gaza, US officials said.\par \par \uc2 US service members have already begun arriving in the region from around the globe, according to one of the officials, and will continue to travel to the region over the weekend to begin planning and establishing the center.\par \par \uc2 American troops will not be sent into Gaza, they said, and the coordination center will be staffed by about 200 US service members who have expertise in transportation, planning, security, logistics and engineering.\par \par \uc2 11.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Federal appeals court hears arguments on whether Trump can federalize Oregon national guard\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court heard arguments on whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  had authority to take control of 200 Oregon national guard troops. The president had planned to deploy them in Portland, where protesters have shown up wearing frog and chicken costumes at the mostly small, nightly demonstrations outside an Ice building.\par \par \uc2 A three-judge panel in San Francisco on Thursday appeared likely to set aside the ruling blocking Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/portland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Portland}}}\uc2  deployment, which would clear the way for hundreds of soldiers to enter that city.\par \par \uc2 A judge on Sunday granted a temporary restraining order blocking the move. Trump had mobilized California troops for Portland just hours after the judge first blocked him from using Oregon\u8217\'20\'19s guard.\par \par \uc2 Stacy Chaffin, an Oregon assistant attorney general, echoed the language of the lower court judge who blocked Trump\u8217\'20\'19s deployment, saying the president\u8217\'20\'19s descriptions of Portland as riven by violence were \u8220\'20\'1Cuntethered from reality\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The judges questioned whether they should only consider the current circumstances or take into account more active protests earlier this year that temporarily shut down Ice\u8217\'20\'19s Portland headquarters.\par \par \uc2 The US circuit judge Ryan Nelson, a Trump appointee, said courts should not engage in a \u8220\'20\'1Cday-by-day\u8221\'20\'1D review of whether troops were needed at any given time.\par \par \uc2 10.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Letitia James criminally charged in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s latest effort to punish rivals\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the US politics live blog. I\u8217\'20\'19m Tom Ambrose and I\u8217\'20\'19ll be bringing you the latest news lines over the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 We begin with the news that a federal grand jury has indicted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/letitia-james"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Letitia James}}}\uc2 , the New York attorney general, for bank fraud, according to a person familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Lindsey Halligan, the US attorney for the eastern district of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2 , personally presented the case to the grand jury on Thursday, the person said. US attorneys do not typically present to a grand jury.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is nothing more than a continuation of the president\u8217\'20\'19s desperate weaponization of our justice system. He is forcing federal law enforcement agencies to do his bidding, all because I did my job as the New York state attorney general,\u8221\'20\'1D James said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/NewYorkStateAG/status/1976400103989764190"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recorded video statement}}}\uc2  on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese charges are baseless, and the president\u8217\'20\'19s own public statements make clear that his only goal is political retribution at any cost. The president\u8217\'20\'19s actions are a grave violation of our constitutional order and have drawn sharp criticism from members of both parties.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Halligan was installed in the role last month after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  became frustrated with the pace of investigations against his rivals. \u8220\'20\'1CNo one is above the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Halligan said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe charges as alleged in this case represent intentional, criminal acts and tremendous breaches of the public\u8217\'20\'19s trust. The facts and the law in this case are clear, and we will continue following them to ensure that justice is served.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 In other developments:\par \par \uc2 * A federal judge in Illinois issued a temporary restraining order blocking the deployment of National Guard troops to Chicago, saying in court that there was no evidence of a rebellion brewing in Illinois and that the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cnarrative of events is simply unreliable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * In a similar case unfolding in federal court in San Francisco, challenging Trump\u8217\'20\'19s deployment of troops to Portland, Oregon, appellate judges heard arguments and seemed more likely to rule in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s favor, allowing the deployment of troops.\par \par \uc2 * Nearly half of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI}}}\uc2  agents working in the US\u8217\'20\'19s major field offices have been reassigned to aid immigration enforcement, according to newly released data, a stunning shift in law enforcement priorities that has raised public safety concerns.\par \par \uc2 * US troops have been sent to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  as part of the peace deal approved on Thursday to support and help monitor the ceasefire, according to multiple news reports.\par \par \uc2 * The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate}}}\uc2  remained deadlocked on legislation to end the government shutdown on Friday, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  reiterated his threat to make Democrats pay for the funding lapse that has closed federal agencies and furloughed workers nationwide.\par \par \uc2 * The chances of the US stock market crashing is far greater than many financiers believe, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/oct/09/head-of-jpmorgan-chase-warns-of-risk-of-american-stock-market-crash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the head of America\u8217\'20\'19s largest bank has said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A \uc2 Rutgers University\uc2  professor who taught a course on anti-fascism was blocked from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/09/anti-fascism-mark-bray-rutgers-university"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaving the US for Spain, according to media reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Meanwhile, the winner of the Nobel Peace Prize is slated to be announced today. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants to win the prize this year, but probably won\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251010elaa002p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
