\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US retail workers and shoppers: tell us about the impact of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian community team \par \uc2 147 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 October 2025\par 18:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than three in four store managers report more empty shelves since the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s global tariff rollout, new poll suggests\par \par \uc2 US store managers are reporting more empty shelf space since the global {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tariff}}}\uc2  rollout by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More than three-quarters of managers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.retailbrew.com/stories/2025/10/06/more-than-3-in-4-store-managers-report-more-empty-shelves-since-tariffs-hit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in one recent survey}}}\uc2  reported an increase in bare shelves. And over half (51%) of the store managers surveyed by warehouse software company \uc2 GreyOrange\uc2  also reported that they have reduced their workforce in the last six months, which may affect the shopper experience.\par \par \uc2 Whether you are a shopper or a retail worker, what, if anything, have you noticed in US stores in the wake of the tariffs? Are the shelves the same or emptier? What is missing? What else has changed?\par \par \uc2 Callout\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251010elaa005k2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
