\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  staff told they must share biometric data to access headquarters\b0\par\par\uc2 Mark Sweney \par \uc2 525 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 October 2025\par 12:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Investment bank had previously planned for such information from New York workers to be voluntary\par \par \uc2 JP Morgan Chase\uc2  has told staff moving into its new headquarters in New York that they must share their biometric data to access the multibillion-dollar building.\par \par \uc2 The investment bank had previously planned for the registering of biometric data by employees at its new Manhattan skyscraper to be voluntary.\par \par \uc2 However, employees of the US\u8217\'20\'19s biggest bank who have started work at the headquarters since August have received emails saying that biometric access was \u8220\'20\'1Crequired\u8221\'20\'1D, according to communications seen by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/d5351d3d-d64f-4a90-a3da-d1ef8e8bea66"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Financial Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/oct/09/head-of-jpmorgan-chase-warns-of-risk-of-american-stock-market-crash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Head of largest US bank warns of risk of American stock market crash}}}\par \par \uc2 Biometric access requires staff to scan their fingerprints or eye to gain access through security gates in the lobby instead of swiping their ID badges.\par \par \uc2 The bank\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters, which cost a reported $3bn (\u163\'00\'A32.25bn) to build, will eventually be a base for 10,000 employees once it is fully occupied later this year.\par \par \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  declined to comment but it is understood that the use of biometric data for access is designed to make the building more secure.\par \par \uc2 There are exemptions for some employees who will still be able to use a badge for access, the Guardian understands, although the criteria for who will use more traditional ID access is unclear.\par \par \uc2 Biometric enrolment is understood to remain voluntary at other \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  offices, including London, where voluntary hand biometrics have been introduced at its Bank Street office.\par \par \uc2 This process involves an employee\u8217\'20\'19s hand print being encrypted so the company does not have access to the data.\par \par \uc2 This system operates in a similar fashion to \uc2 Apple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Face ID option on iPhones, where the Silicon Valley company cannot access customers\u8217\'20\'19 facial data.\par \par \uc2 Alongside the introduction of palm and eye scanners, the company has also launched the \u8220\'20\'1CWork at \uc2 JPMC\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D mobile app, which works as a digital badge and hub for employee services.\par \par \uc2 The app allows staff to manage guest registration, navigate indoor maps of the building and pre-order meals from the building\u8217\'20\'19s 19 on-site dining vendors.\par \par \uc2 The implementation of stricter access protocols comes as US corporations, particularly those with significant operations in New York, look to increase security after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/04/unitedhealthcare-ceo-shooting-what-we-know-so-far"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shooting last year }}}\uc2 of the chief executive of one of the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest health insurers. \uc2 Brian Thompson\uc2 , the boss of \uc2 UnitedHealthcare\uc2 , was fatally shot not far from \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s offices.\par \par \uc2 The move comes amid debate over the use of technology to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/14/uk-firms-bossware-monitor-workers-activity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 track workers by their employers}}}\uc2 , including monitoring office attendance levels. Earlier this year all \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  workers on hybrid work schedules were told they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/jan/10/jp-morgan-chase-return-to-office"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 must return to the office five days a week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive, \uc2 Jamie Dimon\uc2 , has described \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new 60-storey headquarters as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbeautiful physical manifestation\u8221\'20\'1D of the company.\par \par \uc2 Dimon, one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful bankers, this week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/oct/09/head-of-jpmorgan-chase-warns-of-risk-of-american-stock-market-crash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that the chance of the US stock market crashing was far greater than many financiers believed.\par \par \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  has been contacted for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251010elaa001up\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\i